pair A=(0,0),B=(12,0),C=(0,9);draw(A--B--C--cycle);draw((.7,0)--(.7,.7)--(0,.7));label("$A$",A,SW);label("$B$",B,SE);label("$C$",C,N);label("$12$",(6,0),S);label("$9$",(0,4.5),W);label("$15$",(6,4.5),NE);
\end{asy}

Let the vertex angle be $\theta$. The cosine rule gives $16=2\cdot\dfrac{27}{4}-2\cdot\dfrac{27}{4}\cos\theta$. Consequently $\cos\theta=\dfrac{27-32}{27}=\boxed{-\dfrac{5}{27}}$. A negative cosine for an angle between $0$ and $180^\circ$ means it is obtuse.
\begin{asy}
