If the inradius is $r$, the altitude is $3r$ and the side is $2\sqrt3r$. Thus the perimeter is $6\sqrt3r$. Equating this with $\pi r^2$ and dividing by $r>0$ gives $\boxed{r=\dfrac{6\sqrt3}{\pi}}$.
\begin{asy}
