The sine of either angle between adjacent sides is $\sin45^\circ=\dfrac{\sqrt2}{2}$. If their lengths are $u,v$, the two heights are $u\sin45^\circ$ and $v\sin45^\circ$. Hence $(u+v)\dfrac{\sqrt2}{2}=2\sqrt2$, giving $u+v=4$. The perimeter is $\boxed8$.
\begin{asy}
