\end{asy}

Let $t=\dfrac{CD}{CB}=\dfrac{CE}{CA}=\dfrac{DE}{AB}$. The smaller perimeter is $42t$. The quadrilateral perimeter is $15+13(1-t)+14(1-t)+15t=42-12t$. Thus $54t=42$, or $t=\dfrac{7}{9}$. Therefore $\dfrac{BD}{DC}=\dfrac{1-t}{t}=\boxed{\dfrac{2}{7}}$.
