If the rectangle has height $h$, similarity shows its width is $10(1-\dfrac{h}{8})$. Thus its area is $10h-\dfrac{5}{4}h^2=20-\dfrac{5}{4}(h-4)^2\le20$. Equality occurs at height $4$, width $5$, so the maximum is $\boxed{20}$.
