In an equilateral triangle each median is an altitude and an angle bisector. The centre lies on all medians. Therefore $AP$ and $AM$ bisect the $60^\circ$ angle at $A$, and $CP$ bisects the angle at $C$, making all three angles in the first equality $30^\circ$. The median from $B$ passes through $N,P$ and is perpendicular to $AC$, so $\angle ANP=90^\circ$. Also $AM\perp BC$, giving $\angle AMB=90^\circ$.
\begin{asy}
