Let the rectangle area be $S$. Set $u=\dfrac{BE}{BC}$ and $v=\dfrac{DF}{DC}$. Then $Su=8$, $Sv=10$, and $S(1-u)(1-v)=6$. Substitution gives $S-18+\dfrac{80}{S}=6$, or $S^2-24S+80=0$. Thus $S=20$ or $4$. Since $S$ exceeds the sum $4+3+5=12$, it is $20$. Therefore $[AEF]=20-12=\boxed8$.
