The parallel sides are $24$ apart, so $648=\dfrac{1}{2}(AB+DC)24$, giving $AB+DC=54$. In a tangential quadrilateral the two sums of opposite sides are equal, by pairing equal tangent segments from each vertex. Thus $AD+BC=54$ and $AD=54-25=\boxed{29}$.

