The base angles are $40^\circ$, so in $ABD$ the angles at $B,D$ are $20^\circ,60^\circ$. The sine rule gives\[\dfrac{AD+DB}{AB}=\dfrac{\sin20^\circ+\sin100^\circ}{\sin60^\circ}=2\cos40^\circ=2\sin50^\circ.\]Here the middle identity uses $\sin u+\sin v=2\sin\dfrac{u+v}{2}\cos\dfrac{u-v}{2}$. Bisecting the isosceles triangle also gives $BC=2AB\sin50^\circ$. The desired equality follows.
