Similarity gives $CD=\dfrac{1}{2}CA$, so $D$ is the midpoint of the hypotenuse $AC$ of right triangle $APC$. Consequently $DP=DC=DA$. Also $\angle PCD=\angle ACB=20^\circ$, because $P$ lies on segment $BC$. The isosceles triangle $DPC$ has base angles $20^\circ$, so $\angle PDC=180^\circ-40^\circ=\boxed{140^\circ}$.
