Let $k$ be half the altitude from $A$ to line $BE$, so a triangle on a base of length $x$ has area $kx$. Then $kBC=10$, $kDE=24$, $k(BD)=8k$, and $k(CE)=12k$. Subtracting the last two corresponding base decompositions gives $12k-8k=24-10$, so $k=\dfrac{7}{2}$. Therefore $[ACD]=kBD-[ABC]=8\cdot\dfrac{7}{2}-10=\boxed{18}$.
