The vertical parallel sides have lengths $RP=\sin a$ and $SQ=\tan a$. Their horizontal separation is $1-\cos a$. Hence the area is\[\boxed{\dfrac{1}{2}(1-\cos a)(\sin a+\tan a)}.\]All lengths are positive because $0<a<\dfrac{\pi}{2}$.
