The altitude is $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}$, the inradius is one third of this, $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{6}$, and the triangle area is $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}$. The circle area is $\dfrac{\pi}{12}$. The median is an axis of symmetry through the circle centre, so each semicircle has area $\boxed{\dfrac{\pi}{24}}$, and each outside-circle half has area $\boxed{\dfrac{\sqrt3}{8}-\dfrac{\pi}{24}}$.
\begin{asy}
import geometry;
