The cone height is $\sqrt{2^2-1^2}=\sqrt3$. The cone axes form an equilateral triangle of side $2$; its center is distance $d=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt3}$ from each axis. In the vertical plane through one axis and the sphere center, a relevant cone generator has equation $\sqrt3\rho+z-\sqrt3=0$, with axis coordinate $\rho=0$. A sphere of radius $r$ tangent to the plane has center $(d,r)$. Its distance to the generator is $\dfrac{\sqrt3d+r-\sqrt3}{2}$; tangency sets this equal to $r$. Hence $\boxed{r=2-\sqrt3}$. The perpendicular foot has height $\dfrac{2-\sqrt3}{2}$, strictly between $0$ and $\sqrt3$, so the contact is on the finite lateral surface.
\begin{asy}
size(7cm);
pair A=(0,0),B=(2,0),C=(1,sqrt(3)),O=(1,sqrt(3)/3);draw(circle(A,1));draw(circle(B,1));draw(circle(C,1));draw(A--B--C--cycle,dashed);draw(A--O,dashed);dot(O);label("$O$",O,NE);label("$2$",(1,0),S);label("axis",A,SW);
\end{asy}

\begin{asy}
