At an integer point, $m=\dfrac{k}{x}$ with $k=y-2$ integral. If $x$ is odd, the least such slope above $\dfrac{1}{2}$ is $\dfrac{1}{2}+\dfrac{1}{2x}$, minimized at $x=99$. If $x$ is even, the least excess is $\dfrac{1}{x}\ge\dfrac{1}{100}>\dfrac{1}{198}$. Thus the first forbidden slope is $\dfrac{50}{99}$, attained at $(99,52)$. Since the interval for $m$ is open, the largest allowed endpoint is $\boxed{\dfrac{50}{99}}$.
