\end{asy}

$BD$ is a diameter, so $BD=12$. Right triangle $BCD$ is isosceles, giving legs $6\sqrt2$ and area $36$. Right triangle $BAD$ has angles $30^\circ,60^\circ,90^\circ$, so its legs are $6$ and $6\sqrt3$, giving area $18\sqrt3$. Convexity puts $A$ and $C$ on opposite sides of $BD$. The total is $\boxed{36+18\sqrt3}$.
