\end{asy}

In a nondegenerate polygon, each side is shorter than the sum of all the others, by repeated triangle inequality along the remaining boundary path. Here the largest side is 64 while the others sum to $1+2+4+8+16+32=63$. Since $64>63$, $\boxed{\text{no such polygon exists}}$.
