The semiperimeter is $s=\dfrac{13+14+15}{2}=21$. Heron's formula gives area $\sqrt{21(21-13)(21-14)(21-15)}=\sqrt{21\cdot 8\cdot 7\cdot 6}=\sqrt{7056}=\boxed{84}$.
