For a planar region of area A wholly on one side of its rotation axis, rotating about that axis gives volume $2\pi A h$, where h is the distance of its centroid from the axis. Indeed a thin vertical strip with lower and upper heights u,v gives washer volume $\pi(v^2-u^2)\,dx=2\pi\int_u^v y\,dy\,dx$, and integrating gives the formula. The regular polygon's centroid is its center. Its area is $A=\dfrac{3\sqrt 3}{2}$ and its apothem is $h=\dfrac{\sqrt 3}{2}$. Therefore $V=2\pi Ah=\boxed{\dfrac{9\pi}{2}}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
