\end{asy}

Place $C=(0,0)$, $D=(18,0)$, $B=(x,y)$, and $A=(x+7,y)$, with y positive. Then $M=(\dfrac{x+25}{2},\dfrac{y}{2})$. Since $BC=7$, $x^2+y^2=49$. Perpendicularity gives $B\cdot M=0$, so $49+25 x=0$. Consequently $CM^2=\dfrac{x^2+y^2+50 x+625}{4}=144$. Right triangle BCM now gives $BM^2=49+144=193$, and $\boxed{BM=\sqrt{193}}$.
