\end{asy}

An inscribed rectangle has opposite vertices at the ends of diameters, because each right angle subtends a diameter. Conversely, the endpoints of any two distinct diameters form a rectangle. The decagon has five pairs of opposite vertices, hence five such diameters. Choose two in $\boxed{\binom52=10}$ ways.
