\end{asy}

Reflect the start $A=(8,5)$ across $y=2$ to $A^{\prime}=(8,-1)$, and the end $B=(5,4)$ across $y=x$ to $B^{\prime}=(4,5)$. For any intermediate points $P,Q$ on the respective lines, the path length is $A^{\prime}P+PQ+QB^{\prime}\ge A^{\prime}B^{\prime}=\sqrt{(-4)^2+6^2}=2\sqrt{13}$. The segment $A^{\prime}B^{\prime}$ meets $y=2$ at $P=(6,2)$ and then $y=x$ at $Q=(\dfrac{22}{5},\dfrac{22}{5})$, in the required order. These points attain the lower bound, so the minimum is $\boxed{2\sqrt{13}}$.
