Each center lies $2r$ from its vertex along the angle bisector. On either side of the triangle, the adjacent center projects a distance $2r\cos30^\circ=\sqrt3r$ from the vertex. Thus the distance between two adjacent centers is $s-2\sqrt3r$. Tangency sets it equal to $2r$, so $s=2r(1+\sqrt3)$ and $\boxed{\dfrac{r}{s}=\dfrac{\sqrt3-1}{4}}$.
