The three small centers form an equilateral triangle of side $2r$. The large center is equidistant from them, so it is their circumcenter, at distance $\dfrac{2r}{\sqrt3}$ from each. Internal tangency gives $s=r+\dfrac{2r}{\sqrt3}$. Thus $\boxed{\dfrac{r}{s}=\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2+\sqrt3}=2\sqrt3-3}$.
