A triangle whose circumcenter lies on a side is right, with that side a diameter of its circumcircle. Thus $(x-5)^2+(\dfrac{3}{2}x+6)^2=(2x-1)^2$. Simplifying gives $x^2-16x-80=0$, or $(x-20)(x+4)=0$. Positivity of $x-5$ selects $x=20$, and the sides are $15,36,39$, consistent with the specified longest side. The sphere has radius $10$, so its volume is $\dfrac{4}{3}\pi(10)^3=\boxed{\dfrac{4000\pi}{3}}$.
