The length 5 piece must occupy one complete horizontal row. If it is the middle row, all other pieces must be horizontal in the two remaining rows. Their only partition into row totals 5 is $(1,4)$ and $(2,3)$. Choose which row gets each pair in 2 ways and order each pair in 2 ways, giving 8 tilings. If the length 5 piece is the top or bottom row, the other region is 2-by-5. Pieces 3 and 4 must be horizontal and in different rows. Choose the row containing 4 and the end containing its one-cell gap:4 choices. If piece 2 is horizontal, piece 1 fills that gap and piece 3 can occupy either end of the other row:2 completions. If piece 2 is vertical, it occupies that gap column; the other row then has four consecutive free cells, filled by pieces 3 and 1 in 2 orders:2 more completions. Thus each outer-row placement gives $4(2+2)=16$ tilings. Total $8+16+16=\boxed{40}$.
