Place the right-angle vertex at $A=(0,0)$ and the others at $B=(b,0)$ and $C=(0,a)$. Their midpoint is $M=(\dfrac{b}{2},\dfrac{a}{2})$, so $AM=\sqrt{\dfrac{a^2+b^2}{4}}=\dfrac{BC}{2}$ by Pythagoras.
