for(int i=0;i<=8;++i)draw((i,0)--(i,5),lightgray);for(int j=0;j<=5;++j)draw((0,j)--(8,j),lightgray);draw((0,0)--(8,5),blue,Arrow);dot("$(0,0)$",(0,0),SW);dot("$(8,5)$",(8,5),NE);label("unfolded squares",(4,-.5));
\end{asy}

The minute hand gains $6-\dfrac{1}{2}=\dfrac{11}{2}$ degrees per minute, or $3960=11\cdot360$ degrees in twelve hours. Each relative revolution contains two such positions, at relative angles $75^\circ$ and $285^\circ$. Neither endpoint qualifies, so there are $\boxed{22}$ times.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
