real am=90-900.0/11,ah=90-75.0/11;draw(circle((0,0),1));draw((0,0)--.9dir(am));draw((0,0)--.65dir(ah),blue);label("minute",.9dir(am),E);label("hour",.65dir(ah),N);label("$75^\circ$",.4dir((am+ah)/2));
\end{asy}

We have $\dfrac{AP}{AB}=\dfrac{1}{1+a}$. The shared angle gives area ratio $\dfrac{AP}{AB}\dfrac{AQ}{AC}$, so $\dfrac{AQ}{AC}=\dfrac{1+a}{2}$. Hence $\dfrac{QC}{QA}=\dfrac{1-a}{1+a}\le\dfrac{1}{4}$ precisely when $a\ge\dfrac{3}{5}$. This interval has length $\boxed{\dfrac{2}{5}}$.
\begin{asy}
