Use the rectangle $A=(0,0)$, $B=(6,0)$, $C=(6,4)$, $D=(0,4)$. Draw one cut from $E=(0,1)$ to $F=(6,2)$ and another from $G=(0,3)$ to $H=(6,\dfrac{7}{2})$. The three regions are $ABFE$, $EFHG$, and $GHCD$. In each, the two vertical sides are parallel. The other side pairs have slopes respectively $0$ and $\dfrac{1}{6}$, $\dfrac{1}{6}$ and $\dfrac{1}{12}$, and $\dfrac{1}{12}$ and $0$, so they are not parallel. Thus all three are trapezoids even under the exclusive definition.
