Parallelism gives $a=\sqrt3$. The distance between lines $\sqrt3x-y+b=0$ and $\sqrt3x-y-1=0$ is $\dfrac{|b+1|}{\sqrt{3+1}}=\dfrac{|b+1|}{2}$. Setting it equal to $3$ gives $b=5$ or $-7$. The smaller product is $\boxed{-7\sqrt3}$.
\begin{asy}
import geometry;
usepackage("amsmath");
