real m=sqrt(3); draw((-2,-2*m-1)--(2,2*m-1));draw((-2,-2*m+5)--(2,2*m+5));draw((-2,-2*m-7)--(2,2*m-7));label("$y=\sqrt3x-1$",(2,2*m-1),E);label("$b=5$",(2,2*m+5),E);label("$b=-7$",(2,2*m-7),E);
\end{asy}

If the side length is $s>0$, its area is $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}s^2$ and perimeter is $3s$. Thus $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}s^2=9s$, giving $\boxed{s=12\sqrt3}$.
\begin{asy}
