(a) At distance $z$ from the cone's apex, similarity gives cross-sectional radius $\dfrac{rz}{h}$. Thus $V=\int_0^h\pi\dfrac{r^2z^2}{h^2}\,dz=\boxed{\dfrac{1}{3}\pi r^2h}$. (b) Each cross-section parallel to the base is similar to the base with length scale $\dfrac{z}{h}$ and area $B\dfrac{z^2}{h^2}$. Therefore $V=\int_0^hB\dfrac{z^2}{h^2}\,dz=\boxed{\dfrac{1}{3}Bh}$. (c) A sphere slice at signed distance $z$ from the center is a disk of radius $\sqrt{r^2-z^2}$ by the Pythagorean theorem. Hence $V=\int_{-r}^r\pi(r^2-z^2)\,dz=\pi[r^2z-\dfrac{z^3}{3}]_{-r}^r=\boxed{\dfrac{4}{3}\pi r^3}$.
