Partition the square into four unit squares, assigning boundary points to one of their incident cells. Pigeonhole forces two points into a common cell, so their distance is at most its diagonal $\sqrt2$. Conversely, place points at the four corners and the center. Center-to-corner distances are $\sqrt2$ and corner-to-corner distances are at least $2$. Thus $\boxed{x_{\max}=\sqrt2}$.
