\end{asy}

Put $\angle ABC=\beta$. The base angles are $\dfrac{180-\beta}{2}$, so $\beta$ is an even integer with $2\le\beta\le178$. Triangle $BDC$ has angle at $B$ equal to $\dfrac{2\beta}{3}$, giving $\angle BDC=180-\dfrac{2\beta}{3}-\dfrac{180-\beta}{2}=90-\dfrac{\beta}{6}$. For this to be integral, $\beta$ must be divisible by $6$. Its greatest allowable value is $174$, giving smallest angle $\boxed{61^\circ}$. The corresponding base angles are $3^\circ$, so this is attainable.
\begin{asy}
