Use $A=(0,0),B=(9,0),C=(9,8),D=(0,8)$. Then $W=(6,0),X=(9,2),Y=(3,8),Z=(0,4)$. Parametrize $WY$ by $(6-3t,8t)$ and $XZ$ by $(9-9u,2+2u)$. The equations give $u=\dfrac{1+t}{3}$ and $t=\dfrac{4}{11}$, hence $O=(\dfrac{54}{11},\dfrac{32}{11})$. Triangle $OWB$ has base $3$ and height $\dfrac{32}{11}$, while $OBX$ has base $2$ and perpendicular height $9-\dfrac{54}{11}=\dfrac{45}{11}$. Their total area is $\dfrac{48}{11}+\dfrac{45}{11}=\boxed{\dfrac{93}{11}}$.
