If the arc between the endpoint vertices not containing the angle vertex spans $m$ edges, the angle is $\dfrac{180m}{n}$ degrees. Thus $\dfrac{180m}{n}=\dfrac{34}{5}$, or $450m=17n$. Since $17$ and $450$ are coprime, $450\mid n$. For $n=450$, take endpoint vertices $A_1,A_{18}$ and angle vertex $A_{250}$; the subtended arc has $17$ edges and gives the required angle. Hence $\boxed{450}$.
