\end{asy}

The midpoint of a right triangle's hypotenuse is equidistant from all three vertices, so $BC=26$. Let $u=AB,v=AC$. The area formulas give $uv=26\cdot5=130$, and Pythagoras gives $u^2+v^2=676$. Thus $(u+v)^2=936=36\cdot26$ and $(v-u)^2=416=16\cdot26$. Since $v>u$, we get $u+v=6\sqrt{26}$ and $v-u=4\sqrt{26}$, so $u=\sqrt{26},v=5\sqrt{26}$. Therefore $\boxed{\dfrac{AB}{AC}=\dfrac{1}{5}}$.
\begin{asy}
