For a regular $n$-gon, the direction of a chord joining vertices with angular indices $i,j$ is $\dfrac{(i+j)180^\circ}{n}+90^\circ$ modulo $180^\circ$. Consequently angles between chord lines are integer multiples of $\dfrac{180^\circ}{n}$. The condition $50=\dfrac{180m}{n}$ forces $n$ to be a multiple of $18$. For $n=18$, the diagonals from $A_1$ to $A_3$ and $A_8$ subtend the five-edge arc $A_3A_8$, giving inscribed angle $\dfrac{5\cdot180^\circ}{18}=50^\circ$. Therefore $\boxed{18}$.
