\end{asy}

The sample cube has volume $27$. Failure occurs when one value is at least the sum of the other two; the three events are disjoint apart from measure-zero boundaries. For $a\ge b+c$, put $b=1+u,c=1+v$. Then $u,v\ge0$, $u+v\le2$, and the allowable length for $a$ is $2-u-v$. The failure volume for this case is $\int_0^2\int_0^{2-u}(2-u-v)\,dv\,du=\dfrac{4}{3}$. Total failure probability is $\dfrac{3(\dfrac{4}{3})}{27}=\dfrac{4}{27}$, so the answer is $\boxed{\dfrac{23}{27}}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
