\end{asy}

Write $a-1=3r+s$ and $b-1=3u+v$ with $0\le r,s,u,v\le2$. Then the block begins at column $3s$, row $3r$, and the cell adds offsets $v,u$. Thus $\boxed{c=3((a-1)\bmod3)+(b-1)\bmod3}$ and $\boxed{d=3\lfloor\dfrac{a-1}{3}\rfloor+\lfloor\dfrac{b-1}{3}\rfloor}$.
