There are $\binom92=36$ possible point-pairs. Horizontal and vertical lines each account for $9$ pairs. Slopes $1,-1$ account for $5$ each. Slopes $2,-\dfrac{1}{2}$ account for $2$ each, as do slopes $\dfrac{1}{2},-2$. Thus the favorable ordered choices total $2(9\cdot9+5\cdot5+2\cdot2+2\cdot2)=228$. The probability is $\dfrac{228}{36^2}=\boxed{\dfrac{19}{108}}$.
