Fix $A$ at a reference location; list the $4!=\boxed{24}$ clockwise permutations of $B,C,D,E$. This describes each rotation class exactly once. If reflections are identified, each order pairs with its reverse. No distinct-letter arrangement is equal to its reflection up to rotation, so the count becomes $\dfrac{24}{2}=\boxed{12}$.
