The leg semicircles reach left to $x=-3$ and down to $y=-4$. The hypotenuse is $10$, so its semicircle has center $(4,3)$ and radius $5$, on the side $3x+4y\ge24$. Its rightmost point is $(9,3)$ and topmost point $(4,8)$; both lie in that half-plane. No disk extends beyond these four extremes. The enclosing rectangle therefore has width $9-(-3)=12$ and height $8-(-4)=12$, hence area $\boxed{144}$.
