A seating determines a domino tiling of the $2\times5$ grid, with each domino occupied by one pair. Let $T_n$ be the tiling count for $2\times n$. The leftmost column has either one vertical domino, leaving $T_{n-1}$ choices, or two horizontal dominoes, leaving $T_{n-2}$. Thus $T_n=T_{n-1}+T_{n-2}$ with $T_0=T_1=1$, giving $T_5=8$. Assign the five distinct pairs to the dominoes in $5!$ ways and order the partners in $2^5$ ways. The answer is $8\cdot5!\cdot2^5=\boxed{30720}$.
