import geometry;
usepackage("amsmath");
size(270);
for(int i=0;i<=5;++i)draw((i,0)--(i,2));for(int j=0;j<=2;++j)draw((0,j)--(5,j));draw((0,0)--(1,0)--(1,2)--(0,2)--cycle,blue+linewidth(1.5));label("one vertical pair",(.5,-.5));
\end{asy}

Delete cycle edges to obtain a spanning tree of length at most the original network length $L$. Traverse each tree edge twice in a closed walk, of total length at most $2L$. List the houses in order of their first appearances, and join them in that cyclic order. Shortcutting along the traversal cannot increase length, by the triangle inequality, so the resulting cycle has total length at most $2L$. Its alternate edges form two perfect pairings of the $100$ houses. Their lengths add to the cycle length; at least one pairing therefore has length at most $L$, as required.
\begin{asy}
import geometry;
usepackage("amsmath");
size(270);
pair[] P={(0,0),(2,0),(3,2),(1,3),(-1,2),(-1,1)};draw(P[0]--P[1]--P[2]--P[3]--P[4]--P[5]--cycle,gray);for(int i=0;i<6;++i){dot(P[i]);label(string(i+1),P[i],unit(P[i]-(1,1)));}draw(P[0]--P[1]^^P[2]--P[3]^^P[4]--P[5],blue+linewidth(1.2));label("alternate pairing: six-house illustration",(1,-1));
\end{asy}

A cell's black triangle points toward one of its four edges. If it points toward an interior edge, the neighbouring cell must point back, creating a matched pair of cells. Otherwise it points out of the grid. Thus a pattern is a matching of adjacent cells, with unmatched cells allowed only on the boundary; each unmatched corner has two outward choices and every other unmatched boundary cell one. Use the following exact recursion on the set $U$ of still-unassigned cells. Choose its first cell $v$. Either leave it unmatched in $b(v)$ outward directions, or pair it with any adjacent cell $w\in U$. Therefore $F(U)=b(v)F(U\setminus\{v\})+\sum_{w\sim v,\ w\in U}F(U\setminus\{v,w\})$, with $F(\varnothing)=1$. Evaluating gives $\boxed{10724}$. Here is a reproducible implementation:\begin{verbatim}
from functools import lru_cache
@lru_cache(None)
def f(U):
    if not U: return 1
    v=min(U); r,c=divmod(v,4)
    left=frozenset(U-{v})
    b=(r==0)+(r==3)+(c==0)+(c==3)
    total=b*f(left)
    for w in U-{v}:
        s,t=divmod(w,4)
        if abs(r-s)+abs(c-t)==1:
            total+=f(frozenset(left-{w}))
    return total
