Let the side length be $s$, and put $A=(0,0)$ with $AC$ on the positive horizontal axis. Write $c=\cos36^\circ=\dfrac{1+\sqrt5}{4}$ and $t=\sin36^\circ$. Then
\[B=(sc,st),\quad E=(s(2c^2-1),-2sct),\quad M=(\dfrac{s(2c^2-1)}{2},-sct).\]
The segment from $B$ to $M$ reaches height zero at parameter $\dfrac{1}{1+c}$. Its horizontal coordinate is therefore $\dfrac{s(2c^2-\dfrac{1}{2})}{1+c}=\dfrac{sc}{1+c}$, since $2c^2-\dfrac{1}{2}=c$. Thus $s=\dfrac{2(1+c)}{c}$. Finally,
\[BZ^2=(sc-2)^2+s^2t^2=s^2-4sc+4=14-2\sqrt5.\]
Hence $\boxed{BZ=\sqrt{14-2\sqrt5}}$, choice D.
