Use $D=(0,0),C=(27,0),A=(6,8),B=(21,8)$, since the height is $\sqrt{10^2-6^2}=8$. The median is $y=4$, $3\le x\le24$. The circle with diameter $AD$ has centre $(3,4)$ and radius $5$, meeting that line at $x=-2,8$. Only $x=8$ lies on the median, so $X_1=(8,4)$. Reflection gives $X_2=(19,4)$.
Projection onto $AD$ gives
\[H_1=\dfrac{(8,4)\cdot(6,8)}{6^2+8^2}(6,8)=\dfrac{4}{5}(6,8)=(\dfrac{24}{5},\dfrac{32}{5}).\]
Reflecting across $x=\dfrac{27}{2}$ gives $H_2=(\dfrac{111}{5},\dfrac{32}{5})$. Thus $H_1H_2=\dfrac{87}{5}$ and $\boxed{m+n=92}$, choice E.
