Let the radii be $a,b,c$. The centre-triangle sides are $a+b,b+c,c+a$, so its semiperimeter is $a+b+c=20$. Heron's formula gives $K^2=20abc$, hence $abc=100$.
The tangency triangle is obtained by removing three corner triangles from the centre triangle. Its area ratio is
\[1-\left(\dfrac{a^2}{(a+b)(a+c)}+\dfrac{b^2}{(b+a)(b+c)}+\dfrac{c^2}{(c+a)(c+b)}\right)=\dfrac{2abc}{(a+b)(a+c)(b+c)}.\]
The given ratio is $\dfrac{2}{21}$, so the product of the three sides is $2100$. Since this product is $(a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca)-abc$, we get $ab+bc+ca=110$. Thus the radii are the roots of
\[t^3-20t^2+110t-100=(t-10)(t^2-10t+10),\]
namely $10,5+\sqrt{15},5-\sqrt{15}$. The longest side is $15+\sqrt{15}=\sqrt{225}+\sqrt{15}$, so $\boxed{m+n=240}$, choice C.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath"); size(230);
real a=10,b=5+sqrt(15),c=5-sqrt(15),d=a+b,e=a+c;pair O1=(0,0),O2=(d,0);real x=(d*d+e*e-(b+c)^2)/(2*d);pair O3=(x,sqrt(e*e-x*x));pair P=(b*O1+a*O2)/(a+b),Q=(c*O2+b*O3)/(b+c),T=(a*O3+c*O1)/(a+c);draw(circle(O1,a),gray);draw(circle(O2,b),gray);draw(circle(O3,c),gray);draw(O1--O2--O3--cycle,blue);draw(P--Q--T--cycle,red+linewidth(1));dot(O1);dot(O2);dot(O3);label("$O_1$",O1,SW);label("$O_2$",O2,SE);label("$O_3$",O3,N);label("$P$",P,S);label("$Q$",Q,NE);label("$T$",T,NW);
\end{asy}

All $\binom{10}{5}=252$ paths with five moves of each kind are conditionally equally likely. At integer time $k$, if $j$ moves have been rightward, the coordinates are $(j,k-j)$ and the distance is $\dfrac{|2j-k|}{\sqrt2}$. The number of conditioned paths with that prefix count is $\binom kj\binom{10-k}{5-j}$.
On each unit step the signed difference changes by one; its absolute value is linear along the step, since a sign change can occur only at an endpoint. Thus the integral of distance on that step is the average of its endpoint distances. Both overall endpoints lie on the diagonal, so the expected time average is
\[\dfrac{1}{10\sqrt2\binom{10}{5}}\sum_{k=1}^9\sum_j |2j-k|\binom kj\binom{10-k}{5-j}.\]
The sum is $2560$, verified by:
\begin{verbatim}
from math import comb
total=0
for k in range(1,10):
    for j in range(max(0,k-5),min(k,5)+1):
        total += abs(2*j-k)*comb(k,j)*comb(10-k,5-j)
print(total) # 2560
\end{verbatim}
Therefore the expected average is $\dfrac{2560}{2520\sqrt2}=\dfrac{32\sqrt2}{63}$, so $\boxed{a+b+c=97}$, choice A.
