For one triangle area $T$, $1-4T=\dfrac{4}{3}T$, so $T=\dfrac{3}{16}$ and $ab=\dfrac{3}{8}$. Since $a^2+b^2=1$, we have $a+b=\dfrac{\sqrt7}{2}$ and $a-b=\dfrac{1}{2}$. Adding gives $\boxed{a=\dfrac{\sqrt7+1}{4}}$.
\begin{asy}
