Write $\gamma=\angle ACB$. Reflection in the midpoint gives $\overrightarrow{CD^\prime}=\overrightarrow{DB}$, so $CE\parallel BD$. Since $BE\perp AC$, $\angle EBC=90^\circ-\gamma$. The altitude from $A$ is perpendicular to $BC$, so $\angle DAC=90^\circ-\gamma$; equal angles subtending chord $DC$ give $\angle DBC=90^\circ-\gamma$. The parallelism now gives $\angle ECB=90^\circ-\gamma$. Thus $\angle BEC=2\gamma$. Both $A,E$ are on the same side of chord $BC$ in the acute configuration, so they subtend the same angle: $\angle BAC=\angle BEC=\boxed{2\gamma}$.
