Put the side corresponding to this altitude along the horizontal axis, with vector $(a,0)$, $a>0$, and the adjacent side $(u,18)$. Choose the direction so that the longer diagonal has horizontal magnitude $80$, because $\sqrt{82^2-18^2}=80$; the shorter has magnitude $\sqrt{30^2-18^2}=24$. Thus $|a+u|=80$, $|a-u|=24$, up to exchanging diagonal labels. It follows that $a$ is either $\dfrac{80+24}{2}=52$ or $\dfrac{80-24}{2}=28$. Both occur, for example with $(a,u)=(52,28)$ and $(28,52)$. Therefore the least area is $\boxed{28(18)=504\text{ cm}^2}$.
