For each positive leading pair $a,b$, the digit $c=12-a-b$ is forced. The following short exhaustive check tests all possible digit assignments:
\begin{verbatim}
best=None
for a in range(1,10):
    for b in range(1,10):
        c=12-a-b
        if 0<=c<=9 and len({a,b,c})==3:
            value=(10*a+b)*(10*b+c)
            if best is None or value<best[0]:
                best=(value,a,b,c)
print(best) # (348,1,2,9)
\end{verbatim}
Thus $12\cdot29=\boxed{348}$ is attained and no valid assignment is smaller.

