The area of the triangle with vertices $(x_i,y_i)$ is half the absolute determinant
\[(x_2-x_1)(y_3-y_1)-(x_3-x_1)(y_2-y_1).\]
Thus its area is one exactly when this integer determinant has absolute value two. Enumerate each unordered triple once:
\begin{verbatim}
from itertools import combinations
P=[(x,y) for x in range(5) for y in range(5)]
answer=0
for (x1,y1),(x2,y2),(x3,y3) in combinations(P,3):
    det=(x2-x1)*(y3-y1)-(x3-x1)*(y2-y1)
    answer += (abs(det)==2)
print(answer) # 424
\end{verbatim}
The determinant test includes slanted triangles as well as horizontal-base ones, giving $\boxed{424}$.
