For each three-element digit set, form all its permutations with nonzero leading digit. For each triple, first check the position restriction, then sort the three numbers as $u<v<w$ and test $v^2=uw$. This exactly characterizes a positive geometric progression:
\begin{verbatim}
from itertools import combinations,permutations
answers=[]
for digits in combinations(range(10),3):
    words=[p for p in permutations(digits) if p[0]!=0]
    for a,b,c in combinations(words,3):
        if any(len({a[j],b[j],c[j]})<3 for j in range(3)):
            continue
        u,v,w=sorted(100*p[0]+10*p[1]+p[2] for p in (a,b,c))
        if v*v==u*w:
            answers.append((u+v+w,(u,v,w)))
print(sorted(answers))
# [(999,(243,324,432)),(1998,(486,648,864))]
\end{verbatim}
This exhaustive finite test establishes the minimum $\boxed{999}$, attained by ratio $\dfrac{4}{3}$ in $243,324,432$.

The orbit counts under the eight symmetries of a square are $2,1,4,8,8,4,4$ for $I,O,T,L,J,S,Z$ respectively. The straight piece has two orientations and the square one; the T has four; L and J each have four rotations of each handedness, giving eight; S and Z each have two rotations of each handedness, giving four. Averaging over the seven equally likely initial types gives
\[\boxed{\dfrac{2+1+4+8+8+4+4}{7}=\dfrac{31}{7}}.\]
