Apply Burnside's lemma to the $24$ rotations. A colouring fixed by a rotation must be constant on each face cycle.
\[\begin{array}{c|r|r}
\text{rotation type}&\text{number}&\text{face cycles}\\
\text{identity}&1&8\\
90^\circ\text{ or }270^\circ\text{ about opposite vertices}&6&2\\
180^\circ\text{ about opposite vertices}&3&4\\
120^\circ\text{ or }240^\circ\text{ about opposite face centres}&8&4\\
180^\circ\text{ about opposite edge midpoints}&6&4
\end{array}\]
The quarter-turns have two four-cycles; vertex and edge half-turns have four two-cycles; the third-turns have two fixed faces and two three-cycles. These rotations exhaust the orientation-preserving symmetry group. The orbit count is
\[\boxed{\dfrac{3^8+6\cdot3^2+(3+8+6)3^4}{24}=333}.\]
