The outer hexagon has apothem $6\cos30^\circ=3\sqrt3$, the circle radius. The inner hexagon side equals its circumradius, so its area is $6\cdot\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}(3\sqrt3)^2=\boxed{\dfrac{81\sqrt3}{2}}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(7cm);
path p;for(int i=0;i<6;++i)p=p--6dir(60*i);draw(p--cycle);draw(circle((0,0),3sqrt(3)),gray);path q;for(int i=0;i<6;++i)q=q--3sqrt(3)*dir(30+60*i);draw(q--cycle,blue);label("$6$",(4.5,2.6),NE);label("$3\sqrt3$",(0,0),N);draw((0,0)--3sqrt(3)*dir(30),dashed);
