Burnside averages the fixed colourings over eight square symmetries. Identity fixes $3^4=81$. The quarter-turns each fix $3$, and the half-turn fixes $3^2=9$. Each of the two diagonal reflections fixes $3^3=27$, and each of the two opposite-edge-midpoint reflections fixes $3^2=9$. Thus the number is $\dfrac{81+2(3)+9+2(27)+2(9)}{8}=\boxed{21}$.
