draw((-1,-1)--(1,-1)--(1,1)--(-1,1)--cycle);pair[] V={(-1,-1),(1,-1),(1,1),(-1,1)};for(pair p:V)dot(p);draw((-1.3,-1.3)--(1.3,1.3),dashed);draw((0,-1.3)--(0,1.3),blue+dashed);label("two reflection types",(0,-1.7));
\end{asy}

Triangle $ABE$ is isosceles right with hypotenuse $AB=10$ and legs $5\sqrt2$. Thus $R=5$ and $r=\dfrac{10\sqrt2-10}{2}=5\sqrt2-5$. Therefore $\boxed{R-r=10-5\sqrt2}$.
