The empty set is uniform among $\binom{12}{4}=495$ four-seat subsets. In one row, subsets with no adjacent seats have generating polynomial $1+3x+x^2$: the only two-seat choice is both ends. The coefficient of $x^4$ in $(1+3x+x^2)^4$ is $3^4+4\binom32 3^2+\binom42=81+108+6=195$. Thus the probability of at least one adjacent empty pair is $1-\dfrac{195}{495}=\boxed{\dfrac{20}{33}}$.
