Since $g(n)\le2024$, we have $n\le20249$. Thus exact enumeration over $10\le n\le20249$ is complete. For $L$ digits, $f(n)=n\bmod10^{L-1}$ and $g(n)=\lfloor\dfrac{n}{10}\rfloor$. The code finds only $10931$ and $20022$: their pairs of values are $(931,1093)$ and $(22,2002)$, both summing to $2024$. The requested sum is $\boxed{30953}$.
