answer=[n for n in range(10,20250)
        if n%10**(len(str(n))-1)+n//10==2024]
print(answer)
\end{verbatim}

For each integer from $100$ through $999$, compute the digit sum and test divisibility. The sum is always positive, so the test is valid. This checks every possible integer exactly once and gives $\boxed{180}$.
