Through vertex $A$, draw a line parallel to $BC$. The angle between $AB$ and its leftward ray equals $\angle B$ by alternate interior angles. The angle between $AC$ and its rightward ray equals $\angle C$. Together with $\angle A$, these three adjacent angles form a straight angle. Therefore $\boxed{\angle A+\angle B+\angle C=180^\circ}$.
