For counts $a,b,c\ge0$ with $1\le a+b+c\le6$, the mean is $\dfrac{9a+10b+21c}{a+b+c}$. Exact enumeration of these finitely many triples gives possible integer means $9,10,11,12,13,14,15,17,18,19,21$. Thus $\boxed{21-11=10}$ integers are impossible. The following checks every allowable class composition.\begin{verbatim}
means=set()
for a in range(7):
 for b in range(7):
  for c in range(7):
   n=a+b+c
   if 1<=n<=6 and (9*a+10*b+21*c)%n==0:
    means.add((9*a+10*b+21*c)//n)
print(sorted(means))
\end{verbatim}

