For a general positive side $n$, take $A=(0,0),B=(n,0),C=(n,n),D=(0,n),E=(2n,0),F=(2n,n)$. The lines are $DM:y=n-2x$ and $FB:y=x-n$, so $P=(\dfrac{2n}{3},-\dfrac{n}{3})$. The lengths are $AP=\dfrac{n\sqrt5}{3}$, $PE=\dfrac{n\sqrt{17}}{3}$, $EF=n$, $FD=2n$, $DA=n$. Thus the perimeter is $n(4+\dfrac{\sqrt5+\sqrt{17}}{3})$. With $n=47$, it is $\boxed{188+\dfrac{47(\sqrt5+\sqrt{17})}{3}}$.
