usepackage("amsmath");
size(7cm);
real R=16/sqrt(3),r=R-8;pair O=(0,0);for(int k=0;k<3;++k)draw(circle(R*dir(90+120*k),8),gray);pair A=2r*dir(30),B=2r*dir(150),C=2r*dir(270);filldraw(A--B--C--cycle,lightblue,blue);dot(O);label("$O$",O,E);label("$r$",(0,r/2),W);draw(O--(0,r),dashed);
\end{asy}

The probability-generating polynomial is $\prod_{n=1}^{15}(\dfrac{n-1}{n}+\dfrac{t}{n})=\dfrac{t(t+1)\cdots(t+14)}{15!}$. The sum of its coefficients of degrees $11$ through $15$ is the desired probability. The exact recurrence below computes these coefficients and gives $\boxed{\dfrac{966061}{435891456000}}$. At stage $n$, coefficient $k$ is the probability of exactly $k$ solved questions, proving the update.\begin{verbatim}
from fractions import Fraction as F
p=[F(1)]
for n in range(1,16):
    q=[F(0)]*(len(p)+1)
    for k,v in enumerate(p):
        q[k]+=v*F(n-1,n)
        q[k+1]+=v*F(1,n)
    p=q
print(sum(p[11:]))
\end{verbatim}

The spacings are $\dfrac{20}{35}$ and $\dfrac{20}{50}$. Rungs $i,j$ coincide when $\dfrac{i}{35}=\dfrac{j}{50}$, or $10i=7j$. The least positive solution is $i=7,j=10$, at height $\boxed4$ feet. Equal height minimizes their vertical separation to zero.
