for(int k=0;k<15;++k)draw(2dir(24*k)--2dir(24*(k+1)));for(int k=0;k<45;++k)draw((6,0)+2dir(8*k)--(6,0)+2dir(8*(k+1)));label("$Q:15$ sides",(0,-2.5));label("$P:45$ sides",(6,-2.5));
\end{asy}

Place $A=(0,0),B=(51,0)$. The distance equations give $C=(68,68\sqrt3)$, since $68^2+(68\sqrt3)^2=136^2$ and $17^2+(68\sqrt3)^2=119^2$. Thus $C^{\prime}=(68,-68\sqrt3)$ and line $AC^{\prime}$ makes angle $-60^\circ$ with the positive horizontal axis. Reflecting $B$ across it yields $B^{\prime}=51(\cos(-120^\circ),\sin(-120^\circ))=(-\dfrac{51}{2},-\dfrac{51\sqrt3}{2})$. The vertical base $CC^{\prime}$ has length $136\sqrt3$ and the perpendicular height from $B^{\prime}$ is $68+\dfrac{51}{2}=\dfrac{187}{2}$. The area is $\dfrac{1}{2}(136\sqrt3)\dfrac{187}{2}=6358\sqrt3$, giving $\boxed{a+b=6361}$.
