For sides $a,b$, the equation $ab=2a+2b$ is $(a-2)(b-2)=4$. Both sides must exceed $2$: if $a\le2$, then $ab\le2b<2a+2b$. The unordered positive factor pairs of $4$ are $(1,4),(2,2)$, giving sides $(3,6),(4,4)$. Their areas sum to $18+16=\boxed{34}$.
