The first three multipliers are $i$, giving $h_4=-i$. Every block from $h_{4k}$ to $h_{4k+4}$ uses $(k+1)i$ four times, multiplying by $(k+1)^4$. Induction gives $h_{4k}=-i(k!)^4$. Hence $h_{100}=-i(25!)^4$ and $h_{101}=26(25!)^4$. Their real and imaginary differences are perpendicular, so the squared distance is $(26^2+1)(25!)^8=\boxed{(26!)^2(25!)^6+(25!)^8}$.
