Use $P_k=(\cos(\dfrac{2\pi k}{n}),\sin(\dfrac{2\pi k}{n}))$ for $k=0,\ldots,n-1$ and join consecutively, including the last to the first. Adjacent central angles all equal $\dfrac{2\pi}{n}$, so every side is a chord of length $2\sin(\dfrac{\pi}{n})$. After $n$ steps the angle has increased by $2\pi$, closing the polygon.\begin{verbatim}
from math import cos,sin,pi
def regular_polygon(n):
    assert isinstance(n,int) and n>=3
    return [(cos(2*pi*k/n),sin(2*pi*k/n)) for k in range(n)]
\end{verbatim}
