The vectors are unit vectors 120 degrees apart. Each rhombus has area $|\det(u,v)|=\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}$, and the three lie in separate 120-degree sectors, overlapping only on edges. Thus the union has area $\boxed{\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{2}}$. The labelled construction below gives a cube-style projection; it is a plane figure made of three equal rhombi.
