Use $A=(0,0),B=(2,0),C=(\dfrac{3}{2},\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{2})$ and $P=(u,v)$. The two distances give $u^2+v^2-4u+3=0$ and $u-3\sqrt3v+3=0$. Substitution yields $P=(\dfrac{3}{2},\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2})$ or $(\dfrac{15}{7},\dfrac{4\sqrt3}{7})$. The latter is outside the triangle, since its first coordinate exceeds both $B$ and $C$. For the interior point the determinant area is $x=\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{4}$, hence $\boxed{16x^2=27}$.
