Exact integer comparison gives $2^{116}<5^{50}<2^{117}$ and $2\cdot5^{50}<3\cdot2^{116}$. The last inequality says the target lies below the midpoint of those consecutive powers, so $2^{116}$ is closer. Every other power lies farther away by monotonicity. Therefore $\boxed{n=116}$. The comparisons can be checked directly by repeated squaring, or by the following exact assertions.\begin{verbatim}
assert 2**116 < 5**50 < 2**117
assert 2*5**50 < 3*2**116
\end{verbatim}

The inscribed-angle theorem gives minor arc $PA=12^\circ$. Each pentagon arc is $72^\circ$, so the arc from $P$ through $E$ to $D$ is $(72-12)+72=132^\circ$. This arc does not contain $B$, and therefore $\angle PBD=\dfrac{132^\circ}{2}=\boxed{66^\circ}$. This configuration also satisfies the original additional condition $\angle PDC=78^\circ$.
