Use $A=(0,0),M=(5,0),C=(10,0)$ and $B=(u,v)$ above $AC$. The area condition gives $10v=70$, while $u^2+v^2=50$ and acuteness give $B=(1,7)$. Thus $D=(9,-7)$. The circle equation is $x^2+y^2-5x-\dfrac{45}{7}y=0$. Substituting $B+t(C-B)=(1+9t,7-7t)$ gives $t(130t-80)=0$. Hence $E=(\dfrac{85}{13},\dfrac{35}{13})$, and $DE^2=\dfrac{32^2+126^2}{13^2}=100$. Therefore $\boxed{DE=10}$.
