Lay off four unit lengths to construct an equilateral triangle of side four. Its altitude, constructible as a perpendicular bisector, has length $\sqrt{4^2-2^2}=2\sqrt3$. Lay off nine units on another ray and erect a perpendicular of length $2\sqrt3$ at one endpoint. The hypotenuse of this right triangle has length $\sqrt{9^2+(2\sqrt3)^2}=\boxed{\sqrt{93}}$. Every step uses equal-length transfer, straight lines and perpendicular construction.
