If the apex is $V$ and consecutive base vertices are $A_i$, each centroid is $\dfrac{V+A_i+A_{i+1}}{3}$. The square of base-edge midpoints has area $\dfrac{9^2}{2}$. The centroid square is its image under a dilation of factor $\dfrac{2}{3}$ toward $V$, so its area is $\dfrac{4}{9}\cdot\dfrac{81}{2}=\boxed{18}$.
