Let the equal leg length be $L$. The sine of its angle with either base is $\dfrac{5}{L}$, so the base lengths are $AD=\dfrac{3L}{5}$ and $BC=\dfrac{9L}{5}$. Their half-difference is $\dfrac{3L}{5}$, the horizontal projection of a leg. Hence $L^2=25+\dfrac{9L^2}{25}$, giving $L=\dfrac{25}{4}$. The bases are $\dfrac{15}{4},\dfrac{45}{4}$, so area is $\dfrac{1}{2}(15)(5)=\boxed{\dfrac{75}{2}}$.
