The minor arc $AB$ is $40^\circ$, so each of the equal arcs $AC,BC$ is $160^\circ$. Point $D$ bisects the minor arc $BC$ because $OM$ is its perpendicular bisector. Thus the minor arc $AD$ has measure $40^\circ+80^\circ=120^\circ$. In isosceles triangle $AOD$, $\angle ADO=30^\circ$. The diameter theorem gives $\angle OXD=90^\circ$, and $OD=2$, so this right triangle has legs $1,\sqrt3$. Its area is $\boxed{\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}}$.
