Place $A=(0,0),B=(3,0),E=(0,4),D=(0,h),C=(3,h)$ with $h>4$. The unit direction vectors from $E$ along $EB$ and $ED$ are $(\dfrac{3}{5},-\dfrac{4}{5})$ and $(0,1)$. Their sum points along the internal angle bisector $EC$, with slope $\dfrac{\dfrac{1}{5}}{\dfrac{3}{5}}=\dfrac{1}{3}$. Thus $h-4=1$, and $CE^2=3^2+1^2=\boxed{10}$.
