Sides are proportional to the reciprocals of their altitudes. The triangle inequalities become $\left|\dfrac{1}{20}-\dfrac{1}{22}\right|<\dfrac{1}{x}<\dfrac{1}{20}+\dfrac{1}{22}$, or $\dfrac{1}{220}<\dfrac{1}{x}<\dfrac{21}{220}$. Thus $\dfrac{220}{21}<x<220$, so the integer possibilities are $11$ through $219$, totaling $\boxed{209}$. Conversely each such reciprocal triple forms a triangle; scaling makes its altitudes exactly the requested values.
