\end{asy}

The remaining solid is a regular octahedron. Its eight faces are equilateral triangles of side two: four are the central portions of the original faces and four are the new cuts. Each has area $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}\cdot2^2=\sqrt3$, so the total is $\boxed{8\sqrt3}$.
