Every color occupies at least two cells; since there are eight cells and four colors, each occupies exactly two adjacent cells. Thus each color forms one domino. A $2\times n$ rectangle has domino-tiling counts satisfying $T_n=T_{n-1}+T_{n-2}$, by whether its first column uses a vertical domino or begins two horizontal ones. With $T_0=T_1=1$, $T_4=5$. Assign four colors to the four dominoes in $4!$ ways, giving $5\cdot24=\boxed{120}$.
