\end{asy}

The legs satisfy $a+b=21$ and $a^2+b^2=400$. Hence $2ab=21^2-400=41$, so area $\dfrac{ab}{2}=\boxed{\dfrac{41}{4}}$. The positive legs exist, since they are the two positive roots of $t^2-21t+\dfrac{41}{2}=0$.
