Use $A=(0,0),B=(10,0),D=(d,h),C=(d+35,h)$ with $h>0$. Intersecting the leg lines gives $P=(-\dfrac{2d}{5},-\dfrac{2h}{5})$. The diagonals meet with $AQ:QC=AB:CD=2:7$, so $Q=(\dfrac{2(d+35)}{9},\dfrac{2h}{9})$. The point of $PQ$ at height zero is $R=\dfrac{5}{14}P+\dfrac{9}{14}Q=(5,0)$. Hence $\boxed{AR=5}$. The given leg lengths are consistent with $d=-9,h=12$.
