The diagonal joining the other two vertices is the common hypotenuse of two right triangles. The side pairing must therefore give equal sums of squares. Of the three pairings, only $7^2+24^2=15^2+20^2=625$ works. The area is $\dfrac{1}{2}(7\cdot24+15\cdot20)=\boxed{234}$.
