Put $C=\theta$. The sine rule gives $\dfrac{5}{4}=\dfrac{\sin3\theta}{\sin\theta}=3-4\sin^2\theta$. Thus $\sin\theta=\dfrac{\sqrt7}{4}$. Since $4\theta<180^\circ$, we have $\theta<45^\circ$ and $\cos\theta=\dfrac{3}{4}$. Also $A=180^\circ-4\theta$, so $\sin A=4\sin\theta\cos\theta\cos2\theta=4\cdot\dfrac{\sqrt7}{4}\cdot\dfrac{3}{4}\cdot\dfrac{1}{8}=\dfrac{3\sqrt7}{32}$. Hence $BC=4\dfrac{\sin A}{\sin\theta}=\boxed{\dfrac{3}{2}}$.
