The diagonal crosses $M-1$ internal vertical and $N-1$ internal horizontal grid lines. Ordinarily each crossing enters a new square. At an internal lattice vertex the two crossings happen together and enter only one new square, so subtract one for each such vertex. There are $\gcd(M,N)-1$ internal lattice vertices, because the step between consecutive lattice points on the diagonal is $(\dfrac{M}{g},\dfrac{N}{g})$ for $g=\gcd(M,N)$. Thus the answer is $1+(M-1)+(N-1)-(g-1)=\boxed{M+N-\gcd(M,N)}$.
