\end{asy}

At 45 degrees the axial-height difference across a diameter is that diameter, so $2r=10-6=4$ and $r=2$. The mean height over the circular base is the centre height $\dfrac{6+10}{2}=8$, since the height varies linearly and opposite points average to 8. Volume is $\pi r^2\cdot8=\boxed{32\pi}$.
