Represent the points by $(i,j)$ with $i,j\ge0,i+j\le62$ in two 60-degree lattice directions. Comparing two adjacent unit triangles shows that their opposite vertices have the same color. Propagating these equalities yields the three classes $i-j\pmod3$, with a constant color on each class. Every unit triangle uses one of each class, so exactly one class must be black. Each class has 672 points; for instance this follows by counting the residues in the rows, or the finite check below. All three choices are valid, so the sole possible count is $\boxed{672}$.\begin{verbatim}
from collections import Counter
assert Counter((i-j)%3 for i in range(63) for j in range(63-i))=={0:672,1:672,2:672}
\end{verbatim}
