Each jump increases the coordinate sum by $3$, so reaching $(10,8)$ requires exactly six jumps. If $k$ jumps are of type $(2,1)$, the position is $(6+k,12-k)$, so $k=4$. The probability is $\dfrac{\binom64}{2^6}=\boxed{\dfrac{15}{64}}$.
