In the mid-height plane the three corner centres form an equilateral triangle of side $L-2\sqrt3$, where $L$ is the container side: shifting each side inward by 1 reduces the triangle side by $2\sqrt3$. The distance of a corner centre from the middle centre is $\dfrac{L-2\sqrt3}{\sqrt3}$. Nonoverlap with the middle ball requires this at least 2, so $L\ge4\sqrt3$. At equality the three corner-centre separations are $2\sqrt3>2$, so all balls fit. The minimum volume is $2\cdot(\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4})L^2=\boxed{24\sqrt3}$.
