Use $D=(0,0),B=(-2,0),C=(4,0),A=(0,h)$ with $h>0$. The 45-degree angle gives $\dfrac{6h}{h^2-8}=1$, so $h^2-6h-8=0$ and $h=3+\sqrt{17}$. The line through $B$ perpendicular to $AC$ has slope $\dfrac{4}{h}$, hence $E=(0,\dfrac{8}{h})$. Because $h^2-8=6h$, $AE=h-\dfrac{8}{h}=\boxed6$.
