\end{asy}

Write the slow position as $h$ turns modulo 1 and the fast position as $kh$ with $k=2018$. A swapped valid pair requires $k^2h\equiv h\pmod1$, giving $k^2-1$ possible values of $h$ in $[0,1)$. Of these, $k-1$ have coincident positions, since $(k-1)h\in\mathbb Z$. Excluding them gives $(k^2-1)-(k-1)=k(k-1)=\boxed{4070306}$. Every valid pair recurs after whole common periods, so the swapped occurrence can be chosen later.
