Normalize $JA=1$ and put $J=(0,0),A=(1,0)$. The ratio condition gives $JX=\dfrac{3-\sqrt5}{2}$ and $AX=\dfrac{\sqrt5-1}{2}$. Coordinates $M=(1+\cos72^\circ,\sin72^\circ)$ and $E=(\dfrac{1}{2},\sin72^\circ+\sin36^\circ)$ give $AE^2=\dfrac{3+\sqrt5}{2}$ and $XM^2=4-\sqrt5$. Write $P=A+t(E-A)$, $0\le t\le1$. The equation $XP^2=XM^2$ becomes $(3+\sqrt5)t^2-(\sqrt5-1)t-(5-\sqrt5)=0$. Its sole root in $[0,1]$ is $t=\dfrac{3\sqrt5-5}{2}$; the other is negative. Therefore $\dfrac{AE}{PE}=\dfrac{1}{1-t}=\boxed{\dfrac{7+3\sqrt5}{2}}$.
