Set $E=(0,0),A=(a,0),B=(0,b),C=(-c,0),D=(0,-d)$, with positive coordinates. Cyclicity gives $ac=bd=k$. The right-triangle altitude formula gives $EW=\dfrac{ab}{\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}$ and $EY=\dfrac{k}{\sqrt{a^2+b^2}}$. Thus $ab=2k$, so $c=\dfrac{b}{2},d=\dfrac{a}{2}$. Then $EX=\dfrac{b}{\sqrt5},EZ=\dfrac{a}{\sqrt5}$. Write $u=ab,v=a^2+b^2$. The product condition is $\dfrac{u^3}{10v}=36$, hence $v=\dfrac{u^3}{360}$. The requested reciprocal-area sum is $\dfrac{10}{u}+\dfrac{4v}{u^2}=\dfrac{10}{u}+\dfrac{u}{90}\ge\dfrac{2}{3}$ by AM--GM. Equality requires $u=30$, giving $v=75$; this is attainable with $a=2\sqrt{15},b=\sqrt{15},c=\dfrac{\sqrt{15}}{2},d=\sqrt{15}$. Thus the minimum is $\boxed{\dfrac{2}{3}}$.
