Let $P(n,k)$ be the success probability for a uniform target among $n$ possible consecutive integers and $k$ guesses. Put $P(0,k)=P(n,0)=0$. Given first guess position $g$, the probabilities of an immediate hit, a target to the left and a target to the right are $\dfrac{1}{n},\dfrac{g-1}{n},\dfrac{n-g}{n}$. Conditional on either side, the remaining target is still uniform. Average over the $n$ equally likely guesses, using symmetry of the two side sums:
\[P(n,k)=\dfrac{1}{n}+\dfrac{2}{n^2}\sum_{j=1}^{n-1}jP(j,k-1).\]
Evaluating three levels gives $\boxed{P(25,3)=\dfrac{13733255057}{55773217500}\approx0.246234}$. This exact recurrence can be reproduced by:
\begin{verbatim}
from fractions import Fraction as F
from functools import lru_cache
@lru_cache(None)
def p(n,k):
    if n==0 or k==0: return F(0)
    return F(1,n)+F(2,n*n)*sum(
        j*p(j,k-1) for j in range(1,n))
assert p(25,3)==F(13733255057,55773217500)
\end{verbatim}

