An axis of the whole picture must be an axis of each polygon, because their vertex counts differ. If there are common axes, align one as angle 0; the other axes of an $n$-gon occur at multiples of $\dfrac{\pi}{n}$, modulo $\pi$. The common grid has $\gcd(63,91,105)=7$ axes. Concentric polygons with one aligned axis attain this, so $\boxed7$.
