Axis-parallel squares contribute $4^2+3^2+2^2+1^2=30$. For a tilted square, choose its bottom vertex and the up-right side vector $(a,b)$ with positive integers $a,b$. Its other upward side is $(-b,a)$; its bounding box has width and height $a+b$. For each ordered pair $a,b\ge1$ with $a+b\le4$, there are $(5-a-b)^2$ translations. These contribute $9+4+4+1+1+1=20$. Each tilted square has a unique bottom vertex and up-right side, so it is counted once. Total $\boxed{50}$.
\begin{asy}
