Put $A=(0,0),B=(6,0),C=(0,8)$. Then $D=(0,2),E=(0,6)$. Since $BC=10$, the fractions along $BC$ are $\dfrac{3}{10}$ and $\dfrac{6}{10}$, giving $F=(\dfrac{21}{5},\dfrac{12}{5})$ and $G=(\dfrac{12}{5},\dfrac{24}{5})$. Shoelace on $F,G,E,D$ gives $\dfrac{1}{2}\left(\dfrac{72}{5}+\dfrac{72}{5}-\dfrac{42}{5}\right)=\boxed{\dfrac{51}{5}}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(7cm);
pair A=(0,0),B=(6,0),C=(0,8),D=(0,2),Ee=(0,6),F=(21/5,12/5),G=(12/5,24/5);draw(A--B--C--cycle);filldraw(F--G--Ee--D--cycle,lightgray);label("$A$",A,SW);label("$B$",B,SE);label("$C$",C,N);label("$D$",D,W);label("$E$",Ee,W);label("$F$",F,E);label("$G$",G,NE);
