A meeting occurs exactly when two adjacent chickens choose each other; distinct grid edges have distinct midpoints. Each of the eight corner-to-edge-middle edges has meeting probability $\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot\dfrac{1}{3}=\dfrac{1}{6}$. Each of the four centre-to-edge-middle edges has probability $\dfrac{1}{4}\cdot\dfrac{1}{3}=\dfrac{1}{12}$. By linearity of expectation the count is $\dfrac{8}{6}+\dfrac{4}{12}=\dfrac{5}{3}$, giving $\boxed{p+q=8}$.
