If there are $n$ sides, the arc from $A$ to $D$ through $B,C$ has angle $\dfrac{1080^\circ}{n}$. The inscribed angle $ACD$ intercepts the complementary arc, so $120=\dfrac{1}{2}(360-\dfrac{1080}{n})$. This gives $\boxed{n=9}$.
