Let unit vectors $u,v$ point from $A$ along $AB,AC$, and put $AB=c>8$. With $A=0$, $M=\dfrac{c}{2}u+4v$, and the bisector direction is $u+v$. Intersecting $M+t(u+v)$ with line $AB$ gives $F=\dfrac{c-8}{2}u$. Thus $AF=1$ gives $c=10$. The other intersection is $E=-v$, while $F=u$. Hence $EF=|u+v|=\sqrt2$, so $2+2u\cdot v=2$, and $AB\perp AC$. Therefore $BC=\sqrt{10^2+8^2}=\boxed{2\sqrt{41}}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
