pair A=(0,0),B=(10,0),C=(0,8),M=(5,4),F=(1,0),Ee=(0,-1),D=extension(A,(1,1),B,C);draw(A--B--C--cycle);draw(Ee--M);draw(A--D,dashed);label("$A$",A,SW);label("$B$",B,SE);label("$C$",C,N);label("$M$",M,NE);label("$F$",F,S);label("$E$",Ee,S);label("$D$",D,NW);
\end{asy}

Condition on the selected six points, listed cyclically 1 through 6. A chord crossing both others must leave two endpoints on each side, so it must join opposite points among the six. The only matching is $(1,4),(2,5),(3,6)$, and these chords do cross pairwise. There are $\dfrac{6!}{2^3\cdot3!}=15$ matchings total. Thus the conditional and unconditional probability is $\boxed{\dfrac{1}{15}}$.
