Take $A=(0,0),B=(2,0),D=(t,6),C=(t+3,6)$. The diagonals meet at a fraction $\dfrac{2}{5}$ of the way from the lower to upper base, as equating their horizontal coordinates gives $u(t+3)=2+u(t-2)$. Thus $E$ has height $\dfrac{12}{5}$. The midline $FG$ has height 3 and length $\dfrac{2+3}{2}=\dfrac{5}{2}$. Therefore $[FGE]=\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot\dfrac{5}{2}\cdot(3-\dfrac{12}{5})=\boxed{\dfrac{3}{4}}$.
