\end{asy}

Accumulate the divisor sum of every integer from 1 through 20189 by adding each divisor $d$ to all its multiples. Each divisor of each integer is included once, so the sieve computes the defining sum exactly. The resulting count is $\boxed{5001}$, as certified by this complete finite algorithm.
\begin{verbatim}
N=20190
sigma=[0]*N
for d in range(1,N):
 for multiple in range(d,N,d):sigma[multiple]+=d
answer=sum(sigma[n]>2*n for n in range(1,N))
assert answer==5001
\end{verbatim}

