Equality of distances to $(5,3)$ and $(6,0)$ gives $|y-3|-|y|=|x-6|-|x-5|$. The right side lies in $[-1,1]$, so $1\le y\le2$. Equality to $(-2,-2)$ now gives $|x-5|-|x+2|=2y-1\in[1,3]$. Therefore $-2<x<5$, and this difference is $3-2x$. In this interval the first equality gives $3-2y=1$, so $y=1$; then $3-2x=1$ gives $x=1$. All three distances are 6, verifying the point. Thus $\boxed{11}$.
