(a) The numbers $1000003$, $1000037$, and $1000121$ are prime. Their primality is certified by exhaustive trial division through their integer square roots:
\begin{verbatim}
from math import isqrt
for n in (1000003,1000037,1000121):
    assert all(n % d for d in range(2,isqrt(n)+1))
\end{verbatim}
The first is $1$ modulo $6$, while the other two are $5$ modulo $6$. (b) Their products with $1000003$ are respectively $35$ and $11$ modulo $36$, so no unique remainder modulo $36$ follows. Every prime greater than $3$ is $1$ or $5$ modulo $6$; if the remainders differ, their product is always $\boxed5\pmod6$.

