Order the sides $a\le b\le c$. Their condition is $(1+\dfrac{3}{a})(1+\dfrac{3}{b})(1+\dfrac{3}{c})=3$. A side $a=1$ is impossible; since all three factors are at most $1+\dfrac{3}{a}$, we have $a\le6$. If $b\ge32$, then $3=(1+\dfrac{3}{a})(1+\dfrac{3}{b})(1+\dfrac{3}{c})\le\dfrac{5}{2}(\dfrac{35}{32})^2=\dfrac{6125}{2048}<3$, a contradiction. Therefore $b\le31$. Solving the volume equation gives
\[c=\dfrac{3(a+3)(b+3)}{2ab-3a-3b-9}.\]
The following finite exact enumeration checks all possible ordered sides:
\begin{verbatim}
solutions=[]
for a in range(2,7):
    for b in range(a,32):
        den=2*a*b-3*a-3*b-9
        num=3*(a+3)*(b+3)
        if den>0 and num%den==0 and num//den>=b:
            c=num//den
            solutions.append((a*b*c,a,b,c))
assert max(solutions)==(9120,2,16,285)
\end{verbatim}
