\end{asy}

There are exactly $16$ blue small faces in total, and all $16$ are visible in the given assembly. Therefore every hidden small face is red. Each unit cube has exactly three hidden faces, and these three meet at a vertex. Rotate each small cube so this red triple occupies its three exterior directions at its assigned corner of the reassembled cube. Such a rotation exists because any cube vertex can be rotated to any prescribed vertex. All $24$ exterior faces are then red.
