Place $A=(-3,0)$ and $B=(3,0)$. The extended sine rule gives $R=\dfrac{3}{\sin\angle ACB}$, so the condition is $30^\circ\le\angle ACB\le150^\circ$. The boundary circles have radius $6$ and centers $(0,\pm3\sqrt3)$. Above $AB$, the admissible region is inside the upper-centered disk and outside the lower-centered disk; below $AB$ the roles reverse. Thus the locus, up to boundaries of zero area, is the symmetric difference of these disks. Their center distance is $6\sqrt3$. Their intersection consists of two $60^\circ$ sectors minus two triangles of area $9\sqrt3$, hence has area $12\pi-18\sqrt3$. The desired area is $72\pi-2(12\pi-18\sqrt3)=\boxed{48\pi+36\sqrt3}$.
