\end{asy}

Orient the unpainted face as the bottom. To avoid paint on the four vertical sides, a cube must occupy one of $9$ interior positions in each horizontal direction. Vertically it may occupy any of the bottom ten layers, excluding only the painted top layer. Therefore the count is $9\cdot9\cdot10=\boxed{810}$. The usual $9^3$ interior count omits the $81$ unpainted cubes exposed on the bottom face.
