Put $D=(0,0),A=(0,h),B=(b,0),C=(c,0)$, where $h=2018$, $|b|=20$, and $|c|=18$. The circumcenter and centroid are $O=(\dfrac{b+c}{2},\dfrac{h^2+bc}{2h})$ and $G=(\dfrac{b+c}{3},\dfrac{h}{3})$. Therefore $[DOG]=\dfrac{1}{2}|\det(O,G)|=\dfrac{|bc(b+c)|}{12h}$. If $D$ lies between $B,C$, then $|b+c|=2$, giving $\dfrac{60}{2018}=\dfrac{30}{1009}$. If $B,C$ lie on the same side of $D$, then $|b+c|=38$, giving $\dfrac{1140}{2018}=\dfrac{570}{1009}$. Both configurations are nondegenerate, so the answers are $\boxed{\dfrac{30}{1009}\text{ and }\dfrac{570}{1009}}$.
