Any noncrossing collection extends to a triangulation by adding diagonals in its remaining polygonal regions. A triangulation of an $n$-gon has $n-2$ triangles: their angle sum is $(n-2)180^\circ$. Counting triangle edges gives $3(n-2)=n+2d$, hence $d=n-3$. A fan from one vertex attains this bound. Thus the answer is $\boxed{2015}$.
