\end{asy}

Use $C=(0,0),A=(3,0),B=(0,4)$. The circumcenter is $(\dfrac{3}{2},2)$. Perpendicularity to the radii gives tangent equations $3x-4y=9$ at $A$ and $-3x+4y=16$ at $B$. Hence $D=(0,-\dfrac{9}{4})$ and $E=(-\dfrac{16}{3},0)$. Line $DE$ is $27x+64y=-144$, while $AB$ is $4x+3y=12$. Solving gives $F=(\dfrac{48}{7},-\dfrac{36}{7})$. Therefore $BF=\sqrt{(\dfrac{48}{7})^2+(\dfrac{64}{7})^2}=\boxed{\dfrac{80}{7}}$.
