Reflect $A$ across $2x-y+1=0$ to obtain $A\prime=(-2,2)$. Then $AP=A\prime P$, so the triangle inequality gives $AP+BP\ge A\prime B$. The reflected point and $B$ are on opposite sides of the line, so equality occurs where segment $A\prime B$ crosses it. Parametrize that segment by $(-2+6t,2-t)$. Substitution gives $2-t=2(-2+6t)+1$, hence $t=\dfrac{5}{13}$ and $\boxed{P=(\dfrac{4}{13},\dfrac{21}{13})}$.
