An affine scaling to a unit square preserves area ratios. Use $D=(0,1),E=(\dfrac{1}{3},0),F=(1,\dfrac{1}{3})$. The doubled area of $DEF$ is $\left|\dfrac{1}{3}(-\dfrac{2}{3})-(-1)(1)\right|=\dfrac{7}{9}$. Thus $[DEF]=\dfrac{7}{18}[ABCD]$, giving $[ABCD]=\boxed{\dfrac{450}{7}}$.
