Take $B=(0,0),D=(12,0),A=(12,16)$ and $E=(e,0)$ with $e>0$. Then $C=(2e,0)$ and $AB=20$. Projection onto $BA$ gives $BF=\dfrac{3e}{5}$, so $AF=\left|20-\dfrac{3e}{5}\right|=5$. Thus $e=25$ or $\dfrac{125}{3}$. Accordingly $AC^2=(2e-12)^2+256$ is $\boxed{1700\text{ or }\dfrac{48100}{9}}$. Both values exceed $AB^2=400$ and satisfy all conditions. If $F$ is additionally required to lie on segment $AB$, only $1700$ remains.
