Put $a=BC$ and let half of angle $A$ be $\theta$. Choose $A=(0,0)$, $B=(60\cos\theta,60\sin\theta)$, $C=(120\cos\theta,-120\sin\theta)$. The incenter formula gives $I=(\dfrac{14400\cos\theta}{a+180},0)$. Write $D=B+t(C-B)$. The perpendicular line has constant first coordinate equal to that of $I$, so $60(1+t)=\dfrac{14400}{a+180}$, giving $t=\dfrac{60-a}{a+180}<0$ by the triangle inequality. Hence $CD=(1-t)a=\dfrac{2a(a+60)}{a+180}=100$. This reduces to $a^2+10a-9000=(a-90)(a+100)=0$. Therefore $BC=\boxed{90}$.
