\end{asy}

Let $D(a,b)$ count allowable sequences ending at scores $(a,b)$ before the game has ended. Start with $D(0,0)=1$. For $0\le a,b\le21$, omit every other state with $\gcd(a,b)>1$. A permitted state receives $D(a-1,b)$ if $a>0$ and $b<21$, and $D(a,b-1)$ if $b>0$ and $a<21$. These inequalities prevent continuing an already finished game. Computing in increasing order of $a+b$, the only nonzero values $D(21,b)$ for $b<21$ are $D(21,1)=2$, $D(21,11)=14$, $D(21,13)=22$, and $D(21,17)=22$. By symmetry the answer is $2(2+14+22+22)=\boxed{120}$. The following complete finite recurrence certifies the computation.\begin{verbatim}
from math import gcd
D={(0,0):1}
for total in range(1,42):
    for a in range(22):
        b=total-a
        if not 0<=b<=21 or gcd(a,b)!=1:
            continue
        D[a,b]=(D.get((a-1,b),0) if a and b<21 else 0)
        D[a,b]+=(D.get((a,b-1),0) if b and a<21 else 0)
answer=sum(D.get((21,b),0)+D.get((b,21),0)
           for b in range(21))
assert answer==120
\end{verbatim}

Decompose the outside parallel layer by its nearest point on the convex prism. Nearest points in face interiors give outward prisms of total volume equal to the surface area, $9+\dfrac{9\sqrt3}{2}$. For an edge of length $L$ and exterior dihedral angle $\theta$, the edge region is a cylindrical sector of radius $1$ and volume $\dfrac{L\theta}{2}$. The six horizontal edges have total length $18$ and exterior angle $\dfrac{\pi}{2}$, contributing $\dfrac{9\pi}{2}$. The three vertical edges have total length $3$ and exterior angle $\dfrac{2\pi}{3}$, contributing $\pi$. Finally, the vertex regions are spherical sectors whose outward normal directions partition the unit sphere, so their total volume is $\dfrac{4\pi}{3}$. The desired volume is therefore $\boxed{9+\dfrac{9\sqrt3}{2}+\dfrac{41\pi}{6}}$.
\begin{asy}
