Call the first three points $A,B,C$ and the origin $O$. The signed doubled areas of $ABO,BCO,CAO$ are $45,61,39$, all positive. Thus $O$ is inside $ABC$, whose area is $\dfrac{145}{2}$. There are exactly three quadrilaterals, each obtained by replacing one outer edge with two segments through $O$. Their areas are $\dfrac{145-45}{2}=50$, $\dfrac{145-61}{2}=42$, and $\dfrac{145-39}{2}=53$. Their sum is $\boxed{145}$.
