The order of angles agrees with the order of opposite sides. Thus $AB=1$ must lie between $PA$ and $PB$. The region is the symmetric difference of the two unit disks centered at $A,B$. Their overlap is two $120^\circ$ sectors minus two equilateral half-rhombi, so its area is $\dfrac{2\pi}{3}-\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}$. The desired area is $2\pi-2\left(\dfrac{2\pi}{3}-\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}\right)=\boxed{\dfrac{2\pi}{3}+\sqrt3}$.
