\end{asy}

Sides are inversely proportional to their corresponding altitudes, so write them as $7t,3t,5t$. The area $K$ satisfies $2K=7t\cdot\dfrac{15}{7}=15t$. Heron's formula gives $K^2=t^4\left(\dfrac{15}{2}\right)\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\right)\left(\dfrac{9}{2}\right)\left(\dfrac{5}{2}\right)=\dfrac{675t^4}{16}$. Comparing with $K^2=\dfrac{225t^2}{4}$ yields $t^2=\dfrac{4}{3}$. Consequently $K^2=\boxed{75}$.
