\end{asy}

Let the ray $FP$ make angle $\theta$ with the positive $x$-axis, and write $p=FP$, $q=FQ$. By the focus-directrix property, $p=x_P+f=2f+p\cos\theta$, while the opposite ray gives $q=2f-q\cos\theta$. Thus $\dfrac{1}{p}=\dfrac{1-\cos\theta}{2f}$ and $\dfrac{1}{q}=\dfrac{1+\cos\theta}{2f}$. Adding proves the identity. A finite chord has $\cos\theta\ne\pm1$, so both distances are finite and positive.
