Four distinct intersections require $0<k<1$. Their abscissas are $-a,-b,b,a$, where $a=(1+k)^{\dfrac{1}{4}}$ and $b=(1-k)^{\dfrac{1}{4}}$. The condition $2b=2(a-b)$ gives $a=2b$, hence $1+k=16(1-k)$. Solving gives $\boxed{k=\dfrac{15}{17}}$.
