The endpoint graph of three edges has no isolated edge and cannot have two nontrivial components, so it is connected. It is either a triangle on three vertices or a tree on four vertices. Every triple of points yields one triangle, contributing $\binom83=56$. For four fixed cyclic points, there are $16$ labeled spanning trees: four stars and twelve paths (the latter are the $4!$ vertex orders divided by reversal). Four of these cross: they use both diagonals and one of the four sides. Hence twelve are noncrossing. The total is $56+12\binom84=\boxed{896}$.
