A $1\times3$ tile cannot stand vertically in a board of height two, so the two rows tile independently. Let $t_n$ count tilings of a row of length $n$. Its first tile has length one or three, giving $t_n=t_{n-1}+t_{n-3}$, with $t_0=t_1=t_2=1$. The values through $n=12$ are $1,1,1,2,3,4,6,9,13,19,28,41,60$. Therefore the board has $60^2=\boxed{3600}$ tilings.
