The two numbers already do not exceed the longest side. The only remaining triangle inequality is $x+y>1$. This is half of the unit square of equally likely pairs, so the probability is $\boxed{\dfrac{1}{2}}$. Boundaries have probability zero.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
