Equal tangent lengths and symmetry make $AO$ bisect the tangent angle, so $\angle CAO=30^\circ$. In right triangle $ACO$, the radius is $OC=6\tan30^\circ=2\sqrt3$. Since $OC\perp CD$, $OD=\sqrt{6^2+(2\sqrt3)^2}=\boxed{4\sqrt3}$.
