The four even positions must form an independent set of four cells. Color the grid as a checkerboard with the four corners and center black. Four black cells can be chosen in $\binom54=5$ ways, and all four white cells give one more way. There are no mixed choices of size four: including the center forbids all white cells; one corner allows only two white cells; two corners allow at most one white cell if adjacent or none if opposite; three corners allow none. Thus there are six position sets. Assign the four distinct even digits and five odd digits in $4!5!$ ways, yielding $6\cdot4!5!=\boxed{17280}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(7cm);
