\end{asy}

Triangles $ABD,DBC$ share altitude from $B$ to $AC$, so their area ratio is $AD:DC=1:13$. Hence $[ABD]=2$. Triangles $FAB,DAB$ share altitude from $A$ to $BD$, so $[FAB]=\dfrac{BF}{BD}[DAB]=\dfrac{7}{9}\cdot2=\boxed{\dfrac{14}{9}}$.
\begin{asy}
