\end{verbatim}

Put $A=(0,0)$, $B=(w,0)$, $C=(w,h)$, $D=(0,h)$. Then $E=(\dfrac{w}{3},0)$ and $F=(w,\dfrac{h}{3})$. The determinant of $E-D,F-D$ is $\dfrac{7wh}{9}$, so $[DEF]=\dfrac{7wh}{18}$. Consequently $wh=25\cdot\dfrac{18}{7}=\boxed{\dfrac{450}{7}}$. The angle merely fixes the shape by $w=\sqrt3h$ and does not change this area ratio.
