Place $A=(-1,h)$, $B=(1,h)$, $C=(2,0)$, $D=(-2,0)$. The diagonal gives $h^2+3^2=81$, so $h=6\sqrt2$. Then $AD=\sqrt{1+h^2}=\sqrt{73}$. Triangle $ACD$ has area $\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot4\cdot h=12\sqrt2$. Its circumcircle is the trapezoid's, and its radius is $\dfrac{9\cdot4\cdot\sqrt{73}}{4\cdot12\sqrt2}=\boxed{\dfrac{3\sqrt{146}}{8}}$.
