Compute the power exactly by integer exponentiation and add its decimal digits. This yields $\boxed{30001}$. The following complete integer calculation is reproducible and uses no rounding.\begin{verbatim}
import sys
if hasattr(sys,'set_int_max_str_digits'):
    sys.set_int_max_str_digits(0)
value=pow(2018,2018)
answer=sum(int(digit) for digit in str(value))
assert answer==30001
\end{verbatim}

For a $2\times n$ board, the leftmost column is covered either by one vertical domino or by two horizontal dominoes. Thus $c_n=c_{n-1}+c_{n-2}$ with $c_0=c_1=1$. Iteration gives $c_{100}=573147844013817084101$. Therefore $\log_{10}C(100,2)\approx20.758266663$, which rounds to $\boxed{20.758}$. The integer count is certified below.\begin{verbatim}
a,b=1,1
for n in range(2,101):
    a,b=b,a+b
assert b==573147844013817084101
\end{verbatim}
\begin{asy}
