\end{asy}

Let $S,T$ be their respective sums of sixty independent signs. Then $E[S]=E[T]=0$, $E[S^2]=E[T^2]=60$, and independence gives $E[ST]=0$. Their displacement difference is $(S-2T,2S-3T)$, with squared length $5S^2+13T^2-16ST$. Taking expectations yields $5\cdot60+13\cdot60=\boxed{1080}$.
\begin{asy}
