\end{asy}

Use $B=(0,0)$, $C=(14,0)$, $A=(5,12)$. The orthocenter is $H=(5,\dfrac{15}{4})$ and $M=(7,0)$, so $HM$ has slope $-\dfrac{15}{8}$. Thus $HK$ has slope $\dfrac{8}{15}$, meeting the horizontal axis at $K=(-\dfrac{65}{32},0)$ and line $AB$, whose slope is $\dfrac{12}{5}$, at $P=(\dfrac{65}{112},\dfrac{39}{28})$. Consequently $BP=\dfrac{169}{112}$. Orthogonal projection onto $AB$ gives $BF=\dfrac{70}{13}$. Power of $B$ relative to the circle through $F,P,K$ gives the directed equation $BK\cdot BQ=BP\cdot BF=\dfrac{65}{8}$. Since directed $BK=-\dfrac{65}{32}$, directed $BQ=-4$, so $Q=(-4,0)$ and $\boxed{QK=\dfrac{63}{32}}$.
\begin{asy}
