\end{asy}

Use $2\sin\dfrac{1}{2}\sin k=\cos(k-\dfrac{1}{2})-\cos(k+\dfrac{1}{2})$. The sum telescopes to $\dfrac{\cos(\dfrac{1}{2})-\cos(2019+\dfrac{1}{2})}{2\sin(\dfrac{1}{2})}$. A cosine-difference identity rewrites this as $\boxed{\dfrac{\sin(\dfrac{2019}{2})\sin(1010)}{\sin(\dfrac{1}{2})}}$, approximately $\boxed{1.808}$.
\begin{asy}
