Place $M=(0,0)$ and $N=(14,0)$. The side lengths give $L=(9,12)$. The circumcenter lies at $O=(7,\dfrac{33}{8})$, obtained by equalizing squared distances to $M,N,L$, and its radius is $\dfrac{65}{8}$. Since $LT$ bisects angle $L$, the point $T$ is the midpoint of the arc $MN$ opposite $L$; therefore $T=(7,\dfrac{33}{8}-\dfrac{65}{8})=(7,-4)$. The area is $\dfrac{1}{2}|9(-4)-12(7)|=\boxed{60}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
