\end{asy}

The second velocity is $(\cos t,-\sin t)$, so integrating from zero gives position $(\sin t,\cos t-1)$. At $t=5\pi$ this is $(0,-2)$, while the first walker is at $(5\pi,0)$. Their squared separation is $\boxed{25\pi^2+4}$.
