\end{asy}

The two radicals are the distances from $P=(x,2x)$ to $A=(0,4)$ and $B=(5,2)$, respectively. By the triangle inequality their sum is at least $AB=\sqrt{29}$. Equality occurs when $P$ lies on segment $AB$. The segment meets $y=2x$ at $P=(\dfrac{5}{3},\dfrac{10}{3})$, so the bound is attained. The minimum is $\boxed{\sqrt{29}}$.
\begin{asy}
