Heron's formula with semiperimeter $24$ gives area $24\sqrt{21}$. Put $B=(0,0)$, $C=(17,0)$, and $A=(\dfrac{129}{17},\dfrac{48\sqrt{21}}{17})$. The side-weighted incenter formula yields $I=(8,\sqrt{21})$. The circumcenter lies on $x=\dfrac{17}{2}$; equating its distances to $A,B$ gives $O=(\dfrac{17}{2},\dfrac{17}{\sqrt{21}})$. The point $X$ is the midpoint of the arc $BC$ not containing $A$, so also lies on that vertical line. The circumradius is $R=\dfrac{15\cdot16\cdot17}{4\cdot24\sqrt{21}}=\dfrac{85}{2\sqrt{21}}$, hence $OX=R$. The horizontal distance from $I$ to line $OX$ is $\dfrac{1}{2}$. Therefore the area is $\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot R\cdot\dfrac{1}{2}=\boxed{\dfrac{85\sqrt{21}}{168}}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(7cm);
