import graph;real f(real x){return (1-x^10)^0.1;}path q=graph(f,0,1);draw(q);draw(reflect((0,0),(0,1))*q);draw(reflect((0,0),(1,0))*q);draw(scale(-1)*q);draw((-1.2,0)--(1.2,0),Arrow);draw((0,-1.2)--(0,1.2),Arrow);label("$x$",(1.2,0),E);label("$y$",(0,1.2),N);
\end{asy}

If the outer width is $w>4$, the length is $2w$ and the picture dimensions are $w-4$ and $2w-4$. Thus $(w-4)(2w-4)=160$, or $w^2-6w-72=(w-12)(w+6)=0$. The positive valid width is $12$, so the length is $\boxed{24}$ inches.
