Order the sides $a\le b\le c$. The strict triangle inequality requires $c<\dfrac{9}{2}$, so $c\le4$. If $c=3$, the only possibility is $(3,3,3)$. If $c=4$, the other sides sum to $5$, giving $(1,4,4)$ and $(2,3,4)$. Smaller $c$ cannot give perimeter $9$. Thus there are $\boxed3$ triangles.
