\end{asy}

The triangle is right. Place its right-angle vertex at $(0,0)$ and the other vertices at $(6,0),(0,8)$. The circumcenter is the midpoint of the hypotenuse, $(3,4)$. Its inradius is $\dfrac{6+8-10}{2}=2$, so its incenter is $(2,2)$. The squared distance is $(3-2)^2+(4-2)^2=\boxed5$.
\begin{asy}
