The foot of the altitude is the center of the equilateral base. Its distance to a base vertex is $\dfrac{12}{\sqrt3}=4\sqrt3$. A right triangle with hypotenuse $12$ gives altitude $\sqrt{144-48}=4\sqrt6$. Hence $\boxed{m+n=10}$.
