Use affine coordinates $B=(0,0)$, $A=(1,0)$, $C=(0,1)$. Then $E=(\dfrac{2}{7},0)$, $D=(0,\dfrac{4}{9})$, and $G=(\dfrac{2}{5},\dfrac{3}{5})$. Write $F=tG$. Its membership in $ED$ gives $\dfrac{\dfrac{2t}{5}}{\dfrac{2}{7}}+\dfrac{\dfrac{3t}{5}}{\dfrac{4}{9}}=1$, or $\dfrac{11t}{4}=1$. Hence $BF:FG=t:(1-t)=\boxed{4:7}$. Affine coordinates preserve ratios on a line, so the result holds for every nondegenerate triangle.
