\end{asy}

The tangent at $(t,t^2)$ is $y=2tx-t^2$, with $x$-intercept $\dfrac{t}{2}$. Thus each step halves the positive starting abscissa. The corresponding right triangle has base $\dfrac{t}{2}$ and height $t^2$, so its area is $\dfrac{t^3}{4}$. For $t=1,\dfrac{1}{2},\dfrac{1}{4}$, the areas are $\dfrac{1}{4},\dfrac{1}{32},\dfrac{1}{256}$, whose sum is $\boxed{\dfrac{73}{256}}$.
