\end{asy}

Write $z_1=1+it$ with $-3\le t\le7$. At a fixed real coordinate $x$ with $|x-1|\le1$, put $s=\sqrt{1-(x-1)^2}$. The possible imaginary coordinates are the union of $[-3-s,7-s]$ and $[-3+s,7+s]$. Because the segment length $10$ is at least $2s$, these intervals overlap and their union is $[-3-s,7+s]$. Thus the locus is a rectangle of width $2$ and height $10$, capped by two semicircles of radius $1$. Its area is $\boxed{20+\pi}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
