\end{asy}

The hypotenuse is $41$, and the altitude to it is $h=\dfrac{9\cdot40}{41}=\dfrac{360}{41}$. At perpendicular distance $s$ from the hypotenuse, the triangle has width $41(1-\dfrac{s}{h})$ by similarity. For the square this width equals its side $s$. Solving gives $s=\dfrac{41h}{41+h}=\boxed{\dfrac{14760}{2041}}$.
\begin{asy}
