\end{asy}

Before quotienting by rotations there are $6\cdot5\cdot4\cdot3$ injective assignments to labeled edges. Since the colors are all different, no nonidentity rotation fixes a coloring; every rotational class has four members. Hence the count is $\dfrac{6\cdot5\cdot4\cdot3}{4}=\boxed{90}$.
