usepackage("amsmath");
size(7cm);
draw((0,0)--(1,0),red);draw((1,0)--(1,1),blue);draw((1,1)--(0,1),green);draw((0,1)--(0,0),orange);label("four distinct edge colors",(.5,-.3));
\end{asy}

A regular hexagon consists of six equilateral triangles, so its area is $\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{2}(\sqrt{2\sqrt3})^2=9$. The equal-area square has side $3$ and perimeter $\boxed{12}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
