\end{asy}

Let $T_n$ count triangulations of a convex $(n+2)$-gon, and put $T_0=1$ for an empty side region. Fix one boundary edge. The triangle containing it splits the remaining polygon into two independent regions, so $T_n=\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}T_jT_{n-1-j}$. Starting with $T_0=1$, this gives $T_1=1$, $T_2=2$, $T_3=5$, $T_4=14$, and $T_5=14+5+4+5+14=\boxed{42}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
