\end{asy}

Let $A=0$, $B=u$, $C=v$ as plane vectors, and let $J$ rotate vectors counterclockwise through $90^\circ$, choosing $ABC$ counterclockwise. External construction gives $E=-Ju$, $D=u-Ju$, $G=u-J(v-u)$, $F=v-J(v-u)$, $H=Jv$, and $I=v+Jv$. Therefore the squared lengths in question are $|u+v|^2$, $|2u-v|^2$, and $|2v-u|^2$. Their sum is $6(|u|^2+|v|^2-u\cdot v)=3(|u|^2+|v|^2+|u-v|^2)$. This is $3(6^2+9^2+13^2)=\boxed{858}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
