pair A=(0,0),Bp=(6,0),C=(-13/3,4*sqrt(35)/3);pair D=Bp+rotate(-90)*(Bp-A),Ep=A+rotate(-90)*(Bp-A),F=C+rotate(-90)*(C-Bp),G=Bp+rotate(-90)*(C-Bp),H=A+rotate(-90)*(A-C),I=C+rotate(-90)*(A-C);draw(A--Bp--C--cycle);draw(A--Bp--D--Ep--cycle);draw(Bp--C--F--G--cycle);draw(C--A--H--I--cycle);draw(H--Ep,blue);draw(D--G,blue);draw(F--I,blue);pair[]v={A,Bp,C,D,Ep,F,G,H,I};string[]names={"A","B","C","D","E","F","G","H","I"};for(int j=0;j<v.length;++j)label("$"+names[j]+"$",v[j],dir(30+40*j));
\end{asy}

At each dodecagon vertex, the square rotates through $90^\circ+30^\circ=120^\circ=\dfrac{2\pi}{3}$. Take square coordinates $A=(0,5)$, $B=(5,5)$, $C=(5,0)$, $D=(0,0)$. The stated distances give $P=(3,4)$. Its distances from $A,B,C,D$ are $\sqrt{10},\sqrt5,2\sqrt5,5$, respectively. Successive pivots use these four square vertices cyclically, so each is used three times in twelve pivots. Each traced arc has radius equal to the corresponding distance. The total length is $3\cdot\dfrac{2\pi}{3}(\sqrt{10}+3\sqrt5+5)=\boxed{2\pi(5+\sqrt{10}+3\sqrt5)}$.
\begin{asy}
