\end{asy}

Equal inscribed angles $\angle BAD=\angle DAC$ imply equal chords $BD=DC=14$. Since $A,B,D,C$ form a cyclic quadrilateral, $\angle BDC=180^\circ-120^\circ=60^\circ$. Thus triangle $BDC$ is equilateral and $BC=14$. Set $AC=x$. The cosine rule in $ABC$ gives $196=36+x^2-12x\cos120^\circ=36+x^2+6x$. Hence $(x-10)(x+16)=0$, and positivity yields $\boxed{AC=10}$.
\begin{asy}
