\end{asy}

To avoid $3$ for three moves, the path is forced to be $1\to2\to1\to2$. Its probability is $\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot\dfrac{2}{3}\cdot\dfrac{1}{2}=\dfrac{1}{6}$. The desired complementary probability is $\boxed{\dfrac{5}{6}}$.
