Let $D(i,j)$ count paths to $(i,j)$. The last step gives $D(i,j)=D(i-1,j)+D(i,j-1)+D(i-1,j-1)$, with $D(i,0)=D(0,j)=1$. Equivalently, with exactly $k$ diagonal steps, the remaining horizontal and vertical counts are both $5-k$, so the count is $\sum_{k=0}^{5}\dfrac{(10-k)!}{k!(5-k)!^2}=252+630+560+210+30+1=\boxed{1683}$.
\begin{asy}
