Put $B=(0,0)$, $C=(L,0)$, $A=(u,h)$. Then $D=(\dfrac{L}{2},0)$, line $EF$ has height $\dfrac{h}{2}$, and $X=(\dfrac{L}{2},\dfrac{h}{2})$. Extending $AX$ to height zero gives $Y=(L-u,0)$, so $|L-2u|=2$. The distance equations give $AC^2-AB^2=L^2-2Lu=11$, hence $L|L-2u|=11$. Thus $L=\dfrac{11}{2}$ and $p+q=\boxed{13}$.
