Use $B=(1,\sqrt3)$, $C=(-1,\sqrt3)$, $D=(-2,0)$, $E=(-1,-\sqrt3)$, $F=(1,-\sqrt3)$. Then $G=(-\dfrac{3}{2},-\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2})$, and solving the line equations gives $O=(-\dfrac{1}{4},\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4})$. Consequently $BC=2$, $CO=\dfrac{3}{2}$, $BO=\dfrac{\sqrt{13}}{2}$, and $[BOC]=\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{4}$. Dividing area by semiperimeter yields $r=\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{7+\sqrt{13}}=\dfrac{7\sqrt3-\sqrt{39}}{12}$. The answer is $7+3+39+12=\boxed{61}$.
