Inscribed angles subtending chord $BC$ give $\angle EAB=\angle EDC$. The vertically opposite angles at $E$ are equal, so triangles $AEB$ and $DEC$ are similar in that correspondence. Inradii scale by the similarity ratio, as follows from $r=\dfrac{\text{area}}{\text{semiperimeter}}$. Equal positive inradii force ratio one. Corresponding sides are therefore equal: $\boxed{AE=DE,\ BE=CE}$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(7cm);
