For an isosceles right triangle with leg $s$, its circumradius is $\dfrac{s}{\sqrt2}$ and inradius is $\dfrac{s(2-\sqrt2)}{2}$. Thus the ratio of circumradius to inradius is $1+\sqrt2$. The next triangle has inradius equal to the previous circumradius, so successive side ratios are $1+\sqrt2$. Across two steps the area ratio is $(1+\sqrt2)^4=17+12\sqrt2$. Hence $a+b+c=\boxed{31}$.
