Use $A=(0,0)$ with $AB$ along the positive $x$-axis and $AC$ at $60^\circ$. The circle has equation $x^2+y^2-ux-vy=0$. From $AE=10$, $u=10$. From $AF=11$, $10\cos60^\circ+v\sin60^\circ=11$, giving $v=4\sqrt3$. Thus its center is $(5,2\sqrt3)$ and radius $\sqrt{37}$. Writing $AB=s$, the opposite side is $\sqrt3x+y=s\sqrt3$. Its distance from the center is $\dfrac{(s-7)\sqrt3}{2}=\sqrt{37}$, since $s\ge11$. Therefore $\boxed{s=7+\dfrac{2\sqrt{111}}{3}}$.
