The area formula $[ADC]=\dfrac{1}{2}(6)(16)\sin\angle ADC=48$ forces $AD\perp CD$. Put $D=(0,0)$, $A=(6,0)$, $C=(0,16)$. Since $D$ is interior, write $B=(-u,-v)$ with $u,v>0$. Then $u^2+v^2=16$, and area decomposition gives $48+8u+3v=80$. Substituting $v=\dfrac{32-8u}{3}$ yields $73u^2-512u+880=0$, with roots $4$ and $\dfrac{220}{73}$. The first gives $v=0$ and is excluded. The second gives $v=\dfrac{192}{73}$, so $[ADB]=3v=\boxed{\dfrac{576}{73}}$.
