Let $AD=h$, $CD=c$. Apply the angle bisector theorem in right triangle $ACD$: $\dfrac{AX}{XD}=\dfrac{AC}{CD}$, so $\dfrac{3}{h-3}=\dfrac{6}{c}$ and $c=2h-6$. Pythagoras gives $h^2+c^2=36$, hence $5h^2-24h=0$. Since $h>0$, $h=\dfrac{24}{5}$ and $c=\dfrac{18}{5}$. Therefore $[ABC]=\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot\dfrac{24}{5}(6+\dfrac{18}{5})=\boxed{\dfrac{576}{25}}$.
