\end{asy}

The acute angle between chord $DE$ and the tangent $AB$ is $40^\circ$, because $DE\parallel BC$. A radius to a tangency point is perpendicular to the tangent. Hence in isosceles triangle $ODE$, the base angle at $D$ is $90^\circ-40^\circ=50^\circ$, and the smaller central angle is $180^\circ-2\cdot50^\circ=\boxed{80^\circ}$.
