Use $B=(0,0)$, $A=(0,3)$, $C=(4,0)$. Write $D=(4t,3-3t)$. Then $BD^2=9$ gives $25t^2-18t=0$; excluding $t=0$ yields $D=(\dfrac{72}{25},\dfrac{21}{25})$. If $E=(e,0)$, perpendicularity gives $D\cdot(E-D)=0$, or $\dfrac{72}{25}e=BD^2=9$. Thus $e=\dfrac{25}{8}$ and $EC=4-e=\boxed{\dfrac{7}{8}}$.
