Triangles $ABD$ and $BCD$ have side triples $7,24,25$ and $15,20,25$. They are right at $A$ and $C$, since $7^2+24^2=25^2$ and $15^2+20^2=25^2$. The quadrilateral angle sum is $360^\circ$, so the other two angles sum to $360^\circ-90^\circ-90^\circ=\boxed{180^\circ}$.
