\end{asy}

Scale $BC=1$ and set $B=(0,0)$, $C=(1,0)$. The ray from $B$ gives $A=(u,u)$, while the $30^\circ$ angle at $C$ gives $u=\dfrac{1-u}{\sqrt3}$, hence $u=\dfrac{\sqrt3-1}{2}$. The midpoint is $M=(\dfrac{u+1}{2},\dfrac{u}{2})$, so $\tan\angle MBC=\dfrac{u}{u+1}=2-\sqrt3=\tan15^\circ$. Since the angle is acute, $\boxed{\angle MBC=15^\circ}$.
