Set $ A=(0,0),B=(1,0),C=(1,1),D=(0,1)$. Then $ E=(\dfrac{1}{2},0),F=(0,\dfrac{1}{2})$. The two lines are $ y=1-2x $ and $ y=\dfrac{1}{2}+\dfrac{x}{2}$, giving $ G=(\dfrac{1}{5},\dfrac{3}{5})$. The determinant area is $\dfrac{1}{2}|\det(F-E,G-E)|=\dfrac{1}{2}|(-\dfrac{1}{2})(\dfrac{3}{5})-(\dfrac{1}{2})(-\dfrac{3}{10})|=\boxed{\dfrac{3}{40}}$.
