Subtracting 2015 gives labels 0 through 7, whose permissible differences are 1, 2, 4. Recursively pair the smallest remaining label with each permissible remaining partner. This counts each unordered matching exactly once because its smallest unpaired label has a unique partner. The recurrence evaluates to $\boxed{15}$:
\begin{verbatim}
from functools import lru_cache
@lru_cache(None)
def f(mask):
 if mask==0:return 1
 i=(mask&-mask).bit_length()-1
 return sum(f(mask^(1<<i)^(1<<j)) for j in range(i+1,8)
  if (mask>>j)&1 and j-i in (1,2,4))
assert f(255)==15
\end{verbatim}

Put $ AP=t $, so $ CP=5t-8 $. The law of cosines in $ ACP $ gives $ CP^2=64+t^2-8t $. Equating to $(5t-8)^2 $ yields $ 24t(t-3)=0 $. The value 0 cannot satisfy $ CP=5t-8\ge0 $, so $\boxed{AP=3}$. It gives $ CP=7 $ and lies on the side, verifying the solution.
