Reflection fixes $ C $ and preserves area, so $[PHC]=60 $. Put $ B=(0,0),C=(52,0)$. The side lengths give $ A=(40,9)$, and the altitude $ AH $ is $ x=40 $. The distance from $ C $ to this line is 12, so $ 60=\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot PH\cdot12 $, yielding $\boxed{PH=10}$. This holds whether $ P $ lies above or below $ H $.
