A rectangle's diagonals divide it into four triangles of equal area: each has a full side as base and half the opposite dimension as altitude. Extruding these triangles through the same prism depth gives four equal-volume pieces. The total volume is 250, so each, including the largest, has volume $\boxed{\dfrac{125}{2}}$.
