\end{asy}

The triangle has area 9 and hypotenuse $ 2x+y=6 $. A unit lattice square with lower-left corner $(i,j)$ is contained precisely when $ i,j\ge0 $ and its upper-right corner satisfies $ 2(i+1)+(j+1)\le6 $, or $ 2i+j\le3 $. For $ i=0 $ there are 4 choices of $ j $, and for $ i=1 $ there are 2. Thus six squares fit, leaving $\boxed{3}$ square units.
