\end{asy}

Writing $ q=\dfrac{3}{4}$, the areas form the geometric series $\pi(1-q^2)\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}q^{4j}$. Its sum is $\dfrac{\pi(1-q^2)}{1-q^4}=\dfrac{\pi}{1+q^2}=\boxed{\dfrac{16\pi}{25}}$.
