Use the angle bisector as the positive horizontal axis, with $ A=(0,0)$ and half-angle $\theta $. Then $ B=(4\cos\theta,4\sin\theta)$ and $ C=(6\cos\theta,-6\sin\theta)$. The angle-bisector theorem gives $ BD:DC=2:3 $, hence $ D=\dfrac{3B+2C}{5}=(\dfrac{24}{5}\cos\theta,0)$. Also $ AE=6\cos\theta $. Thus $\boxed{\dfrac{AD}{AE}=\dfrac{4}{5}}$.
