\end{asy}

Put $ U=(3+2s+3t,7-2t,5-2s-t)$. Its coordinates sum to 15, and every point of that plane is attained because the two coefficient vectors are independent. The constraint is $|U|^2=83 $. With $ H=(5,5,5)$, perpendicular decomposition gives $|U-H|^2=83-75=8 $. The objective is $|U-V|^2 $ for $ V=(8,4,3)$, which lies in the same plane and satisfies $|V-H|=\sqrt{14}$. On the circle of radius $\sqrt8 $ about $ H $, the closest point to $ V $ lies on ray $ HV $, at distance $\sqrt{14}-\sqrt8 $. Hence the minimum is $\boxed{22-8\sqrt7}$.
