Two intersecting lines make four regions. Each line meets the circle at most twice, so the circle is divided into at most four arcs; each arc can add at most one region. Thus there are at most eight pieces. Draw perpendicular lines through the circle centre: four interior sectors and four exterior regions give $\boxed8 $. 
