Only A and M repeat, with multiplicities three and two; the other five letters are distinct. A recurrence tracks the remaining multiplicities and the previous letter, allowing exactly the choices that do not repeat the previous letter. It counts each valid word once, and gives $\boxed{115920}$:
\begin{verbatim}
from collections import Counter
from functools import lru_cache
counts=tuple(Counter('MATHMAXBAD').values())
@lru_cache(None)
def count(t,last):
    if not sum(t):return 1
    return sum(count(t[:i]+(v-1,)+t[i+1:],i)
               for i,v in enumerate(t) if v and i!=last)
assert count(counts,-1)==115920
\end{verbatim}

Symmetry makes the perpendicular feet the side midpoints. Thus $ DEF $ is the medial triangle, with side length $\dfrac{s}{2}$. Its area is $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}(\dfrac{s}{2})^2=\boxed{\dfrac{\sqrt3s^2}{16}}$.
