\end{asy}

(a) Ties have probability zero, and all $ 3!$ orders are equally likely, so the probability is $\boxed{\dfrac{1}{6}}$. (b) Let the ordered cut points be $ u<v $. Their sample region $ 0<u<v<1 $ has area $\dfrac{1}{2}$ and constant density. The pieces $ u,v-u,1-v $ form a triangle exactly when each is less than $\dfrac{1}{2}$. The inequalities $ u<\dfrac{1}{2}$, $ v>\dfrac{1}{2}$, $ v<u+\dfrac{1}{2}$ cut out a triangle of area $\dfrac{1}{8}$. Therefore the probability is $\boxed{\dfrac{1}{4}}$. 
