\end{verbatim}

A two-dimensional face has exactly two freely varying coordinates. Choose them in $\binom{2014}{2}$ ways. Each of the other 2012 coordinates is fixed at one of two endpoint values, giving $ 2^{2012}$ choices. Thus the answer is $\boxed{\binom{2014}{2}2^{2012}}$. 
