Use unit-square coordinates $ A=(0,0),B=(1,0),C=(1,1),D=(0,1)$. Then $ X=(\tan15^\circ,0)=(2-\sqrt3,0)$ and $ Y=(1,1-\dfrac{1}{\sqrt3})$. The slope of $ XY $ is $\dfrac{1-\dfrac{1}{\sqrt3}}{\sqrt3-1}=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt3}$, so its direction angle is 30 degrees. Ray $ XD $ has direction 105 degrees, since it is 15 degrees left of vertical. Hence $\boxed{\angle DXY=75^\circ}$. 
