Here $ 1\le f(n)\le28 $. For an integer $ s $ in this range, $ f(s)$ is at least 10 only for $ s=19 $ or 28, when $ f(s)=10 $ and $ f(f(s))=1 $. All other $ s $ give a one-digit $ f(s)$ that does not change under another digit sum. Thus count $ n $ with digit sum 19 or 28:
