Let $ MT=2 $. With $ M=(-1,0),T=(1,0)$, the other points are $ L=(0,\sqrt3),A=(0,1),H=(0,-1)$. Thus $ HL=\sqrt3+1 $ and $ AL=\sqrt3-1 $, giving $\boxed{\dfrac{\sqrt3+1}{\sqrt3-1}=2+\sqrt3}$.
