There are $\dfrac{n(n-3)}{2}$ diagonals, since every vertex joins $ n-3 $ non-neighbours and each diagonal is counted twice. The quotient by $ n $ is integral exactly when $ n $ is odd. The odd numbers 3 through 2017 number $\boxed{1008}$.
