Take $ B=(0,0),C=(17,0),A=(x,y)$. Then $ x^2+y^2=400 $, while $ MC^2=(\dfrac{x}{2}-17)^2+\dfrac{y^2}{4}=100-17x+289=289 $. Consequently $ x=\dfrac{100}{17}$, which lies between 0 and 17, and $\boxed{BP=\dfrac{100}{17}}$.
