Put $ B=(0,0),C=(c,0),X=(x,y),A=(x,h)$. Perpendicularity gives $ y^2=x(c-x)$, hence $ BX^2=cx $ and $ CX^2=c(c-x)$. Also $ AB^2-AC^2=c(2x-c)=111 $. Therefore $|BX^4-CX^4|=|(BX^2-CX^2)(BX^2+CX^2)|=111c^2 $. Thus $ c^2=289 $ and $\boxed{BC=17}$. This is attainable: $ A=(\dfrac{200}{17},\dfrac{\sqrt{75600}}{17})$ and $ X=(\dfrac{200}{17},\dfrac{\sqrt{17800}}{17})$ with $ B=(0,0),C=(17,0)$ satisfy all conditions and place $ X $ inside the triangle.
