The substitution $ u=\dfrac{x}{2}$ maps the old region to the new one by doubling every horizontal distance and leaving vertical distances unchanged. Areas double, so the answer is $\boxed{20}$. This remains true even if $ f $ changes sign, because geometric area scales uniformly. 
