If the legs are $ a,b $ and hypotenuse $ c $, then $ a^2+b^2=c^2 $, so $ 2c^2=338 $ and $ c=13 $. Thus $ a+b=17 $, and $ ab=\dfrac{17^2-169}{2}=60 $. The legs are roots of $ t^2-17t+60=(t-5)(t-12)$, giving $\boxed{5,12,13}$. 
