Normalize the small triangular-grid side length to one. In oblique coordinates with basis vectors at 60 degrees, the lattice vertices are integer pairs $(u,v)$ satisfying $|u|,|v|,|u+v|\le2 $. Every drawn side lies in one of three directions, so two vertices can share a straight drawn side exactly when $ u $, $ v $, or $ u+v $ agrees. Convexity of the hexagon keeps that whole segment inside the grid. Thus enumerate all noncollinear triples satisfying these side tests:
\begin{verbatim}
from itertools import combinations
P=[(u,v) for u in range(-2,3) for v in range(-2,3) if abs(u+v)<=2]
def side(a,b):return a[0]==b[0] or a[1]==b[1] or sum(a)==sum(b)
T=[]
for a,b,c in combinations(P,3):
    det=(b[0]-a[0])*(c[1]-a[1])-(b[1]-a[1])*(c[0]-a[0])
    if det and all(side(x,y) for x,y in combinations((a,b,c),2)):T.append((a,b,c))
assert len(T)==38
\end{verbatim}
The required count is $\boxed{38}$. 
