\end{asy}

Unfold reflected tables into a rectangular grid. A corner-to-corner path becomes a segment from the origin to $(24m,15n)$ with nonnegative integers $ m,n $. For an interior path both are positive, and reaching no earlier corner requires $\gcd(m,n)=1 $. The number of side reflections is $ m+n-2 $, so $ m+n\ge4 $. The pair $(2,2)$ is forbidden. If $ m=1 $, the smallest admissible $ n $ is 3, giving length $\sqrt{24^2+45^2}=51 $. If $ m\ge2,n\ge2 $ and coprime, one is at least 3; the resulting lengths exceed 51. If $ n=1 $, then $ m\ge3 $ and the length also exceeds 51. Thus $\boxed{51\text{ feet}}$, attained by $(m,n)=(1,3)$. 
\begin{asy}
