draw((0,0)--(24,0)--(24,15)--(0,15)--cycle);draw((0,0)--(8,15)--(16,0)--(24,15),blue+linewidth(1));dot("$A$",(0,0),SW);dot("$B$",(24,15),NE);label("$24$",(12,0),S);label("$15$",(24,7.5),E);label("Two reflections",(12,18));
\end{asy}

A $ k $-gon has $ D(k)=\dfrac{k(k-3)}{2}$ diagonals, by counting vertex pairs and removing sides. Hence $ D(n+2)-D(n-3)=5n-10=200 $, giving $\boxed{n=42}$. The image side counts 44 and 39 are valid. The sketch illustrates how all vertex pairs except neighbours form diagonals.
