For height $ h\in(0,4)$, the shorter base is $ 2\sqrt{16-h^2}$. Area is $ A(h)=h(4+\sqrt{16-h^2})$. Put $ u=\sqrt{16-h^2}>0 $. Differentiation gives $ A'(h)=4+u-\dfrac{h^2}{u}=4+2u-\dfrac{16}{u}$. This vanishes at $ u=2 $, and changes from positive to negative as $ h $ increases, yielding $ h=2\sqrt3 $. The maximum is $(2\sqrt3)(4+2)=\boxed{12\sqrt3}$.
