\end{asy}

For the sphere, $ f(x)=\dfrac{4\pi x^2}{\dfrac{4}{3}\pi x^3}=\dfrac{3}{x}$. Completing the square gives the polynomial minimum $ c-\dfrac{b^2}{4}$, so the stated minimum forces $ b=0 $. Then $ g(6)=0 $ gives $ c=-36 $. Since $ x=\dfrac{3}{f(x)}$, the answer is $\boxed{g(x)=\dfrac{9}{f(x)^2}-36}$.
