Label vertices by three-bit strings. Flipping one bit moves to exactly one edge neighbour. Encode a subset by an eight-bit mask and test its stated local condition at each included vertex. Every nonempty subset is checked exactly once:
\begin{verbatim}
good=[]
for mask in range(1,256):
    if all(not(mask>>v&1) or
           sum(mask>>(v^(1<<j))&1 for j in range(3))>=2
           for v in range(8)):good.append(mask)
assert len(good)==31
\end{verbatim}
Thus the count is $\boxed{31}$.
