Set $ O=(0,0),T=(1,0)$. By reflection symmetry take $ R=(-\dfrac{3}{5},\dfrac{4}{5})$. Homothety centered at $ T $ with ratio 2 takes the small circle to the large, so $ S=2R-T=(-\dfrac{11}{5},\dfrac{8}{5})$. For the unit circle, the chord of contact from $ S $ has equation $ S\cdot(x,y)=1 $, namely $-11x+8y=5 $. The tangent at $ R $ is $-3x+4y=5 $. Their intersection is $ Z=(1,2)$. The determinant area is $\dfrac{1}{2}|\det(R-Z,S-Z)|=\boxed{\dfrac{8}{5}}$. Reflecting all points across $ OT $ covers the other choice of $ R $ and preserves area.
