A bisector consists of points equidistant from the two lines. For a point $(1,m)$ this gives $\dfrac{|m-20|}{\sqrt{401}}=\dfrac{|m-17|}{\sqrt{290}}$. Squaring and simplifying yields $ 37m^2-678m-37=0 $, so
\[\boxed{\left\{\dfrac{339+\sqrt{116290}}{37},\dfrac{339-\sqrt{116290}}{37}\right\}}.\]
The vertical line is not a bisector because points $(0,y)$ have unequal distances to the given lines unless $ y=0 $, so both have been captured. Their slope product is $-1 $, as expected for perpendicular bisectors.
