The angle-bisector theorem gives $AE:EB=6:14=3:7$, hence $AE=3$. The midpoint has $AD=5$, so $DE=2$. Both triangles have the same altitude to $AB$, and their area ratio is $\dfrac{DE}{AB}=\boxed{\dfrac{1}{5}}$.
