Let $R$ be the circumradius and $C=\angle ACB$. The sine rule in $ABC$ gives $AB=2R\sin C$. In triangle $BCH$, the altitude relations give $\angle CBH=90^\circ-C$ and $\angle BHC=180^\circ-A$. The sine rule therefore gives $\dfrac{CH}{\cos C}=\dfrac{BC}{\sin A}=2R$. Thus $CH=2R\cos C$. Since $CH=AB$, $\sin C=\cos C$, and the acute angle is $\boxed{45^\circ}$.
