All blocks begin at an integer from 100 through 982. Divisibility by the digit sum is an exact finite test. The following exhaustive certificate checks each of these 883 blocks; its inner loop tests every integer in that block, and the assertion verifies the required witness exists.
\begin{verbatim}
def digit_sum(n):
    return sum(int(d) for d in str(n))
for start in range(100,983):
    witnesses=[n for n in range(start,start+18)
               if n % digit_sum(n)==0]
    assert witnesses
\end{verbatim}
This covers every possible block within 100 through 999 and proves the statement.

