\end{asy}

Scale the side length to 2. Put $a=1+\sqrt2$ and take the vertices in order as $(-1,-a),(1,-a),(a,-1),(a,1),(1,a),(-1,a),(-a,1),(-a,-1)$. Successive edges all have length 2 and successive directions differ by $45^\circ$, so this is a regular octagon. The rectangle has area $2\cdot2a=4a$. Each outer trapezoid has parallel side lengths 2 and $2a$ and width $a-1=\sqrt2$, hence area $\dfrac{2+2a}{2}\sqrt2=2a$. The two therefore sum to $4a$, as required.
