After a prime $p$, until the next prime, $f(n)=n-p+1$. The longest relevant run has length 8: $89,90,\ldots,96$ or $113,\ldots,120$. Checking primes through 120 gives no longer gap before the cutoff, so the answer is $\boxed8$. The exact recurrence verifies it.
