The original area is $16-4(\dfrac{1}{2})=14$. Any inscribed regular octagon lies in the width 4 strip $-2\le x\le2$. If its circumradius is $R$, its width in any direction is at least $2R\cos22.5^\circ$: one pair of opposite vertices lies within 22.5 degrees of that direction. Thus $R\le\dfrac{2}{\cos22.5^\circ}$. Its area is $8(\dfrac{R^2\sin45^\circ}{2})=2\sqrt2R^2$, at most $32(\sqrt2-1)$. This bound is attained by vertices $(\pm2,\pm b),(\pm b,\pm2)$ with $b=2(\sqrt2-1)$. These vertices satisfy $|x|,|y|\le2$ and $|x|+|y|=2\sqrt2<3$, hence lie in the original octagon. The removal area is therefore $\boxed{46-32\sqrt2}$.
