Cuts cannot cross at new interior points, since that would create new piece vertices. Any nontriangular piece can be split further along a diagonal, so a maximum partition is a triangulation. Every triangulation of an $n$-gon has $n-2$ triangles: its total angle sum is $(n-2)180^\circ$, and the triangles contribute 180 degrees each. Thus the maximum is $\boxed{2011}$, attained by drawing a fan from one vertex.
