Because $TB=TC$, triangle $BCT$ has base angles 29 degrees, so $\angle ABT=87^\circ-29^\circ=58^\circ$. Angle $A$ is 64 degrees, giving $\angle ATB=58^\circ$. Thus $AB=AT$, and $AB+BT=AT+TC=AC=\boxed{37}$.
