The first two disks are interchanged by a half-turn about $(0,1)$, so any line through that point divides their combined area equally. Choose the line also through the third center $(2,0)$, which bisects that disk. The disks have disjoint interiors, so the line bisects their union. Its equation is $\boxed{y=1-\dfrac{1}{2}x}$.
