\end{asy}

Let $DC=x$, so $AD=2x$ and $AC=3x$. Stewart's theorem gives $9^2(2x)+12^2x=3x(6^2+2x^2)$. Dividing yields $306=108+6x^2$, so $x^2=33$. Thus $AC=3\sqrt{33}\approx\boxed{17.2}$.
