An inscribed angle has half the measure of its intercepted arc. A diameter intercepts a semicircle, so its opposite angle is $90^\circ$. Conversely a $90^\circ$ angle intercepts an arc of $180^\circ$, whose endpoints determine a diameter. The opposite side is the hypotenuse and is longest.
