There are $2^7=128$ labelled colourings. The two monochromatic colourings each form a class of size 1. Every other class has size 7: a nonidentity rotation cycles all seven sectors, so any colouring fixed by it is monochromatic. Thus there are $2+\dfrac{128-2}{7}=\boxed{20}$ classes.
