Use $B=(0,0),C=(0,8)$ and the field to their left. The band between $E=(0,3)$ and $F=(0,5)$ contributes a $6\times2$ rectangle of area 12. Above and below are two identical pieces of a left semicircle of radius 6, each extending 3 vertically from its center. Its area is $\dfrac{1}{2}(3\sqrt{36-9}+36\arcsin\dfrac{1}{2})=\dfrac{9\sqrt3}{2}+3\pi$. Thus total area is $6\pi+9\sqrt3+12=6\pi+\sqrt{243}+12$, giving $\boxed{84312}$. Boundary exclusion does not affect area.
