In each column there are initially four empty cells between the pawns. Every move reduces this gap by 1. Either player has a move whenever some gap is positive, so the game ends after exactly 24 moves, twelve by each. Let $w_i$ be white advances in column $i$. At termination $0\le w_i\le4$ and $\sum w_i=12$; black advances are $4-w_i$. Conversely any such vector is reachable: alternate white and black moves toward their prescribed targets, never exceeding either target. The count by inclusion-exclusion is $\binom{17}{5}-6\binom{12}{5}+\binom62\binom75=6188-4752+315=\boxed{1751}$.
