Remove all factors of 2 and 5 from $n$, leaving $m$ coprime to 10. A nonterminating reciprocal has period 1 exactly when $10\equiv1\pmod m$, so $m\mid9$. Including termination, $m\in\{1,3,9\}$. For each value, count numbers $n=m2^a5^b<100$. The three counts are 14,10,6, totaling $\boxed{30}$. An exact check follows.
\begin{verbatim}
count=0
for n in range(1,100):
 m=n
 for p in (2,5):
  while m%p==0:m//=p
 count+=m in (1,3,9)
assert count==30
\end{verbatim}

At radius $r$, a thin annulus has area $2\pi r\,dr$, so its probability weight is proportional to $r^2\,dr$. The desired ratio is $\dfrac{\int_0^1r^2\,dr}{\int_0^5r^2\,dr}=\boxed{\dfrac{1}{125}}$.
