The nine divisors are 1,2,3,4,6,9,12,18,36, giving $\binom96=84$ equiprobable sets. For each, check $a_1$ divides all entries, $a_2$ divides $a_4,a_6$, and $a_3$ divides $a_6$; these are all nontrivial index-divisibility requirements. Exactly 40 sets pass the complete finite check below. Thus probability $\boxed{\dfrac{10}{21}}$.
