Assign equal masses $ m $ to $ A,C $, so $ M $ has mass $ 2m $. The ratio $ BP:PM=3:2 $ requires mass at $ B $ to be $\dfrac{4}{3}m $. Thus $ BD:DC=m:\dfrac{4}{3}m=3:4 $. By the angle-bisector theorem, $ AB:AC=3:4 $, giving $\boxed{AB=\dfrac{27}{4}}$.
