The five empty cells must occupy exactly one cell in each row and column, so they correspond to a permutation $ p $ of 0 through 4. Each long diagonal must contain at least one empty cell, requiring some $ p(i)=i $ and some $ p(j)=4-j $. Testing all $ 5!=120 $ permutations gives $\boxed{48}$:
