Every positive even $ x $ goes in two steps to $ x-1 $, while every odd $ x\ge3 $ goes to the smaller nonnegative integer $\dfrac{x-3}{2}$. Thus a positive orbit eventually reaches 0 or 1. The latter follows $ 1,-1,-2,-3,-3,\ldots $ and never reaches 0. Exact iteration gives the successful starts $ 3,4,9,10,11,12 $, so the answer is $\boxed6 $:
\begin{verbatim}
sol=[]
for n in range(1,21):
 x=n;seen=set()
 while x!=0 and x not in seen:
  seen.add(x);x=2*x+1 if x%2==0 else (x-3)//2
 if x==0:sol.append(n)
assert sol==[3,4,9,10,11,12]
\end{verbatim}

Its area is $\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot12\cdot5=30 $. If the other altitude is $ h $, $\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot10h=30 $, so $\boxed{h=6}$.
