The quarter-disks have disjoint interiors and total area $ 16\pi $, so the remaining region has area $ 64-16\pi $. The square's center is $ 4\sqrt2 $ from each corner; tangency therefore gives the inner-circle radius $ r=4\sqrt2-4 $. Its area is $\pi r^2=16\pi(3-2\sqrt2)$. Subtraction gives $\boxed{64-64\pi+32\sqrt2\pi}$.
