Suppose its sides are $ a,b,c $ and altitudes $ h_a,h_b,h_c $. The area formula gives $ ah_a=bh_b=ch_c=6 $, so $ abc=\dfrac{6^3}{24}=9 $. Its circumradius would therefore be $ R=\dfrac{abc}{4\Delta}=\dfrac{3}{4}$. Every side is a chord and thus at most the diameter $ 2R=\dfrac{3}{2}$. But the area using any two sides is at most $\dfrac{1}{2}ab\le\dfrac{1}{2}(\dfrac{3}{2})^2=\dfrac{9}{8}<3 $, a contradiction. Therefore $\boxed{\text{no such triangle exists}}$.
