Each rectangle is uniquely determined by its two diagonals, which have the same midpoint and length. Group unordered pairs of posts by their coordinate sum and squared distance; any two pairs in one group give a rectangle, since their four endpoints are distinct and form equal bisecting diagonals. The complete enumeration below gives $\boxed{44}$.\begin{verbatim}
from itertools import combinations
from collections import Counter
pts=[(x,y) for x in range(4) for y in range(4)]
g=Counter((a[0]+b[0],a[1]+b[1],
           (a[0]-b[0])**2+(a[1]-b[1])**2)
          for a,b in combinations(pts,2))
assert sum(v*(v-1)//2 for v in g.values())==44
\end{verbatim}
