\end{asy}

Truth status alternates around the circle, so $b$ is even and $a=\dfrac{b}{2}$. The coordinate determinant gives $b=|c^2-21|$. If the other root is $d$, Vieta gives $cd=189$ and $c+d=a>0$. Since $c,d$ have positive product and positive sum, both are positive. The factor pairs with $c\le d$ are $(1,189),(3,63),(7,27),(9,21)$. Their root sums are 190,66,34,30, while $\dfrac{|c^2-21|}{2}$ equals 10,6,14,30. Only the last agrees. Hence $\boxed{(a,b,c)=(30,60,9)}$.
