\end{asy}

Since $2018=2\cdot1009$, removing the factor 2 leaves period equal to the multiplicative order of 10 modulo 1009. Direct modular exponentiation gives $10^{252}\equiv1$, while $10^{126}\equiv1008$, $10^{84}\equiv634$, and $10^{36}\equiv394\pmod{1009}$. Since $252=2^2\cdot3^2\cdot7$, any proper divisor of 252 divides at least one of 126,84,36. Therefore the order is exactly $\boxed{252}$. These congruences can be checked by repeated squaring.
\begin{verbatim}
assert pow(10,252,1009)==1
assert [pow(10,k,1009) for k in (126,84,36)]==[1008,634,394]
\end{verbatim}

For edges $ a,b,c\ge1 $, the nonnegative expression $ c(a-1)(b-1)+(c-1)(ab-1)$ equals $ 2abc-ab-ac-bc+1 $. Thus $ ab+ac+bc\le2abc+1=145 $, giving surface area at most 290. Edges $(1,1,72)$ attain this, so the maximum is $\boxed{290}$.
