\end{asy}

We have $ BM=2 $, $ BN=\dfrac{4}{3}$, and included angle $ 60^\circ $. Thus $[BNM]=\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot2\cdot\dfrac{4}{3}\cdot\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}=\dfrac{2\sqrt3}{3}$. Therefore $\boxed{k+m+n=8}$.
