An axis-aligned square touching the boundary at every vertex would be the outer square, so the permitted square is tilted. It has one vertex on each side, and can be written cyclically as $(0,t),(6-t,0),(6,6-t),(t,6)$ for integer $ 1\le t\le5 $, up to symmetry. Its side squared, hence area, is $ t^2+(6-t)^2 $. This convex quadratic is largest at the endpoints $ t=1,5 $, giving $\boxed{26}$.
