Put $ C=(0,0),A=(a,0),B=(0,a)$ and reflect coordinates if convenient; equivalently use $ A=(0,a),B=(a,0),C=(0,0)$. Then $ D=(\dfrac{a}{\sqrt3},0)$ and $ a^2=\dfrac{3}{4}AD^2=\dfrac{1881}{2}$. Since $\tan15^\circ=2-\sqrt3 $, we get $ E=(0,a(\dfrac{2}{\sqrt3}-1))$. The line from $ D $ at 75 degrees has slope $ 2+\sqrt3 $ and meets $ x+y=a $ at $ F=(\dfrac{2a}{3},\dfrac{a}{3})$. Coordinate areas now give
 \[[AFE]=\dfrac{2a^2}{3}(1-\dfrac{1}{\sqrt3}),\qquad [DFE]=a^2(\dfrac{4}{3\sqrt3}-\dfrac{2}{3}).\]
The irrational terms cancel in twice the first plus the second, leaving $\dfrac{2a^2}{3}=\boxed{627}$.
\begin{asy}
