\end{asy}

Use $ A=(0,0),B=(5,0),C=(5,5),D=(0,5)$. Subtracting the equations $ BE^2=64 $ and $ CE^2=25 $ gives $ E_y=\dfrac{32}{5}$. The first two distances give $ E_x=\dfrac{49}{5}$ or $\dfrac{1}{5}$; the distance $ DE^2=98 $ selects $ E=(\dfrac{49}{5},\dfrac{32}{5})$, which also obeys the noncrossing conditions. The incenter's side-weighted average is $ O=\dfrac{5B+8C+5E}{18}=(\dfrac{19}{3},4)$. Line $ BD $ is $ x+y=5 $; its length is $ 5\sqrt2 $ and the distance of $ O $ from it is $\dfrac{16}{3\sqrt2}$. Hence $[BDO]=\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot5\sqrt2\cdot\dfrac{16}{3\sqrt2}=\boxed{\dfrac{40}{3}}$.
\begin{asy}
