For a $ k $-dimensional face, choose its $ k $ varying coordinates and fix the other $ 4-k $ coordinates at either endpoint. Thus the count is $\binom4k2^{4-k}$. Vertices, edges, and squares number 16,32,24 respectively, summing to $\boxed{72}$.
