A cyclic trapezoid is isosceles: its base angles are equal because opposite angles are supplementary both from cyclicity and from parallel bases. Each leg therefore has horizontal projection 3 and height 4, so its length is 5. Hence $ CD=14 $ and $ AB=8 $. The area is $\dfrac{14+8}{2}\cdot4=\boxed{44}$.
