\end{asy}

A meridian arc of length $\pi $ on a radius 2 sphere changes angular position by $\dfrac{\pi}{2}$. The northern parallel has radius $ 2\cos(\phi+\dfrac{\pi}{2})=-2\sin\phi $. Its circumference is $\pi $, so its radius is $\dfrac{1}{2}$. The southern endpoint has distance $|2\cos(\phi-\dfrac{\pi}{2})|=|2\sin\phi|$ from the polar axis, which is the same radius. Thus the answer is $\boxed{\dfrac{1}{2}}$ mile.
