\end{asy}

Triangle $PQC$ has base $QC=4$ along line $BC$ and perpendicular height $PB=8$, so its area is 16. Since $M$ is the midpoint of $PQ$, triangles $PMC$ and $QMC$ have equal bases on $PQ$ and the same altitude from $C$. Each has half the area 16, so $\boxed{[PMC]=8}$.
