A midpoint square has diagonals equal to the previous square's side, so it has half the previous area. Four constructions multiply area by $(\dfrac{1}{2})^4=\dfrac{1}{16}$. Hence $\boxed{[ABCD]:[QRST]=16:1}$.
\begin{asy}
