Write the side length as $L$. The two centre coordinates each differ by at most $L-3r$, so their distance is at most $\sqrt2(L-3r)$. Nonoverlap requires distance at least 3 r. Hence $r\le\dfrac{\sqrt2L}{3(1+\sqrt2)}=\dfrac{2}{3}$. Equality is attained by placing the centres at $(r,r)$ and $(L-2r,L-2r)$, where the disks are tangent. Thus $\boxed{\dfrac{2}{3}}$.
