Intersecting chords give $CP\cdot DP=12$, so $CP$ must be a positive divisor of 12: $1,2,3,4,6,12$. Every pair $(d,\dfrac{12}{d})$ is realizable: take two lines crossing at $P$, put endpoints at opposite signed distances 2,6 on one line and $d,\dfrac{12}{d}$ on the other; the equal products ensure the four endpoints are concyclic. Thus $\boxed6$.
