Let the square be $(0,0),(s,0),(s,s),(0,s)$ and put $U=\dfrac{s x_P}{2},V=\dfrac{s y_P}{2},K=\dfrac{s^2}{2}>0$. The conditions become $|V|=10,|K-U|=14,|U|=18$. If $U=-18$ no positive $K$ works; if $U=18$, $K=4$ or 32. The target is $|K-V|$, with $V=\pm10$, giving $6,14,22,42$. The maximum $\boxed{42}$ occurs at $K=32,V=-10$.
