Power of a point in the plane through the centre and the secant gives $AY\cdot AZ=AX^2=2017$. The number 2017 is prime (trial division by primes at most 44 verifies this), so the only positive ordered pair with $AY<AZ$ is $(1,2017)$. It is attainable: take a sphere of radius 1008 and put $A$ at centre distance 1009; its radial secant has these distances and its tangent length is $\sqrt{1009^2-1008^2}=\sqrt{2017}$. Thus the sum is $\boxed{2016}$.
\begin{verbatim}
assert all(2017 % d for d in range(2,45))
assert 1009**2-1008**2 == 2017
\end{verbatim}

