Use $B=(0,0),A=(4,0),C=(0,4)$. In right triangle $BDC$, $BD=\dfrac{4}{\sqrt3}$, so $F=(-\dfrac{4}{\sqrt3},0)$. Write $E=(t,4-t)$ with $0<t<4$. The 60-degree condition gives $\dfrac{4-2t}{\sqrt2\sqrt{t^2+(4-t)^2}}=\dfrac{1}{2}$, so $t<2$ and $3(t-2)^2=4$. Thus $t=2-\dfrac{2}{\sqrt3}$. The horizontal and vertical components of $EF$ both equal $2+\dfrac{2}{\sqrt3}$, giving $\boxed{EF=2\sqrt2+\dfrac{2\sqrt6}{3}}$.
