Rotations about the circle centre show that the three chord lengths $AX,BY,CZ$ have the same distribution. The independently sampled points make these lengths independent. The distribution is continuous, so ties have probability 0. Permuting the three independent identically distributed lengths makes all six strict orders equiprobable; their probabilities sum to 1. Thus the desired probability is $\boxed{\dfrac{1}{6}}$.
