The diagonal passes through the circle centre, so $PQ$ is a diameter of length 4. With $A=(0,0),B=(4,0),D=(0,4)$, $X=(2,0)$ has distance $\dfrac{|2-4|}{\sqrt2}=\sqrt2$ from $BD$, whose equation is $x+y=4$. Thus the area is $\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot4\cdot\sqrt2=\boxed{2\sqrt2}$.
