The first condition gives $2R-2r=6$, so $r=R-3$ and the centres are 3 apart. The perpendicular diameter cuts the smaller disk in a chord of length $2\sqrt{r^2-9}$. Thus $2R-2\sqrt{(R-3)^2-9}=8$. Rearranging and squaring gives $R^2-6R=(R-4)^2$, hence $2R=16$ and $\boxed{R=8}$. Here $r=5$ and the smaller chord has length 8, verifying both conditions.
