Each coordinate has absolute value at most 44. For any pair $(x,y)$ with $x^2+y^2\le2017$, the possible $z$ values are the integers from $-m$ to $m$, where $m=\lfloor\sqrt{2017-x^2-y^2}\rfloor$. Thus the exact count is $\displaystyle\sum_{x=-44}^{44}\sum_{\substack{-44\le y\le44\\x^2+y^2\le2017}}(2\lfloor\sqrt{2017-x^2-y^2}\rfloor+1)=\boxed{379149}$. The following integer-only exhaustive summation evaluates every term, with no floating-point boundary errors.
\begin{verbatim}
from math import isqrt
answer = sum(2*isqrt(2017-x*x-y*y)+1
             for x in range(-44,45) for y in range(-44,45)
             if x*x+y*y <= 2017)
assert answer == 379149
\end{verbatim}

\begin{asy}
