Without teleportation there are $\binom{12}{6}=924 $ journeys. Each machine lies on $ x+y=6 $, so an ordinary monotone path cannot visit two machines. The numbers of paths from the origin to the machines are $\binom61,\binom62,\binom64 $, or 6,15,15. The numbers from those machines to the destination are the same respective values. A journey using one teleport has a unique departure machine and a distinct arrival machine. Its count is $(6+15+15)^2-(6^2+15^2+15^2)=810 $. Thus the total is $ 924+810=\boxed{1734}$.
