Use the triangle $x\ge0,y\ge0,x+y\le5$. A semicircle centre $(t,5-t)$ on the hypotenuse, bulging into the triangle, has radius at most $t$ and at most $5-t$, because its lowest $x$ and $y$ values are centre coordinates minus radius. Thus $r\le\min(t,5-t)\le\dfrac{5}{2}$. The centre $(\dfrac{5}{2},\dfrac{5}{2})$ and radius $\dfrac{5}{2}$ attain the bound. The area is $\dfrac{1}{2}\pi(\dfrac{5}{2})^2=\dfrac{25\pi}{8}$, giving $\boxed{33}$.
