Measured clockwise from 12, the minute hand is at 270 degrees and the hour hand at $ 9\cdot30+45\cdot\dfrac{1}{2}=292.5 $ degrees. The minute hand gains $ 6-\dfrac{1}{2}=\dfrac{11}{2}$ degrees per minute. The catch-up time is $\dfrac{22.5}{5.5}=\dfrac{45}{11}$ minutes, which rounds to $\boxed4 $.
\begin{asy}
