Write the other vertices as $P=(u,u^2)$ and $Q=(v,v^2)$. Equal distances from the origin imply $u^2+u^4=v^2+v^4$. Since $t+t^2$ is strictly increasing for $t\ge0$, we get $u^2=v^2$. Distinct vertices require $v=-u$. Thus $PQ=2|u|$, and equality with $OP$ gives $4u^2=u^2+u^4$, so $u^2=3$. The side is $2\sqrt3$, yielding area $\boxed{3\sqrt3}$.
