\end{asy}

The altitude to the hypotenuse is $h=\dfrac{3\cdot4}{5}=\dfrac{12}{5}$. At perpendicular distance $s$ from the hypotenuse, a parallel cross-section has length $5(1-\dfrac{s}{h})$ by similarity. For the square this equals $s$, so $s=\dfrac{5h}{5+h}=\boxed{\dfrac{60}{37}}$.
