The area of $KBC$ is $50$, and its semiperimeter is $\dfrac{10+\sqrt{x^2+100}+\sqrt{(x+10)^2+100}}{2}$. Therefore $r=\dfrac{100}{10+\sqrt{x^2+100}+\sqrt{(x+10)^2+100}}$. For $u>0$, $u<\sqrt{u^2+100}<u+10$. Hence $2x+20<\dfrac{100}{r}<2x+40$, giving $\dfrac{50}{r}-20<x<\dfrac{50}{r}-10$. With $r=10^{-100}$, this is $x=\boxed{5\times10^{101}}$ to one significant figure.
