After $n$ moves their positions are $J_n=8(1-(-\dfrac{1}{2})^n)$ and $D_n=\sum_{k=1}^n\dfrac{1}{k}$. The following finite computation uses exact rational arithmetic, checks every earlier move, and finds the first strict inequality at $\boxed{1674}$.
\begin{verbatim}
from fractions import Fraction
h=Fraction(0)
first=None
for n in range(1,1675):
    h+=Fraction(1,n)
    j=8*(1-Fraction(-1,2)**n)
    if h>j:
        first=n
        break
assert first==1674
\end{verbatim}

