Positivity forces $x>-\dfrac{1}{5}$. For $x\ge0$, the largest side is $5x+1$, and Pythagoras would give $4x+1=0$, impossible in this range. For $-\dfrac{1}{5}<x<0$, the largest is $3x+1$, so $(4x+1)^2+(5x+1)^2=(3x+1)^2$. This reduces to $32x^2+12x+1=0$, with roots $-\dfrac{1}{8},-\dfrac{1}{4}$. Only $\boxed{-\dfrac{1}{8}}$ satisfies positivity; the resulting sides are $\dfrac{3}{8},\dfrac{1}{2},\dfrac{5}{8}$.
