Put the first center at $(0,0)$ and $A=(-2,0),B=(2,0)$. The second center can be $(0,2)$. The overlap consists of the upper semicircle of the first disk, area $2\pi$, together with the circular segment of the second disk below $AB$. The latter has central angle $90^\circ$ and area $\dfrac{1}{4}\pi(2\sqrt2)^2-\dfrac{1}{2}(2\sqrt2)^2=2\pi-4$. Thus the overlap has area $\boxed{4\pi-4}$.
