Use coordinates $[0,16]\times[0,9]$. Cut along the staircase $(12,0)\to(12,3)\to(8,3)\to(8,6)\to(4,6)\to(4,9)$. A half-turn about $(8,\dfrac{9}{2})$ exchanges the pieces, so they are congruent. Keep the left piece fixed and translate the right piece by $(-4,3)$. At heights 0 to 3 the left piece fills width 0 to 12. At heights 3 to 6 the two pieces fill widths 0 to 8 and 8 to 12; at heights 6 to 9 they fill 0 to 4 and 4 to 12; and at heights 9 to 12 the translated piece fills 0 to 12. Thus they exactly form a $12\times12$ square, with no gaps or overlaps.
