Since $6\cdot INK\le999$, its hundreds digit $I$ must be 1. Thus $INK=100+10N+K$ with $0\le N\le6$. Testing these finite possibilities with distinct digits gives $\boxed{105\cdot6=630}$, so $I=1,N=0,K=5,P=6,E=3$. The following exhaustive digit check proves uniqueness.
