\end{verbatim}

The area is $\dfrac{1}{2}ab\sin C\le\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot20\cdot30=300$, where $a,b$ are the first two sides. Equality occurs when these sides have lengths 20 and 30 and are perpendicular. The third side is $\sqrt{20^2+30^2}=10\sqrt{13}<45$, so this configuration is permitted. The maximum is $\boxed{300\text{ square miles}}$.
