The other leg is $8$, so the triangle area is $24$. The three circular sectors inside the triangle are disjoint and have angles summing to $180^\circ$. Each radius-one sector remains within the triangle because all three altitudes exceed $1$. Their combined area is therefore $\dfrac{\pi}{2}$, and the requested area is $\boxed{24-\dfrac{\pi}{2}}$.
\begin{asy}
