Triangles $ABE,CDE$ are similar with length ratio $1:3$. Their altitudes to the parallel bases have the same ratio, so the distance from $E$ to $AB$ is $3$. Hence $[ABE]=\dfrac{1}{2}(2)(3)=\boxed3$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
