Let $E,F$ be its edge and face counts. A face with $k$ sides has angle sum $(k-2)\pi$. Summing the side counts over faces counts each edge twice, so the total angle sum is $(2E-2F)\pi$. Euler's formula $n-E+F=2$ gives $E-F=n-2$, hence the claimed $2\pi(n-2)$.
