Any circle of radius $r_1$ maps to a circle of radius $r_2$ by a dilation of factor $\dfrac{r_2}{r_1}$. A dilation multiplies every length, including arc length and diameter, by the same factor. Thus $\dfrac{C_2}{d_2}=\dfrac{C_1}{d_1}$. This common ratio is the number denoted by $\pi$.
