\end{asy}

Write $z=x+iy$. The given equation is $2i(2x+y)=i$, so $2x+y=\dfrac{1}{2}$. Write $w=u+iv=\dfrac{x+iy}{x^2+y^2}$. Inversion gives $x=\dfrac{u}{u^2+v^2},y=\dfrac{v}{u^2+v^2}$. Hence $u^2+v^2=4u+2v$, or $(u-2)^2+(v-1)^2=5$. Conversely every nonzero point on this circle inverts to a point of the line. Thus the locus is the circle with centre $(2,1)$ and radius $\sqrt5$, with the origin omitted.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
