Place $ A=(0,0),B=(4,0),C=(2,2\sqrt3)$. Then $ D=(2\sqrt3,2)$ and $ E=(0,4)$. The overlap is the quadrilateral with vertices $ A,Q,P,R $, where $ Q=AD\cap BC=(3,\sqrt3)$, $ R=AC\cap DE=(\sqrt3,3)$ and $ P=BC\cap DE=(6-2\sqrt3,6-2\sqrt3)$. These coordinates follow by solving the corresponding line equations. Reflection in $ y=x $ interchanges $ Q,R $, so the two triangles $ AQP,APR $ have equal area. Their combined area is $\det(Q,P)=(3-\sqrt3)(6-2\sqrt3)=\boxed{24-12\sqrt3}$.
