The centroid divides each median in ratio $ 2:1 $, so $ PA,PB,PC $ are one third of the three median lengths. Equality of these distances is equivalent to equality of the medians. If the opposite side lengths are $ a,b,c $, the median formula $ m_a^2=\dfrac{2b^2+2c^2-a^2}{4}$ gives $ m_a^2-m_b^2=\dfrac{3}{4}(b^2-a^2)$. Thus equal medians imply equal sides. Conversely equal sides give equal medians by the same formula, proving the equivalence.
