Put its centroid at the origin and let the two corresponding vertex vectors be $ u,v $. They have lengths $ 2,4 $, and the third vertex is $-u-v $. The area is $\dfrac{3}{2}|u\times v|=12\sin\theta $, so $\sin\theta=\dfrac{\sqrt{15}}{4}$ and $\cos\theta=\pm\dfrac{1}{4}$. Thus the third median is $\dfrac{3}{2}\sqrt{20\pm4}$, namely $ 3\sqrt6 $ or $ 6 $. Equal medians imply equal corresponding sides, by $ m_a^2=\dfrac{2b^2+2c^2-a^2}{4}$, so the second value is excluded. The answer is $\boxed{3\sqrt6}$. The two possibilities are shown; the right one has equal medians and is rejected.
\begin{asy}
