The sides are $x,20-x$ with $0<x<20$. Area is $x(20-x)=100-(x-10)^2\le100$. Equality occurs at $x=10$. Thus the maximum is $\boxed{100}$ square metres for a $\boxed{10\text{ by }10}$ square.
