There are $D=\dfrac{n(n-3)}{2}$ diagonals and $I=\binom n4$ interior crossings, one for each four-vertex choice. Insert diagonals one at a time. A diagonal with $k$ previous crossings has $k+1$ segments, each splitting one region. Each crossing is counted once, so the total is $1+D+I=\binom{n-1}2+\binom n4$.
