For side lengths $a,b,c$, take $ab=48,ac=54,bc=72$. Then $a^2=\dfrac{48\cdot54}{72}=36$, $b^2=64$, $c^2=81$. The diagonal is $\sqrt{36+64+81}=\boxed{\sqrt{181}}$.
