Every subset has a unique increasing list. Enumerate the $2^{14}$ subsets and test exactly the two local gcd conditions. The following complete calculation counts each eligible list once and gives $\boxed{55}$.\begin{verbatim}
from math import gcd
count=0
for mask in range(1<<14):
 v=[i+2 for i in range(14) if mask>>i&1]
 if (len(v)>=2 and all(gcd(x,y)>1 for x,y in zip(v,v[1:]))
     and all(gcd(gcd(x,y),z)==1 for x,y,z in zip(v,v[1:],v[2:]))):
  count+=1
assert count==55
\end{verbatim}

Complete the fourth power: $(x-2)^4=81$. The roots are $5,-1,2+3i,2-3i$. They form a square with perpendicular diagonals of length 6. Its area is $\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot6\cdot6=\boxed{18}$.
