pair B=(-1,0),D=(1,0),A=dir(110),C=dir(280),O=(0,0);draw(unitcircle);draw(A--B--C--D--cycle);draw(B--D^^A--C,dashed);draw(O--A^^O--C,gray);label("$A$",A,N);label("$B$",B,W);label("$C$",C,S);label("$D$",D,E);label("$O$",O,SW);
\end{asy}

All four-up and four-down paths number $\binom84=70$. For a bad path, reflect its initial portion through the first visit to height $-1$. This gives a bijection to five-up and three-down paths, counted by $\binom83=56$; the inverse reflects through the first visit to height 1. Thus the answer is $70-56=\boxed{14}$, the fourth Catalan number.
\begin{asy}
