size(7cm);
pair A=dir(90),B=dir(162),C=dir(234),D=dir(306),Ept=dir(18),F=(A+B)/2,G=(C+D)/2,H=(A+Ept)/2;draw(A--B--C--D--Ept--cycle);draw(F--G--H,blue);label("$A$",A,N);label("$B$",B,W);label("$C$",C,SW);label("$D$",D,SE);label("$E$",Ept,E);label("$F$",F,NW);label("$G$",G,S);label("$H$",H,NE);
\end{asy}

The total wire length is $4(a+b+c)$. Since $2022=2\cdot3\cdot337$ is squarefree, triples with all dimensions greater than 1 must be $(2,3,337)$ up to order. If one dimension is 1, the other two ordered as $b<c$ are $(2,1011),(3,674),(6,337)$; $b=1$ is excluded by distinctness. The largest sum is $1+2+1011=1014$, giving $\boxed{4056}$ centimetres.
