Let the first page be $ n $. The product-minus-sum is $ f(n)=n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)-(4n+6)$. For positive integers, $ f(n+1)-f(n)=4(n+1)(n+2)(n+3)-4>0 $, so at most one value works. Direct substitution gives $ f(445)=39744806534 $, with pages $ 445,446,447,448 $ valid in a book of fewer than $ 500 $ pages. Their sum is $ 4(445)+6=\boxed{1786}$.
\begin{verbatim}
from math import prod
assert prod(range(445,449))-sum(range(445,449))==39744806534
\end{verbatim}

Let the trapezoid height be $ h $, the semicircle radius $ r $, and $ KA=x $. The perpendicular distances from $ A $ to the two legs are $ x\sin K=\dfrac{xh}{65}$ and $(80-x)\sin L=\dfrac{(80-x)h}{60}$. Both equal $ r $. Cancelling $ h>0 $ gives $ 60x=65(80-x)$, hence $\boxed{KA=\dfrac{208}{5}}$.
