The expression is $\dfrac{1150274}{28}-\dfrac{3}{14}=\dfrac{1150268}{28}=41081$. This is prime, as the exact trial-division certificate checks every potential divisor from 2 through $\lfloor\sqrt{41081}\rfloor=202$. Hence the prime factorisation is simply $\boxed{41081}$.
