\end{asy}

The data have $n=4$, $\sum x=65$, $\sum y=82$, $\sum x^2=1425$, and $\sum xy=1290$. Minimizing the sum of squared residuals yields the normal equations $65m+4b=82$ and $1425m+65b=1290$. Solving gives $m=-\dfrac{34}{295}$ and $b=\dfrac{1320}{59}$. Thus an integer-coefficient equation is $\boxed{34x+295y=6600}$. The quadratic error function is strictly convex because the $x$ values are not all equal, so this solution is the unique least-squares line.
