No solution has $\cos\theta=0$, so divide by $\cos^2\theta$ and set $t=\tan\theta$. Then $1+t^2=2004(t-1)$, or $t^2-2004t+2005=0$. Its discriminant is positive and its roots have positive sum and product, so both roots are positive and correspond to unique angles in $(0,\dfrac{\pi}{2})$. Thus Vieta's formula gives the requested sum $\boxed{2004}$.
