For integer $x$ with $-12\le x\le12$, the exponent is positive, so the integer base gives an integer value: $25$ points. No integer $x$ makes the exponent zero. Outside that range the exponent is negative. Such a power of an integer is an integer only when the base is $1$ or $-1$; these occur at $x=154,152$ and give two more points. A zero base at $x=153$ is undefined. Every remaining integer base has absolute value at least $2$ and yields a nonintegral reciprocal. Therefore the answer is $\boxed{27}$.
