\end{asy}

Let the base sides be $x,y>0$ and height $h=\dfrac{4}{xy}$. The surface area is $S=xy+2h(x+y)=xy+\dfrac{8}{x}+\dfrac{8}{y}$. The three terms have product 64, so AM-GM gives $S\ge3\sqrt[3]{64}=12$. Equality requires $xy=\dfrac{8}{x}=\dfrac{8}{y}$, whence $x=y=2$ and $h=1$. Thus the minimum is $\boxed{12}$ square units.
