If $\theta$ is the included angle, $\dfrac{1}{2}(7)(9)\sin\theta=6\sqrt{26}$ gives $\sin\theta=\dfrac{4\sqrt{26}}{21}$. Hence $\cos^2\theta=1-\dfrac{416}{441}=\dfrac{25}{441}$ and $\cos\theta=\pm\dfrac{5}{21}$. By the law of cosines, the third side satisfies $c^2=7^2+9^2-126\cos\theta=130\mp30$, so the possible lengths are 10 and $4\sqrt{10}$. The smaller is $\boxed{10}$.
