If the horizontal motion uses $h$ steps, then $2\le h\le4$ and $4-h$ of them have length 2. Their possible orders number $\binom h{4-h}$. Similarly $v$ vertical steps have $\binom v{4-v}$ possible orders. Interleave the horizontal and vertical steps in $\binom{h+v}{h}$ ways. Thus the answer is $\sum_{h=2}^4\sum_{v=2}^4\binom h{4-h}\binom v{4-v}\binom{h+v}{h}=\boxed{556}$.
\begin{verbatim}
from math import comb
a=sum(comb(h,4-h)*comb(v,4-v)*comb(h+v,h)
      for h in range(2,5) for v in range(2,5))
assert a==556
\end{verbatim}

The distance is $\sqrt{(4-1)^2+(6-2)^2}=\boxed5$. The midpoint is $\boxed{\left(\dfrac{5}{2},4\right)}$. The slope is $\dfrac{6-2}{4-1}=\boxed{\dfrac{4}{3}}$. Thus a point-slope equation is $\boxed{y-2=\dfrac{4}{3}(x-1)}$, and rearranging gives $\boxed{4x-3y+2=0}$. Setting $x=0$ gives vertical-axis intercept $\boxed{\dfrac{2}{3}}$.
