\end{asy}

Put $AD=L$ and let the horizontal offset of each leg be $t$, so the height is $\sqrt3t$ and $0<t<\dfrac{L}{2}$. Then $AC^2=(L-t)^2+3t^2=\dfrac{3L^2}{4}+4\left(t-\dfrac{L}{4}\right)^2=2100$. Hence $L\le20\sqrt7$. The reverse triangle inequality in $AED$ gives $L\ge ED-EA=20\sqrt7$. Equality holds throughout, so $L=20\sqrt7$, $t=5\sqrt7$, and $E,A,D$ are collinear in that order. Since $AF=L-t=15\sqrt7$, we obtain $EF=EA+AF=\boxed{25\sqrt7}$. If written $m\sqrt n$ with squarefree $n$, then $m+n=32$.
