\end{asy}

Put $A=(0,0)$, $B=(1,0)$, $C=(1,1)$ and $D=(0,1)$. The four lines are $y=\dfrac{x}{2}$, $y=2-2x$, $y=1-\dfrac{x}{2}$ and $y=2x$. Their successive vertices around the bounded quadrilateral are $A$, $P=\left(\dfrac{4}{5},\dfrac{2}{5}\right)$, $Q=\left(\dfrac{2}{3},\dfrac{2}{3}\right)$ and $R=\left(\dfrac{2}{5},\dfrac{4}{5}\right)$. The shoelace formula gives area $\dfrac{1}{2}\left[\left(\dfrac{8}{15}-\dfrac{4}{15}\right)+\left(\dfrac{8}{15}-\dfrac{4}{15}\right)\right]=\boxed{\dfrac{4}{15}}$.
