Let $p_n$ be the probability of visiting $n$. Then $p_0=1$, $p_n=0$ for $n<0$, and $p_n=\dfrac{p_{n-3}+p_{n-8}}{2}$ for $n>0$, by conditioning on the first jump. Since every jump is positive, the recurrence accounts for every way to visit a point without overcounting. The following exact rational computation proves $0.175<p_{2020}<0.185$. Thus the requested rounded probability is $\boxed{18\%}$.
\begin{verbatim}
from fractions import Fraction
p=[Fraction(0) for _ in range(2021)]
p[0]=Fraction(1)
for n in range(1,2021):
    p[n]=sum((p[n-d] for d in (3,8) if n>=d),Fraction(0))/2
assert Fraction(175,1000)<p[2020]<Fraction(185,1000)
print(float(p[2020]))
