Call the crease endpoints $ U=(\dfrac{\sqrt3}{3},0)$ and $ V=(\dfrac{2\sqrt3}{3},1)$, and the upper-left corner $ W=(0,1)$. The crease passes through the centre, so each half has area $\dfrac{A}{2}$. Its angle is $ 60^\circ $. Reflection of the lower-right corner across it is $ W $, and reflection of the upper-right corner is $(\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2},\dfrac{3}{2})$, by the reflection matrix $\begin{pmatrix}-\dfrac{1}{2}&\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}\\\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}&\dfrac{1}{2}\end{pmatrix}$ about $ U $. Thus the overlap is triangle $ UVW $, whose area is $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{3}$. Therefore $ B=A-\dfrac{\sqrt3}{3}=\dfrac{2\sqrt3}{3}$ and $\boxed{\dfrac{B}{A}=\dfrac{2}{3}}$.
