If there are $k$ diagonal steps, there must be $6-k$ horizontal and $6-k$ vertical steps, making $12-k$ steps total. Their orders number $\dfrac{(12-k)!}{(6-k)!^2k!}$. Sum over $k=0,\ldots,6$ to get $\boxed{8989}$. The cases are disjoint and every path has exactly one such diagonal-step count.
