Join the centre to a side's midpoint and one endpoint. The resulting right triangle has angle $\dfrac{\pi}{n}$ at the centre, opposite leg $\dfrac{s}{2}$, adjacent leg $ a $, and hypotenuse $ R $. Therefore $\tan\dfrac{\pi}{n}=\dfrac{s}{2a}$ and $\cos\dfrac{\pi}{n}=\dfrac{a}{R}$. Hence \[\boxed{a=\dfrac{s}{2\tan(\dfrac{\pi}{n})}=R\cos\dfrac{\pi}{n}}.\]
