Put $ c=2023,a=2312,b=300 $. The angle-bisector theorem gives $ AD=\dfrac{bc}{a+c}$ and $ DC=\dfrac{ba}{a+c}$. Stewart's theorem on cevian $ BD=d $ gives $ a^2AD+c^2DC=b(d^2+AD\cdot DC)$. Substitution and cancellation yield $ d^2=ac\left(1-\dfrac{b^2}{(a+c)^2}\right)$. Hence \[\boxed{BD=\dfrac{\sqrt{2023\cdot2312\,(4335^2-300^2)}}{4335}}.\]The side lengths satisfy the strict triangle inequalities, so this positive value is valid.
