The triangle inequality requires $ x+16>31 $, so $ x>15 $. Being the shortest and not equal to 16 gives $ x<16 $. The other triangle inequalities then hold automatically. Thus $\boxed{15<x<16}$; one example is $ x=\dfrac{31}{2}$. No integer value works.
