Adjacent side vectors are $\overrightarrow{EF}=(3,3)$ and $\overrightarrow{EH}=(2,-4)$, whose lengths are $3\sqrt2$ and $2\sqrt5$. The perimeter is $\boxed{6\sqrt2+4\sqrt5}$. The absolute determinant gives the area: $|3(-4)-3(2)|=\boxed{18}$.
\begin{asy}
