By the shoelace formula for $A(0,0),E(2,0),G(3.5,1.2),D(0,4)$:
\[\dfrac12\left|0+2\cdot1.2+3.5\cdot4+0\right|=\dfrac{16.4}{2}=\boxed{\dfrac{41}{5}}.\]

The total volume is $24\cdot5+9\cdot2=138$ cubic inches, shared over a total base area $24+9=33$ square inches at a common depth $h$. So $h=\dfrac{138}{33}=\dfrac{46}{11}=\boxed{4\dfrac{2}{11}}$ inches (below both heights of $6$ in).
