\end{asy}

\emph{Step 1.} $\angle XPY=\angle DPC=45^\circ$, an inscribed angle on arc $DC$; and $\angle XBY=\angle ABD=45^\circ$.

\emph{Step 2.} $P$ and $B$ are on the same side of line $XY$: the line crosses segment $BD$ at $Y$, so $B$ and $D$ are on opposite sides; $X$ lies between $D$ and $P$ on chord $DP$, so $P$ is on the opposite side from $D$. Hence $X,Y,B,P$ are concyclic (segment $XY$ subtends equal angles at $P$ and $B$ on the same side).

\emph{Step 3.} In this circle, $Y$ and $P$ lie on opposite sides of line $XB$ (which is line $AB$: $Y$ is inside the square, $P$ is on the arc beyond $AB$), so $\angle XYB=180^\circ-\angle XPB$. Since $BD$ is a diameter of $\omega$, $\angle XPB=\angle DPB=90^\circ$. Therefore $\angle XYB=90^\circ$, i.e. $XY\perp BD$. $\blacksquare$

