question:
Let $n^*$ denote $\dfrac1n$, the reciprocal of $n$ (so $5^*=\dfrac15$). How many of the following statements are true?
\begin{enumerate}
\item[i)] $3^*+6^*=9^*$ \item[ii)] $6^*-4^*=2^*$ \item[iii)] $2^*\cdot6^*=12^*$ \item[iv)] $10^*\div2^*=5^*$
\end{enumerate}
$\textbf{(A)}\ 0\qquad\textbf{(B)}\ 1\qquad\textbf{(C)}\ 2\qquad\textbf{(D)}\ 3\qquad\textbf{(E)}\ 4$

solution:
Consider the disc $x^2+y^2\le a^2$, of area $\pi a^2$, and the map $(x,y)\mapsto\left(x,\dfrac bay\right)$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(5cm);
defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));
draw(ellipse((0,0),3,1.6));draw(circle((0,0),3),dashed);draw((-3.5,0)--(3.5,0),gray);draw((0,-3.4)--(0,3.4),gray);
pair P=(3*cos(1.0),3*sin(1.0)),Q=(3*cos(1.0),1.6*sin(1.0));draw(P--(P.x,0),dotted);dot(P);dot(Q);label("$(x,y)$",P,NE);label("$\left(x,\dfrac bay\right)$",Q+(0.25,-0.1),E,Fill(white));
label("$a$",(3,0),SE);label("$b$",(0,1.6),NW);
\end{asy}

A point $(x,y)$ lies in the disc iff $\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\dfrac{y^2}{a^2}\le1$. Its image $(X,Y)=\left(x,\dfrac bay\right)$ satisfies $\dfrac{X^2}{a^2}+\dfrac{Y^2}{b^2}=\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\dfrac{y^2}{a^2}$, so the map sends the disc exactly onto the region inside the ellipse. It stretches by the factor $\dfrac ba$ vertically, so the area is $\dfrac ba\cdot\pi a^2=\pi ab$. $\blacksquare$

(The stretching fact itself follows by approximating a region by thin vertical strips, each of whose heights is multiplied by $k$.)

The base angles are $\angle BAC=\angle BCA=\dfrac{180^\circ-36^\circ}2=72^\circ$.
