In triangle $ADC$ ($AD=3$, $DC=8$, $AC=7$) the bisector from $D$ gives $\dfrac{AP}{PC}=\dfrac38$, so $PC=\dfrac{56}{11}$. By the bisector-length formula,
\[DP^2=AD\cdot DC\left(1-\left(\dfrac{AC}{AD+DC}\right)^2\right)=24\left(1-\dfrac{49}{121}\right)=\dfrac{1728}{121},\]
so $DP=\dfrac{24\sqrt3}{11}$ and $\dfrac{DP}{PC}=\boxed{\dfrac{3\sqrt3}7}$.

