The inscribed angles $\angle AA'C$ and $\angle ABC$ subtend the same arc $AC$, so they are equal (or supplementary if $B$ and $A'$ lie on opposite sides of $AC$), and $\angle ACA'=90^\circ$. Hence triangles $AHB$ and $ACA'$ are similar (right angles at $H$ and $C$, equal angles at $B$ and $A'$), giving $\dfrac{AH}{AB}=\dfrac{AC}{AA'}$, i.e. $AH=\dfrac{bc}{2R}$. Then $K=\dfrac12a\cdot AH=\dfrac{abc}{4R}$, so $R=\dfrac{abc}{4K}$.

