question:
A circle with centre $O$ has diameter $AB=10$ cm, and chord $AM=8$ cm.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Find $BM$.
\item The tangent to the circle at $A$ meets line $BM$ at $P$. Find $AP$.
\item Find the area of triangle $AOM$.
\end{enumerate}

solution:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $\angle AMB=90^\circ$ (angle in a semicircle), so $BM=\sqrt{10^2-8^2}=\boxed{6}$ cm.
\item The tangent at $A$ is perpendicular to $AB$, so triangle $PAB$ has a right angle at $A$, and $\tan\angle ABM=\dfrac{AM}{BM}=\dfrac43$. Hence $AP=AB\tan\angle ABP=10\cdot\dfrac43=\boxed{\dfrac{40}3}$ cm.
\item $[ABM]=\dfrac12\cdot8\cdot6=24$, and $O$ is the midpoint of $AB$, so $[AOM]=\dfrac12[ABM]=\boxed{12}$ cm$^2$.
\end{enumerate}
