\[\angle(AM,AQ)=\angle(AM,AB)=\angle(PM,PB)=\angle(PM,PC)=\angle(DM,DC)=\angle(DM,DQ),\]
using in turn $Q\in AB$, circle $PABM$, $C\in PB$, circle $PCDM$ and $Q\in DC$. Hence $A,D,M,Q$ are concyclic. Similarly
\[\angle(BM,BQ)=\angle(BM,BA)=\angle(PM,PA)=\angle(PM,PD)=\angle(CM,CD)=\angle(CM,CQ),\]
so $B,C,M,Q$ are concyclic. All four circles pass through $M$ (the Miquel point). $\blacksquare$

