If $OT$ were not perpendicular to $\ell$, the foot $F$ of the perpendicular from $O$ would satisfy $OF<OT$ (a leg is shorter than the hypotenuse of right triangle $OFT$), which is a contradiction. So $OT\perp\ell$. $\blacksquare$

