\item[(b)] For which $r\ge0$ is $f(r)<0$?
\item[(c)] How many prime numbers are values of $f$? What is the smallest $r\ge0$ for which $f(r)$ is prime?
\end{enumerate}

solution:
The equation only makes sense for $x\ne0$. For such $x$, it is equivalent to $y=-\dfrac x2$. So the graph is the line $y=-\dfrac x2$ with the origin removed. If $x\ne0$ then $y=-\dfrac x2\ne0$, and conversely every $y\ne0$ is reached (at $x=-2y$).
