Row by row from the top (B = black): \texttt{BB..BB..}, \texttt{.......B}, \texttt{..BB...B}, \texttt{B....B..}, \texttt{B....B..}, \texttt{..BB...B}, \texttt{.......B}, \texttt{BB..BB..}. So the answer is $\boxed{\text{yes}}$.

After sorting, $a+b<90$ means $c=360-(a+b)>270$, i.e. the largest of the three numbers exceeds $270$.

In the triangle $\{x+y+z=360,\ x,y,z>0\}$, the region where $x>270$ is a corner triangle similar to the whole with ratio $\dfrac{360-270}{360}=\dfrac14$, so its area is $\dfrac1{16}$ of the whole. The same holds for $y>270$ and $z>270$, and these regions are disjoint (two numbers cannot both exceed $270$).
