If one point is the centre $O$, its distance to any other point is less than $1$. Otherwise draw the rays from $O$ through the six points. Six rays around $O$ make six consecutive angles summing to $360^\circ$, so some two points $P,Q$ satisfy $\angle POQ\le60^\circ$.
