The total area is $45=\dfrac12\cdot c\cdot2c\sin B$, so $c^2=\dfrac{45}{\sin B}$. By the law of cosines
\[AC^2=c^2+4c^2-4c^2\cos B=45\cdot\dfrac{5-4\cos B}{\sin B}.\]
Let $g(B)=\dfrac{5-4\cos B}{\sin B}$. Then $g(B)\ge3$, because $5-4\cos B-3\sin B=5-5\cos(B-\varphi)\ge0$ with $\cos\varphi=\dfrac45$, $\sin\varphi=\dfrac35$; equality holds at $B=\varphi$. So $AC^2\ge135$, i.e. $AC\ge\sqrt{135}\approx11.62$. As $B$ varies, $AC$ takes every value $\ge\sqrt{135}$ continuously, so the smallest integer value is $\boxed{12}$.

