Collinearity of $A,O',C'$: $\dfrac{1-s}{\sqrt2s+\sqrt2}=\dfrac{7}{31\sqrt2}$, i.e. $31(1-s)=7(s+1)$, so $s=\dfrac{12}{19}$. The height of $C'$ is $1-s=\dfrac7{19}$, and $\dfrac{C'C}{PC}=\boxed{\dfrac7{19}}$.

