Use coordinates $A=(0,0)$, $B=(b,0)$, $C=(0,c)$ and put $k=b^2+c^2$.

$D=(0,d)$ with $\overrightarrow{BD}\cdot\overrightarrow{BC}=b^2+dc=0$, so $D=\left(0,-\dfrac{b^2}c\right)$; similarly $E=\left(-\dfrac{c^2}b,0\right)$. Line $DE$ is $b^3x+c^3y=-b^2c^2$, with normal vector $(b^3,c^3)$.
