The square has area $36$, so $[DEA]=14=\dfrac12\cdot6\cdot(3-u)$, giving $3-u=\dfrac{14}3$ and $u=\boxed{-\dfrac53}$.

The pieces have $3\cdot2017+5\cdot2016=6051+10080=16131$ sides in all. The chain has $4033$ pieces and hence $4032$ joins, and each join hides $2$ sides.
