Triangles $ABM$ and $CDM$ are similar with ratio $8:14$. If $[ABM]=x$, then $[CDM]=\left(\dfrac74\right)^2x$ and $[ADM]=[BCM]=\dfrac74x$ (same heights, bases in ratio $\dfrac74$). So $x\left(1+\dfrac72+\dfrac{49}{16}\right)=132$, giving $x=\dfrac{192}{11}$ and $[ADM]=\dfrac74x=\boxed{\dfrac{336}{11}}$ ft$^2$.

$x^2-x-2=x+1$ gives $(x-3)(x+1)=0$: the points $(-1,0)$ and $(3,4)$.
\begin{asy}
