Rotate the picture so that the four points have different $y$-coordinates, and draw a horizontal line with two points above ($U_1$ left of $U_2$) and two below ($L_1$ left of $L_2$). Aim $L_1$ up-right and $L_2$ up-left: since $L_1$ is to the left of $L_2$, together they light the whole half-plane above the higher of $L_1,L_2$. Aim $U_1$ down-right and $U_2$ down-left: they light the whole half-plane below the lower of $U_1,U_2$. These two half-planes together cover the plane (the line separates the pairs), so the plane is lit. $\blacksquare$
