dot((0,0));draw((0,0)--(sqrt(3)*dir(0)),Arrow(3));label("$\sqrt3$",(0.85,0),S,fontsize(8pt));label("$2$",(P[0]+P[1])/2,NE,fontsize(8pt));
\end{asy}

The union has area
\[2\cdot6\sqrt3-(72-36\sqrt3)=\boxed{48\sqrt3-72}\approx11.14.\]
(If ``total area'' meant simply the sum of the two areas, the answer would be $12\sqrt3$.)

By the power of the point $A$ with respect to $\omega$,
\[AD\cdot AE=AB\cdot AC=1\cdot\left(1+\dfrac89\right)=\dfrac{17}9.\]
Since $AE=AD+DE=2AD$, we get $2AD^2=\dfrac{17}9$, so
\[AD=\sqrt{\dfrac{17}{18}}=\boxed{\dfrac{\sqrt{34}}6}.\]
