A number divisible by four of them is divisible by their least common multiple:
\begin{itemize}
\item omitting $6$: $\operatorname{lcm}(15,20,21,70)=420$;
\item omitting $15$: $\operatorname{lcm}(6,20,21,70)=420$;
\item omitting $20$: $\operatorname{lcm}(6,15,21,70)=210$;
\item omitting $21$: $\operatorname{lcm}(6,15,20,70)=420$;
\item omitting $70$: $\operatorname{lcm}(6,15,20,21)=420$.
\end{itemize}
The smallest candidate is $210$, which is divisible by $6,15,21,70$ but not by $20$. The answer is $\boxed{210}$.

Split the board into four $2\times2$ quadrants. A quadrant holds at most $2$ chips (two diagonal squares), so with $7$ chips three quadrants are \emph{full} (one diagonal each) and one holds $1$ chip. Colour the board like a chessboard, so each diagonal of a quadrant has a single colour.

\textbf{Full quadrants have the same colour.} For two side-by-side quadrants, if their diagonals had different colours, the two chips along the common edge would be adjacent (for example, $(1,1)$ and $(2,1)$ with columns and rows numbered $0$ to $3$). The three full quadrants are connected, so they all use the same colour $c$.

\textbf{The remaining chip.} If it lies on a square of colour $c$, all its neighbours have the other colour and are empty: this gives $4\cdot2\cdot2=16$ placements (choose the partial quadrant, the colour $c$, and one of its two $c$-squares). These are the sets of $7$ squares of one colour. If it lies on the other colour, it must avoid the chips of colour $c$ next to it in the adjacent quadrants. Every square of a quadrant except the board's corner has a neighbour in an adjacent quadrant, and that neighbour has colour $c$ and lies on the full diagonal, so the chip must be on the board corner. This requires $c$ to be the colour opposite to that corner, which gives $4$ more placements (one per choice of partial quadrant).

The total is $16+4=\boxed{20}$. None of the answer choices printed with the problem in the post ($16,28,32,40,56$) is correct.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(3cm);
defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));
