Let the trapezoid be $ABCD$ with bases $AB=a>CD=b$ and altitude $3$. By symmetry, $C$ projects onto $AB$ at distance $\dfrac{a+b}2$ from $A$. So in the right triangle formed by the diagonal $AC$, $\tan\theta=3\div\dfrac{a+b}2=\dfrac6{a+b}=\dfrac14$, giving $\dfrac{a+b}2=12$.
