draw(P--Q--R--S_--cycle);draw(P--R,dashed);draw(P--Qp--R,linewidth(0.9));draw(S_--Qp,dotted);
label("$P$",P,NW);label("$Q$",Q,NE);label("$R$",R,SE);label("$S$",S_,W);label("$Q'$",Qp,S);label("$\dfrac75$",(S_+Qp)/2,W,fontsize(8pt));label("$4$",(2,3),N,fontsize(8pt));label("$3$",(4,1.5),E,fontsize(8pt));
\end{asy}

Answer $\boxed{\textbf{(E)}\ \dfrac75}$. (Alternatively, $PRQ'S$ is an isosceles trapezoid with $SQ'\parallel PR$.)

Subtract the three corner triangles. A corner triangle with sides along the triangle's sides has area equal to the product of the two side fractions times $[ABC]$:
\[[AZY]=\dfrac34\cdot\dfrac13\cdot120=30,\quad[BXZ]=\dfrac12\cdot\dfrac14\cdot120=15,\quad[CYX]=\dfrac23\cdot\dfrac12\cdot120=40.\]
