So $[XYZ]=120-30-15-40=35$. Answer $\boxed{\textbf{(A)}\ 35}$.

Since $|x+y|+|x-y|=2\max(|x|,|y|)$, the first two conditions say $2\max(|x|,|y|)\ge|x||y|$. The region is symmetric in all four quadrants, so take $x,y\ge0$. If $x\ge y$ the condition is $2x\ge xy$, i.e. $y\le2$ (or $x=0$); if $y\ge x$ it is $x\le2$. So in the first quadrant we keep the part of the triangle $x+y\le15$ where $\min(x,y)\le2$, removing the triangle $x,y>2$, $x+y\le15$ with legs $11$.
\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(4.5cm);
defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));
fill((15,0)--(0,15)--(-15,0)--(0,-15)--cycle,rgb(0.85,0.9,1));
fill((2,2)--(13,2)--(2,13)--cycle,white);fill((-2,2)--(-13,2)--(-2,13)--cycle,white);fill((2,-2)--(13,-2)--(2,-13)--cycle,white);fill((-2,-2)--(-13,-2)--(-2,-13)--cycle,white);
draw((15,0)--(0,15)--(-15,0)--(0,-15)--cycle);
