The area is $\dfrac12\cdot BD\cdot AC=\dfrac12\cdot16\cdot21=\boxed{168}$.

Let $F$ be the point of the road directly below $P$. The angles of elevation increase as the observer approaches, so $A,B,C,F$ lie in this order and $3\theta<90^\circ$, i.e. $\theta<30^\circ$.

\begin{asy}
