Write $a^2-1=(a-1)(a+1)$.
\begin{itemize}
\item Since $a$ is odd, $a-1$ and $a+1$ are consecutive even numbers, so one of them is divisible by $4$ and the other by $2$; hence $8\mid(a-1)(a+1)$.
\item Since $3\nmid a$, one of the three consecutive integers $a-1,a,a+1$ that is divisible by $3$ is $a-1$ or $a+1$; hence $3\mid(a-1)(a+1)$.
\end{itemize}
As $\gcd(8,3)=1$, we get $24\mid a^2-1$. $\blacksquare$

