Through $D$ draw the line parallel to $AC$, meeting line $AB$ at $E$. Then $ACDE$ is a parallelogram, so $DE=AC=5$ and $EA=DC$. Hence $EB=EA+AB=DC+AB$, and since $DE\parallel AC\perp BD$, triangle $EDB$ has a right angle at $D$.

