Here $l(n)$ is the Gregorian leap-year rule and $f(a,b)$ is the number of days in month $a$ of year $b$. So $365(c-1)+h(c-1)$ is the number of days in years $1,\dots,c-1$, and $g(a,b,c)$ is the position of day $b$ of month $a$ within year $c$. Thus $d(a,b,c)$ numbers the date (day $b$, month $a$, year $c$) counting 1 January of year $1$ as day $1$, and the required difference is the number of days from 12 May 2008 to 31 December 2021.
\begin{itemize}
\item From 12 May 2008 to 12 May 2021: $13$ years containing the leap days of 2012, 2016 and 2020 (29 February 2008 is earlier), so $13\cdot365+3=4748$ days.
\item From 12 May 2021 to 31 December 2021: $19$ more days of May, then $30+31+31+30+31+30+31=214$, giving $233$ days.
\end{itemize}
The answer is $4748+233=\boxed{4981}$. (A direct computation of $d$ gives the same.)

Note that $365=13^2+14^2$, so a square of area $365$ has side $\sqrt{365}$, the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs $13$ and $14$.

