A square of side $1$ contains the disc of radius $\dfrac12$ about its centre (its inscribed circle). Both squares contain the same disc, so their intersection contains it, and
\[\text{area of intersection}\ \ge\ \pi\left(\dfrac12\right)^2=\dfrac\pi4>\dfrac34,\]
since $\pi>3$. $\blacksquare$

