By the angle bisector theorem, $\dfrac{CD}{DB}=\dfrac{CA}{AB}$ and $\dfrac{CE}{EA}=\dfrac{CB}{BA}$. Since $DE\parallel AB$, $\dfrac{CD}{DB}=\dfrac{CE}{EA}$, so $CA=CB$ and $\angle A=\angle B$. Let $\angle A=\angle B=2x$.

