Let circle $B$ have radius $3r$ and circle $A$ radius $r$. The centre of $A$ travels around a circle of radius $3r+r=4r$, a distance of $2\pi\cdot4r$. For rolling without slipping, the rotation of $A$ equals the distance travelled by its centre divided by its radius, so $A$ turns through $\dfrac{8\pi r}{r}=8\pi$ radians, i.e. $\boxed{4}$ full rotations.

