\[\tan\theta=\dfrac{\dfrac{9}{x+6}}{1-\dfrac{3x(9-3x)}{(x+6)^2}}=\dfrac{9(x+6)}{10x^2-15x+36}>0,\]
so $\theta<90^\circ$ and maximising $k=\sin\theta$ means maximising $\tan\theta$. Setting the derivative of $\dfrac{x+6}{10x^2-15x+36}$ to zero gives $5x^2+60x-63=0$, so
\[x=\dfrac{9\sqrt{15}-30}{5}\approx0.971,\qquad\tan\theta=1+\dfrac{4}{\sqrt{15}}.\]
