For $i\le m$ the condition gives $a_i\ge\left\lceil\dfrac{21-i}{2}\right\rceil\ge\left\lceil\dfrac{21-m}{2}\right\rceil$. So $P_m$ is a sum of $m$ distinct integers that are all at least $\left\lceil\dfrac{21-m}{2}\right\rceil$:
\begin{itemize}
\item $m=2t$: $P_{2t}\ge(11-t)+\cdots+(10+t)=21t$;
\item $m=2t-1$: $P_{2t-1}\ge(11-t)+\cdots+(9+t)=20t-10$.
\end{itemize}
Hence $\displaystyle\sum_{m=0}^{19}P_m\ge\sum_{t=0}^{9}21t+\sum_{t=1}^{10}(20t-10)=945+1000=1945$, and the sum is at most $4200-1945=2255$.

The permutation $10,11,9,12,8,13,\dots,1,20$ (that is, $a_{2t-1}=11-t$ and $a_{2t}=10+t$) satisfies the conditions and attains every bound. So the maximum is $\boxed{2255}$.

