In polar coordinates the first-quadrant region has area
\[\dfrac{\rho^2}{2}\int_0^{\dfrac\pi2}\dfrac{d\theta}{1-\sin\theta\cos\theta}=\dfrac{\rho^2}{2}\cdot\dfrac{4\pi}{3\sqrt3}=\dfrac{2\pi\rho^2}{3\sqrt3}=\dfrac{2\pi}{9}.\]
So $p=\dfrac{2\pi}{9}$, $900p=200\pi\approx628.3$, and the answer is $\boxed{628}$.

