so its mass is
\[8.92\times759.375\pi=6773.625\pi\approx21280\text{ g}\approx\boxed{21.3\text{ kg}}.\]

\emph{Height.} Through $D$ draw the line parallel to $BC$, meeting $AB$ at $E$. Then $DEBC$ is a parallelogram, so $DE=8$, $EB=5$ and $AE=5$. Triangle $ADE$ has $AD=AE=5$ and $DE=8$, so its altitude from $A$ is $\sqrt{25-16}=3$ and $[ADE]=\dfrac12\cdot8\cdot3=12$. Its altitude from $D$ is the height $h$ of the trapezoid: $\dfrac12\cdot5\cdot h=12$ gives $h=\dfrac{24}{5}$. Hence $[BCD]=\dfrac12\cdot CD\cdot h=\dfrac12\cdot5\cdot\dfrac{24}{5}=12$.

\emph{Ratio $BP:PD$.} Extend $AM$ to meet line $DC$ at $N$. Since $AB\parallel CN$ and $BM=MC$, triangles $MAB$ and $MNC$ are congruent, so $CN=AB=10$ and $DN=15$. Triangles $PAB$ and $PND$ are similar (as $AB\parallel DN$), so
\[\dfrac{BP}{PD}=\dfrac{AB}{DN}=\dfrac{10}{15}=\dfrac23,\qquad\dfrac{BP}{BD}=\dfrac25.\]

\emph{Area.} Triangles $BMP$ and $BCD$ share the angle at $B$, so
\[[BMP]=\dfrac{BM}{BC}\cdot\dfrac{BP}{BD}\cdot[BCD]=\dfrac12\cdot\dfrac25\cdot12=\boxed{\dfrac{12}{5}}.\]

\begin{asy}
