Let $O$ be the vertex on the table, let $\mathbf n$ be the upward unit normal of the table, and let $\mathbf u,\mathbf v,\mathbf w$ be the unit vectors along the three edges from $O$; they are pairwise perpendicular. The vertices are $a\mathbf u+b\mathbf v+c\mathbf w$ with $a,b,c\in\{0,1\}$, and their heights are $a(\mathbf n\cdot\mathbf u)+b(\mathbf n\cdot\mathbf v)+c(\mathbf n\cdot\mathbf w)$. As $O$ is the only point of the cube on the table, the vertices $\mathbf u,\mathbf v,\mathbf w$ are above it: $\mathbf n\cdot\mathbf u$, $\mathbf n\cdot\mathbf v$, $\mathbf n\cdot\mathbf w>0$. So the highest point is the opposite vertex and
\[h=\mathbf n\cdot\mathbf u+\mathbf n\cdot\mathbf v+\mathbf n\cdot\mathbf w.\]

