\item[(b)] Let $F_1=1$, $F_2=2$ and $F_{n+1}=F_n+F_{n-1}$ for $n\ge2$ (so the sequence is $1,2,3,5,8,13,\ldots$). Prove that the ratios $r_n=\dfrac{F_{n+1}}{F_n}$ approach $\phi$ as $n\to\infty$.
