question:
A roof-repair company charges a fixed fee of $x$ dollars plus a charge for each hour of work; a final partial hour is charged as a full hour. An hour of work that starts in the daytime (between dawn and dusk) costs $\$23.50$, and an hour that starts at night costs $h$ dollars.
\begin{itemize}
\item On a day with dawn at 8:04 a.m.\ and dusk at 8:32 p.m., a repair from 11:30 a.m.\ to 2:00 p.m.\ costs $\$105.50$.
\item On a day with dawn at 5:36 a.m.\ and dusk at 10:13 p.m., a repair from 6:30 p.m.\ to 11:50 p.m.\ costs $\$191.60$.
\end{itemize}
Today dawn is at 6:49 a.m.\ and dusk at 9:02 p.m. A customer needs a single continuous $7$-hour repair that must finish by midnight. The workers are busy until 2:00 p.m., so the job can start at any time from 2:00 p.m. What is the positive difference between the most and the least the customer could pay?

