Put $t=xy$. A point lies on the graph exactly when $t=\cos t$. We show this equation has exactly one real solution $c$:
\begin{itemize}
\item if $|t|>1$, then $|\cos t|\le1<|t|$;
\item if $-1\le t\le0$, then $\cos t\ge\cos1>0\ge t$;
\item on $[0,1]$, $t$ increases and $\cos t$ decreases, so $t-\cos t$ is strictly increasing, from $-1$ at $t=0$ to $1-\cos1>0$ at $t=1$, and vanishes exactly once.
\end{itemize}
So the graph is $\boxed{\text{the hyperbola }xy=c}$, where $c\approx0.739$ is the unique solution of $\cos c=c$. It has the coordinate axes as asymptotes and branches in the first and third quadrants.

