Put $O$ at the origin with $A=(-R,-R)$, $B=(R,-R)$, $C=(R,R)$, $D=(-R,R)$, and $M=(x,y)$ with $x^2+y^2=R^2$. Then
\[MA^2=(x+R)^2+(y+R)^2=3R^2+2R(x+y),\qquad MC^2=3R^2-2R(x+y),\]
\[MB^2=(x-R)^2+(y+R)^2=3R^2-2R(x-y),\qquad MD^2=3R^2+2R(x-y).\]
Hence
\[MA^2\cdot MC^2+MB^2\cdot MD^2=18R^4-4R^2\left[(x+y)^2+(x-y)^2\right]=18R^4-8R^2\left(x^2+y^2\right)=10R^4.\ \blacksquare\]

