Let $a,b,c,d$ be the numbers of $10$-, $25$-, $50$- and $100$-boxes, each at most $5$. The $10$-, $25$- and $50$-boxes hold $10a+25b+50c=815-100d$ marbles, a number ending in $15$; it is at least $815-500=315$ and at most $50+125+250=425$, so it is $315$ ($d=5$) or $415$ ($d=4$). Also $25b$ must end in $5$, so $b$ is odd.
\begin{itemize}
\item $10a+25b+50c=315$: $b=1$ gives $10a+50c=290$, forcing $c=5$, $a=4$ (total $4+1+5+5=15$); $b=3$ gives $10a+50c=240$, forcing $c=4$, $a=4$ (total $16$); $b=5$ gives $10a+50c=190$, forcing $c=3$, $a=4$ (total $17$).
\item $10a+25b+50c=415$: only $b=5$, $c=5$, $a=4$ works (total $18$).
\end{itemize}
(Here ``forcing'' uses $a\le5$.) The minimum is $\boxed{15}$.

