Let $F$ be the foot of the perpendicular from $B$. The regions are the triangles $ABF$, $BCF$ and $ACD$, where $[ACD]=[ABC]=[ABF]+[BCF]$. Triangles $ABF$ and $BCF$ are similar to triangle $ACB$ (they share its angles), with hypotenuses $AB$ and $BC$, so $\dfrac{[BCF]}{[ABF]}=\left(\dfrac{BC}{AB}\right)^2>1$.

