It remains to show that the reflection in $y=x$ maps $(a,b)$ to $(b,a)$. If $a=b$ the point is on the line. Otherwise the midpoint of $(a,b)$ and $(b,a)$ is $\left(\dfrac{a+b}2,\dfrac{a+b}2\right)$, on the line $y=x$, and the segment joining them has direction $(b-a,a-b)$, perpendicular to the direction $(1,1)$ of the line. So $(b,a)$ is the mirror image of $(a,b)$, and the two graphs are reflections of each other. $\blacksquare$

