The curve consists of the four arcs $y=\pm\sqrt{x^2-1}$, $|x|\ge1$, symmetric about both axes, so it suffices to treat $x\ge1$, $y=\sqrt{x^2-1}$, and the line $y=x$. The vertical gap is
\[x-\sqrt{x^2-1}=\dfrac{1}{x+\sqrt{x^2-1}}<\dfrac1x,\]
which is positive and tends to $0$ as $x\to\infty$. So this arc approaches $y=x$ from below; by symmetry the other arcs approach $y=x$ or $y=-x$. Hence $y=\pm x$ are the asymptotes. $\blacksquare$

