Let $[ABC]=1$. Then $[ABQ]=\dfrac{AQ}{AC}=\dfrac15$ and $[PBQ]=\dfrac{PB}{AB}[ABQ]=\dfrac45\cdot\dfrac15=\dfrac4{25}$.

Since $\dfrac{AP}{AB}=\dfrac{AQ}{AC}$, $PQ\parallel BC$ with $PQ=\dfrac15BC$, so triangles $RPQ$ and $RCB$ are similar with ratio $\dfrac15$, and $\dfrac{QR}{RB}=\dfrac15$, i.e. $\dfrac{QR}{QB}=\dfrac16$. Therefore
\[[PQR]=\dfrac16[PQB]=\dfrac16\cdot\dfrac4{25}=\boxed{\dfrac{2}{75}}.\]

