(The sketch shows three regular pentagons around a vertex: $3\cdot108^\circ=324^\circ$ leaves a $36^\circ$ gap, so they fold into a corner of the dodecahedron.)

The base is a disc of area $\pi r^2$.

Cut the lateral surface along a slant line and unroll it. It becomes a sector of a circle of radius $\ell$ (every point of the base circle is at distance $\ell$ from the apex). Its arc is the base circumference $2\pi r$. A full circle of radius $\ell$ has circumference $2\pi\ell$, so the sector is the fraction $\dfrac{2\pi r}{2\pi\ell}=\dfrac r\ell$ of that circle, and its area is
\[\dfrac r\ell\cdot\pi\ell^2=\pi r\ell.\]
Hence the total surface area is $\boxed{\pi r^2+\pi r\ell}$, which equals $\pi r^2+\pi r\sqrt{r^2+h^2}$ in terms of the height $h$. $\blacksquare$

