The sphere is obtained by rotating the semicircle $y=\sqrt{r^2-x^2}$, $-r\le x\le r$, about the $x$-axis. Here $y'=\dfrac{-x}{\sqrt{r^2-x^2}}$, so for $|x|<r$
\[y\sqrt{1+\left(y'\right)^2}=\sqrt{r^2-x^2}\cdot\sqrt{\dfrac{r^2-x^2+x^2}{r^2-x^2}}=r.\]
Hence
\[S=\int_{-r}^{r}2\pi r\,dx=2\pi r\cdot2r=\boxed{4\pi r^2}.\ \blacksquare\]
(Geometrically: every band of the sphere between two parallel planes at distance $\Delta x$ apart has area $2\pi r\,\Delta x$, the same as the band of the circumscribed cylinder. This is Archimedes' hat-box theorem.)

