Write points as coordinate pairs and add them componentwise. The midpoint of $BC$ is $M_a=\dfrac{B+C}{2}$. The point of the median $AM_a$ that divides it in the ratio $2:1$ from $A$ is
\[A+\dfrac23\left(M_a-A\right)=\dfrac{A+2M_a}{3}=\dfrac{A+B+C}{3}=G.\]
The expression $\dfrac{A+B+C}{3}$ is symmetric in $A$, $B$, $C$, so the same computation for the medians from $B$ and $C$ gives the same point. Hence all three medians pass through $G$, which divides each of them in the ratio $2:1$ from the vertex. $\blacksquare$

