\item $a=3$: $\dfrac1b+\dfrac1c=\dfrac16$, i.e. $(b-6)(c-6)=36$ with $0<b-6\le c-6$. So $b-6\in\{1,2,3,4,6\}$, giving $(b,c)=(7,42),(8,24),(9,18),(10,15),(12,12)$.
\item $a=4$: $(b-4)(c-4)=16$ with $0<b-4\le c-4$, giving $(5,20),(6,12),(8,8)$.
