The Collatz rule replaces an even number $n$ by $\dfrac n2$ and an odd number $n$ by $3n+1$. A student argues: ``If $n$ is odd, then $3n+1$ is even, so the next step halves it. So the sequence keeps going down and eventually reaches $1$.''
