The big square is tiled by $2020^2$ unit squares, all alike, so it suffices to consider one unit square $[0,1]^2$. The lattice point nearest to a point of this square is one of its four corners.

If $d\le\dfrac12$, the points of the unit square within $d$ of a corner form four non-overlapping quarter discs of radius $d$, of total area $\pi d^2$. At $d=\dfrac12$ this is $\dfrac\pi4>\dfrac12$, so the required $d$ is less than $\dfrac12$ and satisfies $\pi d^2=\dfrac12$:
\[d=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\approx0.399.\]
Since $\pi(0.35)^2\approx0.385<0.5<0.636\approx\pi(0.45)^2$, $d$ lies between $0.35$ and $0.45$, so to the nearest tenth $d=\boxed{0.4}$.
