question:
Wheat of four kinds costs Rs $8$, Rs $10$, Rs $16$ and Rs $18$ per kg.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] Show that mixing $x_1,x_2,x_3,x_4$ kg of the four kinds (in this order) gives a mixture worth Rs $15$ per kg exactly when $7x_1+5x_2=x_3+3x_4$. Conclude that the required proportion is not unique.
\item[(b)] Find the proportion if equal quantities of the two cheaper kinds and equal quantities of the two dearer kinds are used.
\end{enumerate}

solution:
Triangles $BTC$ and $BAC$ have the same base $BC$, so the ratio of their areas is the ratio of their heights $TT_1$ and $AA_1$, where $T_1$ and $A_1$ are the feet of the perpendiculars from $T$ and $A$ to line $BC$.

If $AD\perp BC$ then $A_1=T_1=D$ and the heights are $TD$ and $AD$. Otherwise $TT_1\parallel AA_1$, and triangles $DTT_1$ and $DAA_1$ are similar (they share the angle at $D$ and have right angles at $T_1$ and $A_1$). Hence
\[\dfrac{[BTC]}{[ABC]}=\dfrac{TT_1}{AA_1}=\dfrac{TD}{AD}.\qquad\blacksquare\]

