The displaced water has volume $\pi\cdot20^2\cdot1=400\pi$ cm$^3$. By Archimedes' principle, a floating body weighs as much as the water it displaces, so the sphere has mass $400\pi$ g. Its volume is $\dfrac43\pi\cdot15^3=4500\pi$ cm$^3$, so its density is
\[\dfrac{400\pi}{4500\pi}=\dfrac{4}{45}\approx\boxed{0.09\text{ g per cm}^3}.\]
(Check: the submerged cap of depth $h$ has volume $\dfrac{\pi h^2(45-h)}{3}=400\pi$, giving $h\approx5.5$ cm, less than the diameter, so the sphere does float.)

