A fraction in lowest terms terminates exactly when its denominator has no prime factors other than $2$ and $5$ (a terminating decimal is $\dfrac{N}{10^t}$, and the reduced denominator must divide $10^t$).
\begin{itemize}
\item $\dfrac7{31}$ is in lowest terms and $31\nmid10^t$, so it $\boxed{\text{repeats}}$: $\dfrac7{31}=0.\overline{225806451612903}$.
\item $\dfrac7{40}=\dfrac{7\cdot25}{1000}=\boxed{0.175}$ terminates, since $40=2^3\cdot5$.
\end{itemize}

Without the closure there are $\dbinom{13}{5}=1287$ routes. A route uses the closed block exactly when it goes from $(0,0)$ to $(2,4)$, then north to $(2,5)$, then on to $(5,8)$: $\dbinom62\cdot\dbinom63=15\cdot20=300$ routes. So $1287-300=\boxed{987}$ routes remain.

