\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] How many positive divisors of $4^{40}$ are perfect squares?
\item[(b)] Prove that exactly $21$ positive divisors of $4^{40}$ are perfect fourth powers, namely the numbers $4^{2k}$ with $0\le k\le20$.
