draw(arc(B,0.6,-30,0));label("$30^\circ$",B+0.6*dir(-15),dir(-15),fontsize(7pt));
dot(A1);dot(A2);
label("$B$",B,dir(235));label("$A$",A,SE);label("$C$",C,N);label("$A'$",A1,SE);label("$A''$",A2,W);
label("$\sqrt3$",(A+B)/2,N,fontsize(8pt));label("$3$",(A+C)/2,E,fontsize(8pt));label("$2\sqrt3$",B+0.72*(C-B),W,fontsize(8pt));
\end{asy}

The object, its shadow and the sun's ray through the top of the object form a right triangle with the angle $20^\circ$ at the tip of the shadow. If $L$ is the length of the shadow, then $\tan20^\circ=\dfrac2L$, so
\[L=\dfrac{2}{\tan20^\circ}\approx\boxed{5.49\text{ m}}.\]

