An even number divisible by $x$ is a multiple of $L=\operatorname{lcm}(2,x)$, which is $x$ if $x$ is even and $2x$ if $x$ is odd. The number of such multiples up to $100$ is $\left\lfloor\dfrac{100}{L}\right\rfloor=5$, i.e. $\dfrac{100}{6}<L\le20$. Since $L$ is even, $L=18$ or $L=20$.
\begin{itemize}
\item $L=18$: $x=18$, or $x=9$ (odd, with $2x=18$).
\item $L=20$: $x=20$. (An odd $x$ would need $x=10$, which is even.)
\end{itemize}
The sum is $9+18+20=\boxed{47}$.

Let the triangle have side $s$. A rectangle of height $h$ inscribed this way leaves a right triangle with a $60^\circ$ angle at each end of its base, with legs $h$ and $\dfrac{h}{\sqrt3}$. So its base is
\[s-\dfrac{2h}{\sqrt3}.\]
From the first rectangle, $1=s-\dfrac4{\sqrt3}$, so $s=1+\dfrac4{\sqrt3}$. The second rectangle has base
\[w=s-\dfrac2{\sqrt3}=1+\dfrac{2}{\sqrt3}=\dfrac{3+2\sqrt3}{3},\]
so $a+b+c=3+2+3=\boxed{8}$.

