We have $b=2a$, $c=3a$ and $d=4a$, and $252=2^2\cdot3^2\cdot7$.
\begin{itemize}
\item $4a\mid252$ means $a\mid63$.
\item $3a\mid252$ means $a\mid84$.
\end{itemize}
So $a$ divides $\gcd(63,84)=21$, and $a\le21$. Conversely $a=21$ works: $21$, $42$, $63$ and $84$ all divide $252$, since $252=12\cdot21=6\cdot42=4\cdot63=3\cdot84$. The maximum is $\boxed{21}$.

