Put the tied corner at the origin with the house occupying $0\le x\le40$, $0\le y\le30$.
\begin{itemize}
\item Outside the quarter-plane $x,y>0$ the leash runs straight, so the goat reaches three quarters of a disc of radius $55$: area $\dfrac34\pi\cdot55^2=\dfrac{9075\pi}{4}$.
\item Points with $x>0$, $y>0$ outside the house are reached only by wrapping the leash around a corner. Around the corner $(40,0)$, $55-40=15$ feet remain, sweeping a quarter disc of radius $15$: area $\dfrac{225\pi}{4}$.
\item Around the corner $(0,30)$, $55-30=25$ feet remain, sweeping a quarter disc of radius $25$: area $\dfrac{625\pi}{4}$.
\end{itemize}
The two small quarter discs do not overlap: one lies in $x\ge40$, $y\le15$ and the other in $x\le25$, $y\ge30$. The total area is
\[\dfrac{9075\pi+225\pi+625\pi}{4}=\boxed{\dfrac{9925\pi}{4}\ \text{square feet}}\approx7795\text{ square feet}.\]

