Let $x=[CDO]$ and $y=[AOE]$. Triangles with the same height have areas in the ratio of their bases. For the cevian $CF$, both $\dfrac{[ACF]}{[BCF]}$ and $\dfrac{[AOF]}{[BOF]}$ equal $\dfrac{AF}{FB}$, so
\[\dfrac{40+y+84}{30+35+x}=\dfrac{40}{30}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad4x-3y=112.\]
For the cevian $BE$, both $\dfrac{[CBE]}{[ABE]}$ and $\dfrac{[COE]}{[AOE]}$ equal $\dfrac{CE}{EA}$, so
\[\dfrac{84+x+35}{y+40+30}=\dfrac{84}{y}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad xy+35y=5880.\]
Substituting $x=\dfrac{112+3y}{4}$ gives $3y^2+252y-23520=0$, i.e. $y^2+84y-7840=(y-56)(y+140)=0$. So $y=56$ and $x=70$. (Check with the cevian $AD$: $\dfrac{40+30+35}{56+84+70}=\dfrac12=\dfrac{35}{70}$.)

The area is $40+30+35+70+84+56=\boxed{315}$.

