Left: opposite sides. Right: same side, with the reflection $B'$.

Always $|AP-PB|\ge0$, with equality exactly when $PA=PB$, i.e. when $P$ lies on the perpendicular bisector $m$ of $AB$.

The line $m$ is perpendicular to $AB$. If $m$ were parallel to $\ell$, then $AB$ would be perpendicular to $\ell$, which is excluded. So $m$ meets $\ell$ in exactly one point $P$, and there $|AP-PB|=0$.

So in both cases (same side or opposite sides) the answer is the same:
\[\boxed{P=\ell\cap m,\ \text{where }m\text{ is the perpendicular bisector of }AB,\ \text{and the minimum is }0.}\]

\begin{asy}
