Let the legs be $a,b>0$. The area condition is $\dfrac{ab}{2}=1$, so $ab=2$, and the perimeter is
\[P=a+b+\sqrt{a^2+b^2}.\]
By AM-GM, $a+b\ge2\sqrt{ab}=2\sqrt2$. Also $a^2+b^2\ge2ab=4$, so $\sqrt{a^2+b^2}\ge2$. Hence $P\ge2\sqrt2+2$, and both inequalities are equalities when $a=b=\sqrt2$ (an isosceles right triangle with hypotenuse $2$). The smallest perimeter is $\boxed{2+2\sqrt2}$. $\blacksquare$

