\item Equilateral: $(3,3,3)$, $(23,23,23)$, $(29,29,29)$, all valid: $3$ triangles.
\item Two equal sides $(p,p,q)$, $p\ne q$: valid when $2p>q$. This holds for $(23,23,3)$, $(23,23,29)$, $(29,29,3)$, $(29,29,23)$, but fails for $(3,3,23)$ and $(3,3,29)$: $4$ triangles.
\item All different: $(3,23,29)$ fails, since $3+23=26<29$.
