solution:
The volume of the ball is about
\[V=\dfrac43\pi\left(2\text{ m}\right)^3\approx33.5\text{ m}^3.\]
Each metre of string occupies a box of volume $(0.004\text{ m})^2\times1\text{ m}=1.6\times10^{-5}\text{ m}^3$. So
\[L\approx\dfrac{33.5}{1.6\times10^{-5}}\text{ m}\approx2.1\times10^{6}\text{ m},\]
and to the nearest order of magnitude $\boxed{L\approx10^{6}\text{ m}}$ (about $2000$ km).

A square cross-section is used because round strands cannot fill space; the square around each strand includes the gaps. Using the circle of diameter $4$ mm instead (no gaps), $L\approx\dfrac{33.5}{\pi\cdot(0.002)^2}\approx2.7\times10^6$ m, the same order of magnitude.

