\end{asy}

The dashed lines $y=\pm1$ are tangent to all three circles, but they are lines, not circles. (For other configurations such circles can exist: for example, three equal circles that touch each other in pairs have a small circle touching all three externally in the middle gap and a large circle enclosing all three. The statements fail because they claim this for \emph{any} three circles.)

