Let $AB=b$, $CD=c$ and let $h$ be the height of the trapezoid. Use coordinates $A=(0,0)$, $B=(b,0)$, $D=(d,h)$, $C=(d+c,h)$. Then
\[P=\left(\dfrac b2,0\right),\quad Q=\left(\dfrac{b+d}2,\dfrac h2\right),\quad R=\left(d+\dfrac c2,h\right),\quad S=\left(\dfrac{d+c}2,\dfrac h2\right).\]
$Q$ and $S$ lie on the midline $y=\dfrac h2$, with $QS=\dfrac{|b-c|}{2}$, while $P$ (on $y=0$) and $R$ (on $y=h$) lie on opposite sides of it, each at distance $\dfrac h2$. Splitting $PQRS$ along $QS$,
\[[PQRS]=\dfrac12\cdot QS\cdot\dfrac h2+\dfrac12\cdot QS\cdot\dfrac h2=\dfrac{|b-c|\,h}{4}.\]

Triangles $AOB$ and $COD$ are similar with ratio $b:c$, so $O$ divides the height in the ratio $b:c$. Its distance to $AB$ is $\dfrac{bh}{b+c}$ and to $CD$ it is $\dfrac{ch}{b+c}$, hence
\[[AOB]=\dfrac{b^2h}{2(b+c)},\qquad[COD]=\dfrac{c^2h}{2(b+c)},\qquad[COD]-[AOB]=\dfrac{\left(c^2-b^2\right)h}{2(b+c)}=\dfrac{(c-b)h}{2}.\]
This difference is $2020-2019=1$, so $c>b$ and $(c-b)h=2$. Therefore
\[[PQRS]=\dfrac{(c-b)h}{4}=\boxed{\dfrac12}.\]

