question:
Solve the system
\begin{align*}
3x-2y-5z&=392,\\
-x-5y+2z&=25,\\
10x+3y-24z&=-13.
\end{align*}

solution:
If $a=c$, the equation reads $0\cdot x=d-b$.
\begin{itemize}
\item If $b\ne d$, the right side is nonzero, while the left side is $0$ for every $x$: there are no solutions.
\item If $b=d$, both sides are $0$ for every $x$: the two sides of the original equation are the same expression $ax+b$, and \emph{every} real number is a solution.
\end{itemize}
So $a=c$ alone only says the formula fails; it does not decide between ``no solutions'' and ``infinitely many''. That is why $b\ne d$ is also needed.

Factor as a quadratic in $s=\sin x$:
\[s^2+s-6=(s+3)(s-2)=0,\qquad\text{so}\qquad\sin x=-3\quad\text{or}\quad\sin x=2.\]
Both are impossible, since $-1\le\sin x\le1$. So the equation has $\boxed{\text{no solutions}}$.

Indeed, for $-1\le s\le1$ we have $s^2+s-6\le1+1-6=-4<0$, so the left side is always negative.

