Let $r$ be the radius. Since $OB\perp AB$ and $OC\perp AC$, triangles $ABO$ and $ACO$ are right-angled at $B$ and $C$. By the Pythagorean theorem,
\[AB^2=AO^2-OB^2=AO^2-r^2=AO^2-OC^2=AC^2.\]
Hence $AB=AC$, and triangle $ABC$ is isosceles. $\blacksquare$ (Equivalently, the two right triangles are congruent by RHS.)

