\end{asy}

The space diagonal is $s\sqrt3$ and the $12$ edges have total length $12s$. So
\[s\sqrt3\cdot(12s)^2=s^5\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad s^2=144\sqrt3\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad s=12\sqrt[4]3.\]
Since $1.31^2=1.7161$ and $1.32^2=1.7424$, we get $1.31^4\approx2.945<3$ and $1.32^4\approx3.036>3$, so $1.31<\sqrt[4]3<1.32$, so $15.72<s<15.84$. The nearest whole number is $\boxed{16}$, answer $\textbf{(C)}$.

\begin{asy}
