question:
Amy can tile her basement floor alone in $4$ hours, and Beth can tile it alone in $6$ hours. Beth starts tiling alone; after one hour Amy joins her, and they finish the floor together.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] For how many hours in total does Beth tile?
\item[(b)] Amy's mother pays them $\$60$ altogether, split in proportion to the amount of work each did. How much does Amy receive?
\end{enumerate}

solution:
The cake has height $6$ and base $8\times10$. A cube has no icing exactly when it does not touch the top or any of the four side faces. Removing a layer of thickness $1$ from the top and from each side face, but nothing from the bottom, leaves a block of
\[(10-2)\times(8-2)\times(6-1)=8\times6\times5=\boxed{240}\]
cubes without icing.

In the sketch, the iced faces are shaded and the un-iced block is dashed in red.

