Completing the squares,
\[\left(x^2-6x+9\right)+\left(y^2+4y+4\right)=21-2+9+4\qquad\Longrightarrow\qquad(x-3)^2+(y+2)^2=32.\]
So the centre is $(3,-2)$, the radius is $\sqrt{32}$ and the area is $32\pi$. Hence $h+k+z=3-2+32=\boxed{33}$.

