\emph{Top and bottom.} Seen from above, the exposed horizontal faces exactly cover the $6\times6$ top of the bottom cube (each cube covers part of the top of the cube below, and its own top is exposed). So the upward-facing area is $36$, and the bottom face adds another $36$: total $72$.

\emph{Sides.} No cube's vertical faces are covered: a cube sits on top of a larger one and only touches it along its bottom. So every cube contributes all four of its side faces:
\[4\left(1^2+2^2+3^2+4^2+5^2+6^2\right)=4\cdot91=364.\]
(Faces that are flush with faces of the cube below are still exposed; they just lie in the same plane.)

The surface area is $72+364=\boxed{436}$.

