Let the acute angles be $\alpha<\beta$, so $\alpha+\beta=90^\circ$. The smallest angle $\alpha$ is half of $\beta$ or half of $90^\circ$. If $\alpha=45^\circ$, then $\beta=45^\circ=\alpha$, which is not allowed. So $\alpha=\dfrac\beta2$, giving $\alpha=30^\circ$ and $\beta=60^\circ$. In a $30^\circ$--$60^\circ$--$90^\circ$ triangle with hypotenuse $8$, the legs are $4$ and $4\sqrt3$, so the longer leg is $\boxed{4\sqrt3}$.

