\emph{Euler line.} Put the circumcentre $O$ at the origin and write $A,B,C$ for the position vectors of the vertices, so $|A|=|B|=|C|$. Let $H'=A+B+C$. Then
\[\left(H'-A\right)\cdot(B-C)=(B+C)\cdot(B-C)=|B|^2-|C|^2=0,\]
so $H'$ lies on the altitude from $A$; similarly it lies on the other altitudes, so $H'$ is the orthocentre $H$. The centroid is $G=\dfrac{A+B+C}{3}=\dfrac H3$. Back in the original coordinates,
\[G=O+\dfrac{H-O}{3}=(8,1)+\dfrac{(-9,3)}{3}=(5,2).\]
So $ab=5\cdot2=\boxed{10}$.

