solution:
The diagonal of the rectangle is $\sqrt{48^2+20^2}=52$, a diameter, so the radius is $26$ and the centre $O$ is the centre of the rectangle. The side $BD=AE=20$ is a chord at distance $\dfrac{48}{2}=24$ from $O$.

Since $BC=CD$, $C$ lies on the perpendicular bisector of $BD$, which passes through $O$; on the arc $BD$ not containing $A$, $E$, it is at distance $26$ from $O$, hence at distance $26-24=2$ from the chord $BD$. The midpoint of $BD$ is $10$ from $B$, so
\[BC=CD=\sqrt{10^2+2^2}=\sqrt{104}=2\sqrt{26}.\]
The perimeter is
\[AB+BC+CD+DE+EA=48+2\sqrt{26}+2\sqrt{26}+48+20=\boxed{116+4\sqrt{26}}\text{ cm}.\]

