The trip along the highways is $24+10=34$ miles at $60$ mph, which takes $34$ minutes. The straight road is the hypotenuse of a right triangle with legs $24$ and $10$, of length $\sqrt{24^2+10^2}=26$ miles. The speed needed is
\[\dfrac{26}{\dfrac{34}{60}}=\dfrac{1560}{34}=\dfrac{780}{17}\approx45.9\text{ mph},\]
