From each of the $n$ vertices, diagonals go to the $n-3$ vertices other than itself and its two neighbours, and each diagonal is counted from both ends. So an $n$-gon has $\dfrac{n(n-3)}2$ diagonals. Then $n(n-3)=40$, which gives $n=8$ (the other root, $-5$, is not allowed). A $10$-gon has $\dfrac{10\cdot7}2=\boxed{35}$ diagonals.

