Since $n^2+\left(\dfrac{n^2-1}2\right)^2=\dfrac{4n^2+n^4-2n^2+1}{4}=\left(\dfrac{n^2+1}2\right)^2$, the hypotenuse is $\dfrac{n^2+1}2$ (it is also the longest side, as $\dfrac{n^2+1}{2}-n=\dfrac{(n-1)^2}2>0$). Each altitude equals $\dfrac{2\cdot\text{Area}}{\text{side}}$, so the shortest altitude is the one to the longest side, the hypotenuse:
\[h=\dfrac{n\cdot\dfrac{n^2-1}2}{\dfrac{n^2+1}2}=\boxed{\dfrac{n\left(n^2-1\right)}{n^2+1}}.\]

