If the sides are $u$ and $v$ yards, then $n=2(u+v)$. For a fixed sum $s=u+v$, the product $uv$ is largest when $u$ and $v$ are as close as possible, giving $\left\lfloor\dfrac s2\right\rfloor\left\lceil\dfrac s2\right\rceil$. This equals $16$ only for $s=8$ (for $s=7$ it is $12$ and for $s=9$ it is $20$, and it increases with $s$). So $n=16$, and with $n+6=22$ beams, $u+v=11$ and the largest area is $5\cdot6=\boxed{30}$ square yards.

