Let $u=B-E=\dfrac{22}{9}(1,1)$ and $v=D-E=\left(\dfrac{40}{9},\dfrac49\right)=\dfrac49(10,1)$. Then
\[EB=|u|=\dfrac{22\sqrt2}{9},\qquad ED=|v|=\dfrac{4\sqrt{101}}{9},\qquad u\cdot v=\dfrac{22}{9}\cdot\dfrac49\cdot11=\dfrac{968}{81}.\]
By the angle bisector theorem $BF:FD=EB:ED$, so
\[F=\dfrac{ED\cdot B+EB\cdot D}{EB+ED},\qquad F-E=\dfrac{ED\,u+EB\,v}{EB+ED}.\]
Since $|ED\,u|=|EB\,v|=EB\cdot ED$,
\[\left|ED\,u+EB\,v\right|^2=2\,EB\cdot ED\left(EB\cdot ED+u\cdot v\right).\]
Here $EB\cdot ED=\dfrac{88\sqrt{202}}{81}$ and $EB+ED=\dfrac{2\sqrt2}{9}\left(11+\sqrt{202}\right)$, so
\[EF^2=\dfrac{2\cdot\dfrac{88\sqrt{202}}{81}\cdot\dfrac{88\left(\sqrt{202}+11\right)}{81}}{\dfrac{8}{81}\left(11+\sqrt{202}\right)^2}=\dfrac{1936\sqrt{202}}{81\left(11+\sqrt{202}\right)}=\dfrac{1936\sqrt{202}\left(\sqrt{202}-11\right)}{81\cdot81}=\dfrac{1936\left(202-11\sqrt{202}\right)}{6561},\]
using $\left(\sqrt{202}+11\right)\left(\sqrt{202}-11\right)=81$. Hence
\[EF=\boxed{\dfrac{44}{81}\sqrt{202-11\sqrt{202}}}\approx3.67.\]

