Let $g$ be the guess and $a$ the correct answer; $(g,a)$ is uniform on the rectangle $[1,2]\times[1,3]$ of area $2$. He is correct when $|g-a|\le0.1a$, i.e. $0.9a\le g\le1.1a$, i.e.
\[\dfrac{g}{1.1}\le a\le\dfrac{g}{0.9}.\]
For $1\le g\le2$ the upper bound $\dfrac g{0.9}\le\dfrac{20}{9}<3$ stays inside the rectangle, while the lower bound $\dfrac g{1.1}$ is below $1$ when $g<1.1$. So the favourable area is
\[\int_1^{1.1}\left(\dfrac{g}{0.9}-1\right)dg+\int_{1.1}^{2}\left(\dfrac{g}{0.9}-\dfrac{g}{1.1}\right)dg=\dfrac{1}{60}+\dfrac{20}{99}\cdot\dfrac{4-1.21}{2}=\dfrac1{60}+\dfrac{31}{110}=\dfrac{197}{660}.\]

