question:
Determine the sign of each product (angles in radians):
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] $\sin2\cdot\sin3\cdot\sin5$;
\item[(b)] $\cos\left(1+\dfrac{2\pi}{5}\right)\cdot\cos\left(1+\dfrac{4\pi}{5}\right)\cdot\cos\left(1+\dfrac{6\pi}{5}\right)\cdot\cos\left(1+\dfrac{8\pi}{5}\right)$.
\end{enumerate}

solution:
We use $3<\pi<\dfrac{10}3$, so $\dfrac\pi2\approx1.57$, $\pi\approx3.14$, $\dfrac{3\pi}2\approx4.71$, $2\pi\approx6.28$.

\textbf{(a)} $0<2<3<\pi$, so $\sin2>0$ and $\sin3>0$. Also $\pi<5<2\pi$, so $\sin5<0$. The product is \textbf{negative}.

