\end{asy}

\textbf{(b)} Let $\theta_k=1+\dfrac{2k\pi}{5}$. Then:
\begin{itemize}
\item $\dfrac\pi2<\theta_1<\pi$ (as $\dfrac{\pi}{10}<1<\dfrac{3\pi}5$), so $\cos\theta_1<0$;
\item $\pi<\theta_2<\dfrac{3\pi}2$ (as $\dfrac\pi5<1<\dfrac{7\pi}{10}$), so $\cos\theta_2<0$;
\item $\dfrac{3\pi}2<\theta_3<2\pi$ (as $\dfrac{3\pi}{10}<1<\dfrac{4\pi}5$), so $\cos\theta_3>0$;
\item $\dfrac{3\pi}2<\theta_4<2\pi$ (as $1<\dfrac{2\pi}5$), so $\cos\theta_4>0$.
\end{itemize}
Two factors are negative and two positive, so the product is \textbf{positive}.

