We use $3.14<\pi<3.15$, so $\dfrac{20}{7}<\pi<\dfrac{10}{3}$ and $\dfrac83<\pi<3.2$.

\textbf{The angle $10$.} $3\pi<10<\dfrac{7\pi}{2}$ (since $\pi<\dfrac{10}3$ and $\pi>\dfrac{20}7$), so $\pi<10-2\pi<\dfrac{3\pi}2$: the angle $10$ ends in the third quadrant. Hence $\sin10<0$, $\cos10<0$, and $\tan10>0$, $\cot10>0$.

\textbf{The angle $8$.} $\dfrac{5\pi}2<8<3\pi$ (since $\pi<3.2$ and $\pi>\dfrac83$), so $\dfrac\pi2<8-2\pi<\pi$: the second quadrant. Hence $\sin8>0$, $\cos8<0$, $\cot8<0$.

\textbf{The angle $\sqrt5+\sqrt[3]7$.} From $2.2<\sqrt5<2.25$ and $1.9<\sqrt[3]7<1.92$ (compare $2.2^2$, $2.25^2$ with $5$ and $1.9^3$, $1.92^3$ with $7$), $4.1<\sqrt5+\sqrt[3]7<4.17$, which lies between $\pi$ and $\dfrac{3\pi}2>4.71$: the third quadrant, so $\cot\left(\sqrt5+\sqrt[3]7\right)>0$.

