\textbf{The area.} Line $EF$ splits the figure into the two half-discs above it and, below it, the sector $EAD$, the square $ABCD$ and the sector $BAF$, which fill adjacent angles at $A$ without overlapping:
\begin{itemize}
\item two half-discs of radius $1$: $2\cdot\dfrac12\pi\cdot1^2=\pi$;
\item two sectors of radius $2$ and angle $45^\circ$: $2\cdot\dfrac{45}{360}\cdot\pi\cdot2^2=\pi$;
\item the square: $2^2=4$.
\end{itemize}
The total area is $\boxed{\textbf{(A) }4+2\pi}$.

All the points $v_n$ lie on segment $AB$. Let $t_n=\dfrac{Av_n}{AB}$. Then
\[t_1=\dfrac12,\qquad t_2=\dfrac34,\qquad t_n=\dfrac{t_{n-1}+t_{n-2}}{2}\quad(n\ge3).\]
We claim $t_n=\dfrac23+\dfrac13\left(-\dfrac12\right)^n$. It holds for $n=1,2$ ($\dfrac23-\dfrac16=\dfrac12$ and $\dfrac23+\dfrac1{12}=\dfrac34$), and if it holds for $n-1$ and $n-2$, then
\[\dfrac{t_{n-1}+t_{n-2}}{2}=\dfrac23+\dfrac16\left(-\dfrac12\right)^{n-2}\left(-\dfrac12+1\right)=\dfrac23+\dfrac1{12}\cdot4\left(-\dfrac12\right)^{n}=\dfrac23+\dfrac13\left(-\dfrac12\right)^n.\]
So $t_n\to\dfrac23$: the points approach the point $L$ on $AB$ with $AL=\dfrac23AB$.

\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(6cm);
defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));
pair C=(0,0),A=(0,3),B=(4,0);
pair[] v; v[1]=(A+B)/2; v[2]=(v[1]+B)/2;
for(int k=3;k<=6;++k) v[k]=(v[k-1]+v[k-2])/2;
pair L=(A+2*B)/3;
