Each interior angle of the hexagon is $120^\circ$. In triangle $ABC$, $AB=BC$ and $\angle B=120^\circ$, so $\angle BCA=30^\circ$ and
\[\angle ACD=120^\circ-30^\circ=90^\circ.\]
The lines $AC$ and $DE$ meet outside the hexagon at a point $P$ beyond $C$ on ray $AC$ and beyond $D$ on ray $ED$. In triangle $PCD$:
\begin{itemize}
\item $\angle PCD=180^\circ-\angle ACD=90^\circ$;
\item $\angle CDP=180^\circ-\angle CDE=180^\circ-120^\circ=60^\circ$.
\end{itemize}
Hence $\angle CPD=180^\circ-90^\circ-60^\circ=30^\circ$, and since $C$ lies on segment $AP$, $\angle APD=\angle CPD=\boxed{30^\circ}$.

