Five digits means $k^4\le666<k^5$. Since $3^5=243<666$ and $6^4=1296>666$, we have $k=4$ or $k=5$.
\begin{itemize}
\item Base $5$: $666=625+25+15+1=1\cdot5^4+0\cdot5^3+1\cdot5^2+3\cdot5+1$, i.e. $10131_5$. The second and fourth digits are $0$ and $3$.
\item Base $4$: $666=2\cdot256+2\cdot64+1\cdot16+2\cdot4+2$, i.e. $22122_4$. The second and fourth digits are both $2$.
\end{itemize}
So $k=\boxed{4}$.

