From March $21$ of one year to March $21$ of the next there are $365=52\cdot7+1$ days, or $366$ if February $29$ lies in between, that is, if the later year is a leap year. So the day of the week moves forward by $1$, or by $2$ when the later year is a leap year:
\begin{itemize}
\item $2022$: Monday; $2023$: Tuesday;
\item $2024$ is a leap year: Thursday;
\item $2025$: Friday.
\end{itemize}
So the answer is $\boxed{2025}$.

