\item[(b)] Under the usual convention that multiplication and division have the same priority and are carried out from left to right, with $2(2+2)$ read as $2\times(2+2)$, evaluate $8\div2(2+2)$.
\item[(c)] Some people (and some calculators) treat a product written by juxtaposition, such as $2(2+2)$, as a single quantity that is computed before the division. What value do they get? How should the expression be written to avoid the ambiguity?
