The area is base times height: $17\cdot5=\boxed{85}$.

The whole ball has volume $2500\pi$, so its radius $R$ satisfies $\dfrac43\pi R^3=2500\pi$, i.e. $R^3=1875=5^3\cdot15$ and $R=5\sqrt[3]{15}$. Since $2.5^3=15.625>15$, we have $\sqrt[3]{15}<2.5$, so the diameter is
\[2R=10\sqrt[3]{15}<25\text{ cm}\quad(\text{about }24.7\text{ cm}).\]
The rim has diameter $\dfrac{103\pi}{\pi}=103$ cm. So the ball (diameter less than $25$ cm) easily passes through the rim (diameter $103$ cm): $\boxed{\text{yes}}$.

