At the start $y=\sin0=0$, and at the end $y=\sin\dfrac{\pi}{2}=1$. So the $y$-coordinate has increased by $\boxed{1}$. (On $\left[0,\dfrac\pi2\right]$ the function $\sin x$ increases steadily from $0$ to its maximum value $1$.)

