Let the edge lengths be $a$, $b$, $c$ (see the sketch). By Pythagoras' theorem on the three faces,
\[a^2+b^2=19,\qquad b^2+c^2=23,\qquad a^2+c^2=30.\]
Adding, $2\left(a^2+b^2+c^2\right)=72$, so $a^2+b^2+c^2=36$. (Then $a^2=13$, $b^2=6$, $c^2=17$, all positive, so such a box exists.)

A space diagonal is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs are an edge of length $c$ and a diagonal of length $\sqrt{a^2+b^2}$ of the face perpendicular to that edge, so its length is
\[\sqrt{a^2+b^2+c^2}=\sqrt{36}=\boxed{6}.\]

