Eliminating $x$ gives $ab=3(a+b)-2$, i.e.
\[ab-3a-3b+9=7,\qquad (a-3)(b-3)=7.\]
Since $7$ is prime, $(a-3,b-3)$ is one of $(1,7)$, $(7,1)$, $(-1,-7)$, $(-7,-1)$, giving the four points
\[(4,10),\quad(10,4),\quad(2,-4),\quad(-4,2).\]
(Conversely each of these satisfies the conditions with $x=a+b$.) The six distances are
\[|(4,10)(10,4)|=|(2,-4)(-4,2)|=6\sqrt2,\qquad|(4,10)(-4,2)|=|(10,4)(2,-4)|=8\sqrt2,\]
\[|(4,10)(2,-4)|=|(10,4)(-4,2)|=\sqrt{2^2+14^2}=\sqrt{200}=10\sqrt2.\]
The largest distance is $\boxed{10\sqrt2}$.

