The circles are
\[x^2+y^2=25\qquad\text{and}\qquad(x-7)^2+(y-7)^2=25.\]
The distance between the centres is $7\sqrt2<10$, so the circles meet in two points. Both points satisfy both equations, hence also their difference:
\[x^2+y^2-\left(x^2-14x+49+y^2-14y+49\right)=0\iff14x+14y=98\iff x+y=7.\]
This is a line, so it is the line through the two intersection points, i.e. the line of the common chord. (The points are $(3,4)$ and $(4,3)$.) Setting $x=0$ gives the $y$-intercept $\boxed{7}$.

