Both $AB$ and $ED$ are perpendicular to $BC$, so $ED\parallel AB$. Triangles $CDE$ and $CBA$ share the angle at $C$ and have right angles at $D$ and $B$, so they are similar, with ratio $\dfrac{CD}{CB}=\dfrac12$ because $D$ is the midpoint of $BC$. Hence $ED=\dfrac12AB$ (in fact $ED$ is the midline of the triangle and $E$ is the midpoint of $AC$), and
\[\dfrac{AB}{ED}=\boxed{2}.\]

