The inscribed angles $\angle BAC$ and $\angle BDC$ stand on the same arc $BC$, so $\angle PAC=\angle PDB$. Also $\angle APC=\angle DPB$ (vertical angles). Hence triangles $PAC$ and $PDB$ are similar (AA), so
\[\dfrac{PA}{PD}=\dfrac{PC}{PB},\qquad\text{i.e.}\qquad PA\cdot PB=PC\cdot PD.\]

\textbf{(b) $P$ outside.} Name the points so that $A$ lies between $P$ and $B$, and $C$ between $P$ and $D$. Then $A,B,D,C$ lie on $\omega$ in this order, so $ABDC$ is a cyclic quadrilateral.

