Write $[\,\cdot\,]$ for area.

\textbf{Ratio of the bases.} Triangles $AXD$ and $DXC$ have the same height from $D$ to line $AC$, so $\dfrac{AX}{XC}=\dfrac{[AXD]}{[DXC]}=\dfrac34$. Since $AB\parallel CD$, triangles $XAB$ and $XCD$ are similar, so $\dfrac{AB}{CD}=\dfrac{XB}{XD}=\dfrac{AX}{XC}=\dfrac34$. In particular $AB<CD$, so the legs meet at $P$ beyond the shorter base $AB$.

\textbf{The trapezoid.} Triangles $AXB$ and $AXD$ have the same height from $A$ to line $BD$, so $[AXB]=[AXD]\cdot\dfrac{XB}{XD}=3\cdot\dfrac34=\dfrac94$. Also $[BXC]=[ABC]-[AXB]=[ABD]-[AXB]=[AXD]=3$, because triangles $ABC$ and $ABD$ have the same base $AB$ and equal heights. So
\[[ABCD]=3+4+3+\dfrac94=\dfrac{49}{4}.\]

\textbf{Triangle $PAB$.} Since $AB\parallel DC$, triangle $PAB$ is similar to triangle $PDC$ with ratio $\dfrac34$, so $[PDC]=\dfrac{16}{9}[PAB]$ and
\[[ABCD]=[PDC]-[PAB]=\dfrac79[PAB]=\dfrac{49}{4},\qquad [PAB]=\dfrac{63}{4}.\]

Finally, quadrilateral $AXBP$ consists of triangle $PAB$ and triangle $AXB$ on the other side of $AB$:
\[[AXBP]=\dfrac{63}{4}+\dfrac94=\dfrac{72}{4}=\boxed{18}.\]

