Let the radius be $r$; then the height is $h=2r$, and
\[V=\dfrac13\pi r^2h=\dfrac23\pi r^3=486\pi\quad\Longrightarrow\quad r^3=729,\quad r=9,\quad h=18.\]
The slant height is $\ell=\sqrt{r^2+h^2}=\sqrt{81+324}=\sqrt{405}=9\sqrt5$. The total surface area is the base plus the lateral surface:
\[\pi r^2+\pi r\ell=81\pi+81\sqrt5\,\pi=\boxed{81\pi\left(1+\sqrt5\right)}.\]

