Let $t=\tan x$ (so $t\ne0$, and $\tan x$ must be defined). Multiplying by $\sqrt3\,t$,
\[\sqrt3\,t^2-4t+\sqrt3=0\iff\left(\sqrt3\,t-1\right)\left(t-\sqrt3\right)=0,\]
so $\tan x=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt3}$ or $\tan x=\sqrt3$. Since $\tan$ has period $\pi$, in $[0,2\pi)$:
\[\tan x=\dfrac{1}{\sqrt3}\iff x=\dfrac\pi6\text{ or }\dfrac{7\pi}{6},\qquad\tan x=\sqrt3\iff x=\dfrac\pi3\text{ or }\dfrac{4\pi}{3}.\]

