\textbf{(c)} Let the right angle be at $C$, and let the incircle touch $BC$, $CA$, $AB$ at $D$, $E$, $F$. The two tangent segments from a point to a circle are equal, so $AE=AF$, $BD=BF$ and $CD=CE$. In quadrilateral $CDIE$ the angles at $C$, $D$, $E$ are right angles and $ID=IE=r$, so it is a square and $CD=CE=r$. Hence
\[a+b-c=(CD+DB)+(CE+EA)-(BF+FA)=CD+CE=2r,\qquad r=\dfrac{a+b-c}{2}.\ \blacksquare\]

