solution:
The radius is $CM=\dfrac12AC=5\sqrt2$, and $CE=5\sqrt2<10$, so $E$ lies on side $BC$. Diagonal $CA$ makes an angle of $45^\circ$ with side $CB$, so the sector $CME$ of the circle has angle $45^\circ$ and area
\[\dfrac{45}{360}\cdot\pi\left(5\sqrt2\right)^2=\dfrac{25\pi}{4}.\]
The region in question is this sector minus triangle $CFE$ (with $F$ on $CM$ and $E$ on $CB$).

To find $F$, place $A=(0,0)$, $B=(10,0)$, $C=(10,10)$, $D=(0,10)$, so $E=\left(10,10-5\sqrt2\right)$. Line $ED$ is $y=10-\dfrac{\sqrt2}{2}x$ and line $AC$ is $y=x$; they meet where $x\left(1+\dfrac{\sqrt2}2\right)=10$, i.e.
\[x=\dfrac{20}{2+\sqrt2}=10\left(2-\sqrt2\right)=20-10\sqrt2.\]
So $CF=\sqrt2\left(10-\left(20-10\sqrt2\right)\right)=\sqrt2\left(10\sqrt2-10\right)=20-10\sqrt2$, which is less than $CM=5\sqrt2$, so $F$ lies between $M$ and $C$. Then
\[[CFE]=\dfrac12\cdot CF\cdot CE\cdot\sin45^\circ=\dfrac12\left(20-10\sqrt2\right)\left(5\sqrt2\right)\dfrac{\sqrt2}{2}=50-25\sqrt2.\]

