Let there be $a$ ones, $b$ twos and $c$ threes, with $a,b,c\ge1$. Then
\[a+b+c=8,\qquad a+2b+3c=16.\]
Subtracting, $b+2c=8$. With $b\ge1$, $c\ge1$ and $a=8-b-c\ge1$:
