\item $c=1$, $b=6$, $a=1$: $\dfrac{8!}{1!\,6!\,1!}=56$ arrangements;
\item $c=2$, $b=4$, $a=2$: $\dfrac{8!}{2!\,4!\,2!}=420$ arrangements;
\item $c=3$, $b=2$, $a=3$: $\dfrac{8!}{3!\,2!\,3!}=560$ arrangements.
\end{itemize}
($c=4$ would force $b=0$.) The total is $56+420+560=\boxed{1036}$.

