Triangle $DGF$ has a right angle at $D$, with legs $DG=10$ and $DF=6$, so its area is
\[\dfrac12\cdot10\cdot6=\boxed{30\text{ cm}^2}.\]
(Without coordinates: the foot of the perpendicular from $E$ to $AF$ is the midpoint of $AF$, at distance $18$ from $A$; triangles $FDG$ and $FME$, where $M=(0,18)$, are similar with ratio $\dfrac{FD}{FM}=\dfrac{6}{18}$, so $DG=\dfrac13\cdot30=10$.)

