In total he writes $5+90+1350+2040=\boxed{3485}$ digits.

question:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] In how many ways can a positive integer $S$ be written as an ordered sum of $n$ positive integers, that is, how many $n$-tuples $(a_1,\dots,a_n)$ of positive integers have $a_1+\cdots+a_n=S$?
\item[(b)] How many ways are there to write $17$ as a sum of three positive integers if the order of the terms does not matter (that is, how many triples $a\le b\le c$ of positive integers have $a+b+c=17$)? How many for $18$?
