From the first, $t=\dfrac{76+24u}{50}$; substituting into the second gives $125(76+24u)=14400(1-u)$, so $u=\dfrac{49}{174}$ (between $0$ and $1$, so $D$ is on the side $AC$) and $t=\dfrac{48}{29}$. Hence $BD=\dfrac{48}{29}R$ and
\[OD=BD-BO=\dfrac{19}{29}R=\dfrac{19}{29}\cdot\dfrac{35\sqrt6}{6}=\boxed{\dfrac{665\sqrt6}{174}\approx9.36}.\]

Put $A=(0,0)$, $B=(x,0)$, $C=\left(\dfrac x2,\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}x\right)$, with centre $G=\left(\dfrac x2,\dfrac x2\tan30^\circ\right)$. The trisectors from $A$ make angles $20^\circ$ and $40^\circ$ with $AB$; those from $B$ make $20^\circ$ and $40^\circ$ with $BA$; those from $C$ make $20^\circ$ and $40^\circ$ with $CB$.

