\textbf{The area.} The hexagon splits into six triangles with sides $d_1,d_2$ and included angle $60^\circ$:
\[\text{Area}=6\cdot\dfrac12d_1d_2\sin60^\circ=\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{2}d_1d_2.\]
Using $\tan\alpha-\tan\beta=\dfrac{\sin(\alpha-\beta)}{\cos\alpha\cos\beta}$,
\[d_1d_2=\dfrac{x^2}{4}\cdot\dfrac{\sin10^\circ}{\cos30^\circ\cos20^\circ}\cdot\dfrac{\sin10^\circ}{\cos40^\circ\cos30^\circ}=\dfrac{x^2}{3}\cdot\dfrac{\sin^210^\circ}{\cos20^\circ\cos40^\circ}.\]
Finally $\cos20^\circ\cos40^\circ\cos80^\circ=\dfrac18$ (multiply by $8\sin20^\circ$ and use $2\sin\theta\cos\theta=\sin2\theta$ three times: $8\sin20^\circ\cos20^\circ\cos40^\circ\cos80^\circ=\sin160^\circ=\sin20^\circ$), so $\cos20^\circ\cos40^\circ=\dfrac{1}{8\sin10^\circ}$ and
\[\text{Area}=\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{2}\cdot\dfrac{8x^2}{3}\sin^310^\circ=\boxed{4\sqrt3\,x^2\sin^310^\circ}\approx0.03628\,x^2.\]
For $x=12$ the area is $576\sqrt3\sin^310^\circ\approx\boxed{5.22}$.

