The sector $BMA$ (radius $4$, angle $30^\circ$) together with triangle $BAC$ forms the region bounded by $BM$, arc $MA$, $AC$ and $CB$. Removing triangle $BMC$ from it leaves exactly the required region. (Triangle $BMC$ lies inside this region: the ray $BA$ lies inside the right angle $MBC$, so it meets the chord $MC$ at a point $X$; as $X$ is inside $\omega$, $BX<4=BA$, so $X$ is on the segment $BA$. Thus triangle $BMC$ splits into triangle $BMX$, which lies in the sector $BMA$, and triangle $BXC$, which lies in triangle $BAC$.) Hence the area is
\[[\text{sector }BMA]+[BAC]-[BMC]=\dfrac{30}{360}\cdot16\pi+\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}\cdot16-\dfrac12\cdot4\cdot4=\boxed{\dfrac{4\pi}{3}+4\sqrt3-8}\approx3.12.\]

The region is the sector $OCD$ with the triangle $OC'D'$ removed (the segment $C'D'$ lies inside the sector).

\textbf{The sector.} The trisectors make $20^\circ$ angles, so $\angle COD=20^\circ=\dfrac{\pi}{9}$ and the sector has area $\dfrac12r^2\cdot\dfrac\pi9=\dfrac{\pi}{18}r^2$.

