\textbf{Slabs.} The surface area of the box is $2(1\cdot2+2\cdot3+1\cdot3)=22$, so the slabs have volume $22\cdot2=44$.

\textbf{Quarter cylinders.} There are $4$ edges of each length $1$, $2$ and $3$, of total length $4(1+2+3)=24$. Four quarter cylinders of the same length would make a whole cylinder, so these have volume $\dfrac14\pi\cdot2^2\cdot24=24\pi$.

\textbf{Corners.} The $8$ eighth-balls make one whole ball of radius $2$, of volume $\dfrac43\pi\cdot2^3=\dfrac{32\pi}{3}$.

The volume of titanium is
\[44+24\pi+\dfrac{32\pi}{3}=\boxed{44+\dfrac{104\pi}{3}\text{ cubic inches}}\approx152.9\text{ cubic inches}.\]

At an intersection point both equations hold, so
\[x^2+bx+c=x^2+cx+b\iff(b-c)x=b-c.\]
\begin{itemize}
\item If $b\ne c$, then $x=1$ and $y=1+b+c$. The graphs meet in exactly one point, $\boxed{(1,\,1+b+c)}$.
\item If $b=c$, the two equations are the same, so the graphs coincide and every point of the parabola $y=x^2+bx+b$ is an intersection point.
\end{itemize}
For example, with $b=1$ and $c=-1$ the parabolas $y_1=x^2+x-1$ and $y_2=x^2-x+1$ meet only at $(1,1)$, as in the sketch.

