Here ``next year I will be $24$'' means that he turns $24$ during next calendar year, so at the end of the current year he is $23$.

So between the day before yesterday (age $21$) and the last day of the current year (age $23$) he has two birthdays. Two birthdays are a year apart, so the stretch of days from the day after the day before yesterday up to December 31 of the current year must contain the same date twice. Since today is in the current year, the day before yesterday is December 30 or December 31 of last year, or a day of the current year:
\begin{itemize}
\item if it is December 31 of last year or a day of the current year, the stretch lies within the current year and contains each date only once, which is impossible;
\item so the day before yesterday was December 30 of last year, today is January 1, and the stretch from December 31 of last year to December 31 of this year contains December 31 twice: his birthday is December 31.
\end{itemize}
Check: on December 30 he was $21$; he turned $22$ on December 31, is $22$ today (January 1), turns $23$ this December 31 and $24$ next December 31.

So $\boxed{\text{his birthday is December 31, and he spoke on January 1}}$.

By the triangle inequality the third side $c$ satisfies $6<c<24$, so $7\le c\le23$. By Heron's formula with $s=\dfrac{24+c}{2}$,
\[16K^2=(24+c)(c+6)(c-6)(24-c)=\left(576-c^2\right)\left(c^2-36\right).\]
As a function of $u=c^2$, the product $(576-u)(u-36)$ is a downward parabola with vertex at $u=\dfrac{576+36}{2}=306$; it increases for $u<306$ and decreases for $u>306$.
\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Largest area.} The nearest squares to $306$ are $17^2=289$ and $18^2=324$: $(576-289)(289-36)=287\cdot253=72611$ and $(576-324)(324-36)=252\cdot288=72576$. So the maximum is at $c=17$, with $K=\dfrac{\sqrt{72611}}{4}$.
\item \textbf{Smallest area.} The minimum over $7\le c\le23$ is at an end: $c=7$ gives $527\cdot13=6851$ and $c=23$ gives $47\cdot493=23171$. So the minimum is at $c=7$, with $K=\dfrac{\sqrt{6851}}{4}$.
\end{itemize}

\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(7cm);
defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));
pair A=(0,0), B=(9,0);
real x1=(81+225-17^2)/18; pair C1=(x1,sqrt(225-x1^2));
pair A2=(12,0), B2=(21,0);
real x2=(81+225-7^2)/18; pair C2=A2+(x2,sqrt(225-x2^2));
draw(A--B--C1--cycle,blue+linewidth(0.9)); draw(A2--B2--C2--cycle,red+linewidth(0.9));
label("$9$",(A+B)/2,S); label("$15$",(A+C1)/2,W,blue); label("$17$",(B+C1)/2,E,blue);
label("$9$",(A2+B2)/2,S); label("$15$",(A2+C2)/2,NW,red); label("$7$",(B2+C2)/2,SE,red);
label("$c=17$: largest area",(4.5,-2),S,blue+fontsize(8pt)); label("$c=7$: smallest area",(19,-2),S,red+fontsize(8pt));
\end{asy}

The difference is
\[\boxed{\dfrac{\sqrt{72611}-\sqrt{6851}}{4}}\approx67.37-20.69=46.67.\]
($72611=7\cdot11\cdot23\cdot41$ and $6851=13\cdot17\cdot31$ are squarefree, so the roots do not simplify.)

The incentre lies on the internal angle bisectors, so $\angle IAB=\dfrac A2$ and $\angle IBA=\dfrac B2$.

\begin{asy}
