Take radius $1$ and centre $O$. Let the first point be $P$, at distance $t$ from $O$; since $P$ is uniform in the disc, $P(OP\le t)=t^2$, so $t$ has density $2t$ on $[0,1]$. Given $P$, the second point is within distance $1$ of $P$ exactly when it lies in the lens where the unit disc around $O$ overlaps the unit disc around $P$ (shaded).

\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
