draw((0,0)--P,blue); label("$t$",(0,0)--P,N,blue);
draw(P--P+dir(-60),red); label("$1$",P+0.5*dir(-60),E,red);
draw((0,0)--dir(200)); label("$1$",0.5*dir(200),N);
\end{asy}

Two unit circles with centres $t$ apart cut each other in a common chord, and the lens consists of two circular segments with central angle $2\arccos\dfrac t2$. Its area is
\[L(t)=2\arccos\dfrac t2-\dfrac t2\sqrt{4-t^2}.\]
So
\[P(\text{distance}\le1)=\int_0^1\dfrac{L(t)}{\pi}\,2t\,dt=\dfrac1\pi\left(\int_0^14t\arccos\dfrac t2\,dt-\int_0^1t^2\sqrt{4-t^2}\,dt\right).\]
\textbf{First integral.} By parts, with $\dfrac{d}{dt}\arccos\dfrac t2=-\dfrac{1}{\sqrt{4-t^2}}$:
\[\int_0^14t\arccos\dfrac t2\,dt=\Bigl[2t^2\arccos\dfrac t2\Bigr]_0^1+\int_0^1\dfrac{2t^2}{\sqrt{4-t^2}}\,dt=\dfrac{2\pi}{3}+2\int_0^{\dfrac\pi6}4\sin^2u\,du,\]
using $t=2\sin u$. Since $\int_0^{\dfrac\pi6}4\sin^2u\,du=\Bigl[2u-\sin2u\Bigr]_0^{\dfrac\pi6}=\dfrac\pi3-\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}$, the first integral is $\dfrac{4\pi}{3}-\sqrt3$.

\textbf{Second integral.} With $t=2\sin u$,
\[\int_0^1t^2\sqrt{4-t^2}\,dt=\int_0^{\dfrac\pi6}16\sin^2u\cos^2u\,du=\int_0^{\dfrac\pi6}2\left(1-\cos4u\right)du=\dfrac\pi3-\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}.\]
\textbf{Result.}
\[P(\text{distance}\le1)=\dfrac1\pi\left(\dfrac{4\pi}{3}-\sqrt3-\dfrac\pi3+\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}\right)=1-\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{4\pi},\]
so the probability that the segment is longer than the radius is
\[\boxed{\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{4\pi}}\approx0.413.\]

question:
Bob drives $n$ stretches of road of equal length, at constant speeds $v_1,v_2,\dots,v_n$ (all positive) on the successive stretches. Alice says that his average speed for the whole trip is $\dfrac{v_1+v_2+\cdots+v_n}{n}$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] Show that Alice's value is always at least the actual average speed, and find exactly when it is correct.
\item[(b)] Show that if instead each stretch took the same \emph{time}, Alice's method would always be correct.
\end{enumerate}

solution:
Let the angle be $x^\circ$ with $0<x<90$. Its supplement is $180-x$ and its complement is $90-x$, so
\[180-x=10(90-x)\iff9x=720\iff x=\boxed{80}.\]

