The centres of the three circles are pairwise $2$ apart, so they form an equilateral triangle of side $2$. Each circle touches two sides of the big triangle, so its centre lies on the bisector of the corresponding angle, at distance $1$ from both sides; the sides of the small triangle are parallel to those of the big one.

