\textbf{The image line} passes through $(0,-3)$ and $(-8,-4)$, so its slope is $\dfrac{-4+3}{-8-0}=\dfrac18$ and its equation is $y=\dfrac18x-3$, that is,
\[\boxed{x-8y=24}.\]

The prism has $10$ vertices, so $\dbinom{10}{2}=45$ segments join two vertices. Of these, $15$ are edges ($5+5$ around the pentagons and $5$ vertical).

\textbf{Face diagonals.} Each pentagon has $5$ diagonals, and each rectangle has $2$: in total $2\cdot5+5\cdot2=20$.

\textbf{Space diagonals.} The remaining segments: $45-15-20=10$. (Directly: each top vertex is joined by a space diagonal to the $2$ bottom vertices that are not below it or below one of its neighbours, giving $5\cdot2=10$.)

\begin{asy}
