Let the triangle be $ABC$ and let $M$ be the midpoint of $BC$. In an equilateral triangle the median $AM$ is also an altitude and an angle bisector, so the incentre $I$ is the centroid, which lies on $AM$ with $IM=\dfrac13AM$. The incircle touches $BC$ at $M$, so its radius is $r=IM$.

