solution:
The two bisected angles are adjacent along ray $CD$, so
\[\angle GCH=\angle ECD+\angle DCF=\dfrac{15^\circ}{2}+\dfrac{165^\circ}{2}=\dfrac{180^\circ}{2}=90^\circ .\]
(The bisectors of two supplementary adjacent angles are always perpendicular.)

\begin{asy}
