Since $DE\parallel BC$, triangle $ADE$ is similar to triangle $ABC$ with ratio $\dfrac{AE}{AB}=\dfrac13$, so $[ADE]=\dfrac19S$.

Since $EF\parallel AC$, triangle $EBF$ is similar to triangle $ABC$ with ratio $\dfrac{EB}{AB}=\dfrac23$, so $[EBF]=\dfrac49S$.

The quadrilateral $CDEF$ (a parallelogram) is what remains:
\[[CDEF]=S-\dfrac19S-\dfrac49S=\dfrac49S.\]
The ratio is $\boxed{\textbf{(A) }\dfrac49}$.

question:
Let $n$ and $k$ be positive integers. We distribute $n$ identical balls into $k$ distinguishable boxes.
