\item[(b)] Prove that the number of distributions with no restriction is $\dbinom{n+k-1}{k-1}$.
\item[(c)] Let $m\ge1$ with $n\ge mk$. Prove that the number of distributions in which every box gets at least $m$ balls is $\dbinom{n-1-(m-1)k}{k-1}$.
