draw(O--3*dir(0),linewidth(0.9),Arrow(5)); draw(O--3*dir(30),linewidth(0.9),Arrow(5)); draw(O--3*dir(60),linewidth(0.9),Arrow(5));
draw((-2.2,0)--O,dashed+gray(0.5));
draw(arc(O,0.9,0,30),blue); draw(arc(O,1.1,30,60),red);
label("$30^\circ$",1.25*dir(15),blue); label("$30^\circ$",1.45*dir(45),red);
label("$X$",3*dir(0),S); label("$Y$",3*dir(30),SE); label("$Z$",3*dir(60),NW); label("$O$",O,SW);
dot(O);
\end{asy}

(Adjacent congruent angles form a linear pair only when each of them is $90^\circ$.)

The midpoint has the averages of the coordinates of the endpoints:
\[M=\left(\dfrac{7+(-2)}{2},\ \dfrac{8+3}{2}\right)=\boxed{\left(\dfrac52,\ \dfrac{11}{2}\right)}.\]

