The name $\overrightarrow{TP}$ would denote the ray starting at $T$ and going through $P$, which points the other way (towards $D$ and beyond), and $\overrightarrow{PD}$ would denote the ray starting at $P$ and going through $D$; neither is the given ray.

The side $JK$ is horizontal, so $JK=1-(-4)=5$, and likewise $ML=2-(-3)=5$. For $KL$, the horizontal change is $1$ and the vertical change is $4$, so by the distance formula
\[KL=\sqrt{1^2+4^2}=\sqrt{17},\]
and likewise $JM=\sqrt{(-3+4)^2+(-2-2)^2}=\sqrt{17}$.

\begin{asy}
