The perimeter is
\[2\cdot5+2\sqrt{17}=\boxed{10+2\sqrt{17}}\approx\boxed{18.2}.\]

The horizontal and vertical changes are both $2$, so by the distance formula (the Pythagorean theorem in the right triangle shown)
\[FG=\sqrt{(8-6)^2+(9-7)^2}=\sqrt8=\boxed{2\sqrt2}\approx\boxed{2.8}.\]

