solution:
Place the right angle at $C=(0,0)$, with $B=(8,0)$ and $A=(0,6)$, so $AB=10$.

The midpoint of the arc of a semicircle on a segment is obtained from the midpoint of the segment by moving one radius perpendicular to the segment, away from the triangle.
\begin{itemize}
\item On $CB$: midpoint $(4,0)$, radius $4$, move downward: $P=(4,-4)$.
\item On $CA$: midpoint $(0,3)$, radius $3$, move left: $R=(-3,3)$.
\item On $AB$: midpoint $(4,3)$, radius $5$. The line $AB$ is $3x+4y=24$, and $C$ lies on the side where $3x+4y<24$, so the outward unit normal is $\left(\dfrac35,\dfrac45\right)$ and $Q=(4,3)+5\left(\dfrac35,\dfrac45\right)=(7,7)$.
\end{itemize}

\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(7cm);
defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));
pair C=(0,0), B=(8,0), A=(0,6);
pair M1=(4,0), M2=(0,3), M3=(4,3);
