\begin{itemize}
\item $\angle XPA$ and $\angle PQB^*$ are corresponding angles, so $\angle XPA\cong\angle PQB^*$.
\item The rays $QP$, $QY$ are opposite, and so are $QB^*$, $QB$. Hence $\angle PQB^*$ and $\angle YQB$ are vertical angles, and $\angle PQB^*\cong\angle YQB$.
\end{itemize}
Therefore $\angle XPA\cong\angle YQB$. $\blacksquare$

Let $A^*$ be a point of $\ell$ on the other side of $P$ from $A$, so that $A^*$ and $B$ are on opposite sides of $t$.

