Since $d$ is a digit, $2019\le d+2019\le2028$. The product $(a-1)(b-2)(c-3)$ is an integer equal to $\dfrac{2020}{d+2019}$, which is positive and at most $\dfrac{2020}{2019}<2$. So it equals $1$, and then $d+2019=2020$, i.e. $d=1$.

Now $(a-1)(b-2)(c-3)=1$ with integers, so each factor is $\pm1$ with an even number of $-1$'s. Since $a\ge1$, $a-1\ge0$, so $a-1=1$ and $a=2$. Then $(b-2)(c-3)=1$:
\begin{itemize}
\item $b-2=c-3=1$: $b=3$, $c=4$;
\item $b-2=c-3=-1$: $b=1$, $c=2$.
\end{itemize}
The numbers are $\boxed{2341\text{ and }2121}$. Check: $1\cdot1\cdot1\cdot2020=2020$ and $1\cdot(-1)\cdot(-1)\cdot2020=2020$.

A circle is tangent to a line exactly when the distance from its centre to the line equals its radius. Let the centre be $\left(t,\dfrac{t^2}{2}+\dfrac{7}{2}\right)$.

\textbf{The line $x-y+7=0$.} The distance from the centre to this line is
\[\dfrac{\left|t-\dfrac{t^2}{2}-\dfrac{7}{2}+7\right|}{\sqrt2}=\dfrac{|g(t)|}{\sqrt2},\qquad g(t)=-\dfrac{(t-1)^2}{2}+4 .\]
So the circle is tangent exactly when $|g(t)|=k$, where $k=r\sqrt2>0$.
\begin{itemize}
\item $g(t)=-k$ means $(t-1)^2=2(4+k)>0$: always two values of $t$.
\item $g(t)=k$ means $(t-1)^2=2(4-k)$: two values if $k<4$, one value if $k=4$, none if $k>4$.
\end{itemize}
Hence $m=4$, $3$ or $2$, and $m$ is odd only when $k=4$, that is $r=\dfrac{4}{\sqrt2}=2\sqrt2$. Then $m=3$ (centres at $t=1$, $t=5$ and $t=-3$) and $r^2=8$.

\textbf{The line $x-y=0$.} Now the distance is $\dfrac{|h(t)|}{\sqrt2}$ with
\[h(t)=t-\dfrac{t^2}{2}-\dfrac{7}{2}=-\left(\dfrac{(t-1)^2}{2}+3\right)\le-3 .\]
Tangency means $|h(t)|=4$, i.e. $\dfrac{(t-1)^2}{2}+3=4$, so $(t-1)^2=2$ and $t=1\pm\sqrt2$. Thus $n=2$.

