question:
Let $X=\{1,2,3,4,5,6,7\}$ and let $f:X\to X$ be a function with an inverse $f^{-1}$ (that is, $f$ is a bijection). Suppose that
\begin{enumerate}
\item[I.] $f(f(x))+f^{-1}(x)=2x$ for $x=1,2,6$;
\item[II.] $f(3)+f(5)=10$;
\item[III.] $f(6)\ne6$.
