Drop the perpendicular from $A$ to line $BC$, with foot at distance $x$ from $B$ (measured towards $C$), and let $h$ be its length.

\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(6cm);
defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));
pair B=(0,0),C=(10,0); real x=(81-169+100)/20; pair A=(x,sqrt(81-x^2)); pair D=(B+C)/2;
draw(A--B--C--cycle,linewidth(0.9)); draw(A--D,red);
dot(D); label("$A$",A,N);label("$B$",B,SW);label("$C$",C,SE);label("$D$",D,S);
