The diagonals $PR$ and $QS$ of a square bisect each other, so they share a midpoint. Comparing $y$-coordinates,
\[\dfrac{th-uh}{2}=\dfrac{h-h}{2}=0\implies t=u,\]
and then comparing $x$-coordinates,
\[\dfrac{\left(1-\dfrac {t}{2}\right)+\left(-1+\dfrac {u}{2}\right)}{2}=\dfrac{\left(\dfrac{1}{2}-s\right)+\left(-\dfrac{1}{2}+w\right)}{2}\implies w=s.\]
So the square is symmetric: $P=\left(1-\dfrac {t}{2},\,th\right)$, $R=\left(-1+\dfrac {t}{2},\,-th\right)$, $Q=\left(\dfrac{1}{2}-s,\,h\right)$, $S=\left(-\dfrac{1}{2}+s,\,-h\right)$.

Now $QS=\left(-1+2s,\,-2h\right)$ and $PR=\left(-2+t,\,-2th\right)$. In a square the diagonals are perpendicular and equally long, so as vectors $PR$ is a quarter turn of $QS$, i.e. $PR$ is either $\left(2h,\,-1+2s\right)$ or $\left(-2h,\,1-2s\right)$ (the two quarter turns of $QS$).

Case 1: $-2+t=2h=\sqrt3$ gives $t=2+\sqrt3>1$, impossible.

Case 2: $-2+t=-2h=-\sqrt3$ gives $t=2-\sqrt3\in[0,1]$, and $-2th=1-2s$ gives
\[s=\dfrac{1+2th}{2}=\dfrac{1+(2-\sqrt3)\sqrt3}{2}=\dfrac{1+2\sqrt3-3}{2}=\sqrt3-1\in[0,1].\]
Both values are admissible, so the square is unique, with
\[P=\left(\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2},\,\sqrt3-\dfrac{3}{2}\right),\qquad Q=\left(\dfrac{3}{2}-\sqrt3,\,\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}\right).\]
Therefore
\[PQ^2=\left(\dfrac{3\sqrt3}{2}-\dfrac{3}{2}\right)^2+\left(\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}-\dfrac{3}{2}\right)^2=\dfrac{9}{4}\left(4-2\sqrt3\right)+\dfrac{1}{4}\left(12-6\sqrt3\right)=12-6\sqrt3.\]
Since $12-6\sqrt3=(3-\sqrt3)^2$ and $3-\sqrt3>0$, the side length is
\[\boxed{3-\sqrt3}.\]

question:
Quadrilateral $ABCD$ is a square. Point $E$ lies outside the square, on the opposite side of line $AD$ from $B$ and $C$, and $\overline{AE}\perp\overline{ED}$ with $AE=8$ and $DE=6$. What is the area of pentagon $AEDCB$?


\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(5cm);
defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));
pair A=(0,0), B=(4,0), C=(4,4), D=(0,4);
pair Ep=(-1.92,2.56);
draw(A--B--C--D--cycle, linewidth(0.9));
draw(A--Ep--D, linewidth(0.9));
pair u1=(0.6,-0.8), u2=(0.8,0.6);
draw(Ep+0.3*u1--Ep+0.3*(u1+u2)--Ep+0.3*u2, linewidth(0.7));
