Let \(K\) be the area, and let \(a,b,c\) be the side lengths to which the altitudes \(21,28,60\) are drawn. Since the area is one half of a side times the corresponding altitude,
\[
a=\dfrac{2K}{21},\qquad b=\dfrac{2K}{28},\qquad c=\dfrac{2K}{60}.
\]
Hence
\[
210=a+b+c=2K\left(\dfrac{1}{21}+\dfrac{1}{28}+\dfrac{1}{60}\right).
\]
Now
\[
\dfrac{1}{21}+\dfrac{1}{28}+\dfrac{1}{60}
=\dfrac{20+15+7}{420}
=\dfrac{1}{10}.
\]
Thus \(210=2K\cdot \dfrac{1}{10}=\dfrac{K}{5}\), so \(K=1050\). Therefore
\[
a=\dfrac{2100}{21}=100,\qquad b=\dfrac{2100}{28}=75,\qquad c=\dfrac{2100}{60}=35.
\]

