Complete the square:
\[
x^2-4x+y^2+6y\le12
\]
becomes
\[
(x-2)^2-4+(y+3)^2-9\le12,
\]
so
\[
(x-2)^2+(y+3)^2\le25.
\]
Thus we count lattice points in a circle of radius \(5\) centered at \((2,-3)\). Let \(d=x-2\). For each possible horizontal offset \(d\), the number of possible vertical offsets is the number of integers in the interval of radius \(\sqrt{25-d^2}\):
\[
\begin{array}{c|cccccc}
d&0&\pm1&\pm2&\pm3&\pm4&\pm5\\ \hline
\#&11&9&9&9&7&1
\end{array}
\]
Therefore the total number of lattice points is
\[
11+2(9+9+9+7+1)=11+70=81.
\]

