A direction vector with slope \(-\dfrac{3}{4}\) is \((4,-3)\). Its length is
\[
\sqrt{4^2+(-3)^2}=5.
\]
So a unit vector along this line is
\[
\left(\dfrac{4}{5},-\dfrac{3}{5}\right).
\]
A point at distance \(12\) from the origin along this line is therefore
\[
\pm 12\left(\dfrac{4}{5},-\dfrac{3}{5}\right)
=\pm\left(\dfrac{48}{5},-\dfrac{36}{5}\right).
\]

