solution:
Let $x=OX$ and $y=OY$. Because $M$ is the midpoint of $OX$ and $N$ is the midpoint of $OY$,
\[OM=\dfrac{x}{2},\qquad ON=\dfrac{y}{2},\]
and since $M$ lies on $OX$ and $N$ lies on $OY$, the angles $\angle XON$ and $\angle YOM$ are both the right angle at $O$.
