Long division in base $5$ works digit by digit. Keep a running remainder $r$, starting at $r=0$. For each digit $d$ of the dividend from left to right, form $rb+d$, write the largest quotient digit $q$ with $qD\le rb+d$, and replace $r$ by $rb+d-qD$.
