A textbook says: ``A function has an inverse if and only if there is no horizontal line that passes through two or more points on the graph of the function.'' A student objects that every function has an inverse relation, so the statement should be: ``A function has an inverse that is also a function if and only if no horizontal line meets its graph more than once.''

