Let $h$ be the altitude from $B$ to $AC$. The centroid $G$ lies one third of the way from $M$ to $B$ along the median $BM$, so its distance to $AC$ is $\dfrac{h}{3}$. Since $AM=\dfrac{AC}{2}$,
