The diagram is only schematic; the diameter ratio is \(80:1\), so the straw is drawn larger than to scale.
The gap is \(40\) m \(=4000\) cm. Since
\[
266\cdot15=3990<4000<4005=267\cdot15,
\]
each of the \(6400\) parallel straw lines needs \(267\) straws joined end to end. Hence the fewest number of straws is
\[
6400\cdot267=\boxed{1{,}708{,}800}.
\]

Let \(O\) be the center of the circle. Since \(AB=AC\), the point \(A\) is the midpoint of the arc \(BC\) on which it lies. The angle \(\angle A\) is half the measure of the arc \(BC\) not containing \(A\), so there are two cases.

\textbf{Case 1: \(A\) lies on the major arc \(BC\).} Then the arc \(BC\) not containing \(A\) is the minor arc, of measure \(102^\circ\). Hence
\[
\angle A=\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot102^\circ=51^\circ,
\]
and
\[
\angle B=\angle C=\dfrac{180^\circ-51^\circ}{2}=64.5^\circ.
\]

\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
