In triangle $ABC$,
\[\angle ABC=180^\circ-\angle BAC-\angle ACB=180^\circ-70^\circ-40^\circ=70^\circ=\angle BAC .\]
So triangle $ABC$ is isosceles, and the sides opposite the equal angles are equal: the side opposite $\angle ABC$ is $AC$ and the side opposite $\angle BAC$ is $BC$. Hence
\[AC=BC=\boxed{6}.\]
