Recall that a quadrilateral $PQRS$ (vertices in this order) is a parallelogram exactly when $\overrightarrow{PQ}=\overrightarrow{SR}$, i.e.\ $Q-P=R-S$, which is equivalent to
\[P+R=Q+S .\tag{1}\]
In words: the sums of opposite vertices are equal, i.e.\ the two diagonals $PR$ and $QS$ have the same midpoint.

