Since $\dfrac{\pi}{12}=15^\circ$, the number is $s_{1997}$, where $s_n=(2+\sqrt3)^n+(2-\sqrt3)^n$.

\textbf{A recurrence.} The numbers $2\pm\sqrt3$ are the roots of $t^2=4t-1$, so $s_{n+1}=4s_n-s_{n-1}$, with $s_0=2$ and $s_1=4$. In particular every $s_n$ is an integer. Modulo $9$:
\[s_0,s_1,s_2,\dots\equiv2,4,5,7,5,4,\ 2,4,5,7,5,4,\ \dots\]
(e.g.\ $s_2=14\equiv5$, $s_3=52\equiv7$, $s_4=194\equiv5$, $s_5=724\equiv4$, $s_6=2702\equiv2$, $s_7\equiv4$). Since two consecutive terms repeat, the residues are periodic with period $6$. As $1997=6\cdot332+5$, $s_{1997}\equiv s_5\equiv4\pmod9$.

