Let $H$ be the foot of the perpendicular from $Z$ to line $XY$. If $\angle XYZ$ were obtuse, then $X$ and $H$ would lie on opposite sides of $Y$, so $XZ>ZY=17$, contradicting $XZ=10$. Hence $\angle XYZ$ is acute, $H$ lies on ray $YX$, and
\[ZH=17\cdot\dfrac{8}{17}=8,\qquad YH=\sqrt{17^2-8^2}=15 .\]
Since $XZ=10$, the point $X$ satisfies $XH=\sqrt{10^2-8^2}=6$, so $X$ is one of the two points $X_1,X_2$ on ray $YH$ with $YX_1=15-6=9$ and $YX_2=15+6=21$.

