The smaller piece is the circular segment, with area
\[
\dfrac{\theta}{2}\cdot6^2-\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot6^2\sin\theta=18(\theta-\sin\theta).
\]
The function $\theta-\sin\theta$ is strictly increasing (its derivative $1-\cos\theta$ is positive on $(0,\pi]$), so the equation $18(\theta-\sin\theta)=12\pi-9\sqrt3$ has at most one solution, and $\theta=\dfrac{2\pi}{3}$ works: $18\cdot\dfrac{2\pi}{3}-18\cdot\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}=12\pi-9\sqrt3$.

The radius $OT$ of circle $B$ is perpendicular to the chord and bisects $\angle POQ$, so
\[
OT=6\cos\dfrac{\theta}{2}=6\cos60^\circ=\boxed{3}.
\]

The radius is $6$ yards.
