As the chord turns about $P$, its length varies continuously between $16$ and $20$. Each length strictly between $16$ and $20$ is achieved by exactly two chords, symmetric about line $OP$, while lengths $16$ and $20$ are each achieved by exactly one chord. The integer lengths are $16,17,18,19,20$, giving
