Put $A=(0,0)$, $B=(L,0)$, $C=(L,45)$, $D=(0,45)$ with $L=AB$. A circle of radius $10$ inside the rectangle tangent to $AB$ and $BC$ sits in corner $B$ and has centre $O_1=(L-10,10)$. The circle of radius $15$ in corner $D$ has centre $O_2=(15,30)$.

Two circles lying side by side inside the rectangle are tangent externally, so $O_1O_2=10+15=25$ (internal tangency would need $O_1O_2=5$, which is impossible because the vertical distance alone is $20$). Hence
\[
(L-25)^2+20^2=25^2\quad\Longrightarrow\quad (L-25)^2=225\quad\Longrightarrow\quad L=40\ \text{or}\ L=10 .
\]

