Since $BC$ is a diameter, the angles inscribed in the semicircle are right angles: $\angle BDC=90^\circ$ and $\angle BEC=90^\circ$. So $BD\perp AC$ and $CE\perp AB$; the diagonals $BD$ and $CE$ of $BCDE$ are two altitudes of $\triangle ABC$, and $F$ is its orthocenter.

The base angles are $\angle CAB=\angle CBA=\dfrac{180^\circ-40^\circ}{2}=70^\circ$. In quadrilateral $AEFD$ the angles at $E$ and $D$ are right angles, so
