draw(A--B--C--cycle);draw(B--D);
draw((0,1.8)--(1.8,1.8)--(1.8,0));
dot(D);
label("$A$",A,SW);label("$B$",B,SE);label("$C$",C,N);label("$D$",D,W);
label("$15$",(A+B)/2,S);label("$39$",(B+C)/2,NE);label("$x$",(A+D)/2,W);label("$36-x$",(D+C)/2,W);
label("\mbox{}",(min(currentpicture,user=true)+max(currentpicture,user=true))/2,black); // keeps the text after the figure black when LaTeX typesets the labels inline
\end{asy}

Triangle $ABD$ has a right angle at $A$, so
\[
15^2+x^2=(45-x)^2\iff 225=2025-90x\iff x=20 .
\]
Hence $AD=\boxed{20}$. (Check: $BD=\sqrt{225+400}=25$ and $CD+9=16+9=25$.)

The parabola meets the $x$-axis at $x=-1$ and $x=5$, so $A=(-1,0)$ and $D=(5,0)$ (with $A$ to the left). The height is $2$ and $\angle BAD=60^\circ$, so $B$ is $2$ above the axis and $\dfrac{2}{\tan60^\circ}=\dfrac{2}{\sqrt3}$ to the right of $A$:
\[
B=\left(-1+\dfrac{2}{\sqrt3},\ 2\right).
\]
By symmetry about the axis $x=2$ of the parabola, $C=\left(5-\dfrac{2}{\sqrt3},2\right)$ is then also on the parabola.

