The cube has surface area $6$. Each face of the tetrahedron is an equilateral triangle of side $\sqrt2$ and area $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}\cdot2=\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}$, so the tetrahedron has surface area $2\sqrt3$. The ratio is
\[
