In the equilateral triangle, $AM=\dfrac{\sqrt3}{2}\cdot6=3\sqrt3$. In right triangle $CMB$, $CM=\sqrt{5^2-3^2}=4$. Since $ABCD$ is convex, $A$ and $C$ are on opposite sides of $BD$, so
