The frame is the set of points outside the triangle at distance at most $2$ cm from it. It consists of
\begin{itemize}
\item three rectangles of width $2$ cm along the sides, with total area $2\cdot(\text{perimeter})$, and
\item three circular sectors of radius $2$ cm at the corners. The angle of the sector at a vertex is $180^\circ$ minus the interior angle, so the three sector angles add up to $3\cdot180^\circ-180^\circ=360^\circ$: together they form one full circle of radius $2$.
\end{itemize}

