Join the centre of the hexagon to its six vertices. This divides the hexagon into $6$ equilateral triangles of side $20$, each of area $\dfrac{\sqrt3}{4}\cdot20^2=100\sqrt3$. Assign each student to one triangle containing him (a student on a shared edge is assigned to just one of the triangles).

