We use directed angles between lines, taken modulo $180^\circ$: $\measuredangle(\ell,m)$ is the angle through which line $\ell$ must be turned counterclockwise to become parallel to $m$, and $\measuredangle UVW=\measuredangle(VU,VW)$. With this convention, four points $U,V,W,Z$ (no three collinear) are concyclic if and only if $\measuredangle UZW=\measuredangle UVW$, whatever the order of the points on the circle; and for any triangle $\measuredangle CAB+\measuredangle ABC+\measuredangle BCA=0$.

