The circle is $x^2+y^2=16$ and the translated line is $y=x-1$.

\textbf{Chord lengths.} The distance from the origin to $14x+3y=7$ is $\dfrac{7}{\sqrt{205}}$, so
\[
CD=2\sqrt{16-\dfrac{49}{205}}=2\sqrt{\dfrac{3231}{205}}=\dfrac{6\sqrt{359}}{\sqrt{205}} .
\]
The distance from the origin to $x-y-1=0$ is $\dfrac{1}{\sqrt2}$, so $EF=2\sqrt{16-\dfrac{1}{2}}=\sqrt{62}$.

\textbf{The chords cross.} The two lines meet where $14x+3(x-1)=7$, i.e. at $\left(\dfrac{10}{17},-\dfrac{7}{17}\right)$, which is inside the circle. So $CD$ and $EF$ are the diagonals of the convex quadrilateral $CEDF$ (shaded).

