\textbf{Area.} A convex quadrilateral with diagonals $d_1,d_2$ meeting at angle $\theta$ has area $\dfrac{1}{2}d_1d_2\sin\theta$. Direction vectors of the two lines are $(3,-14)$ and $(1,1)$, so
\[
\sin\theta=\dfrac{|3\cdot1-(-14)\cdot1|}{\sqrt{205}\,\sqrt2}=\dfrac{17}{\sqrt{410}} .
\]
Therefore
\[
[CEDF]=\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot\dfrac{6\sqrt{359}}{\sqrt{205}}\cdot\sqrt{62}\cdot\dfrac{17}{\sqrt{410}}=\dfrac{51\sqrt{359\cdot62}}{\sqrt{205\cdot410}}=\dfrac{51\sqrt{22258}}{205\sqrt2}=\boxed{\dfrac{51\sqrt{11129}}{205}}\approx26.24 .
\]

