An inscribed angle is half the arc it subtends, the arc lying on the opposite side from the vertex.

$\angle ABC=130^\circ$ subtends the arc $AC$ not containing $B$, so that arc is $260^\circ$, and the arc $A\to B\to C$ is $360^\circ-260^\circ=100^\circ$. Likewise $\angle CDE=110^\circ$ gives arc $C\to D\to E$ equal to $360^\circ-220^\circ=140^\circ$. The remaining arc from $E$ back to $A$ (not containing $B,C,D$) is
\[
360^\circ-100^\circ-140^\circ=120^\circ .
\]

