Let the sides be $a=AB$, $b=BC$, $c=CD$, $d=DE$, $e=EF$, $f=FA$. Every interior angle is $120^\circ$, so extending sides $AB$, $CD$, $EF$ cuts off three equilateral triangles (on sides $b$, $d$, $f$) and gives a big equilateral triangle.

