Hence the minimum is
\[
H'G=\sqrt{(4-(-6))^2+(-1-9)^2}=\sqrt{200}=\boxed{10\sqrt2},
\]
attained with the stop at $R=(3,0)$, where $H'G$ crosses the river.

Cutting off a corner tetrahedron of edge $6$ removes a corner triangle of side $6$ from each of the three faces meeting at that vertex, and exposes a new equilateral triangle of side $6$. So each original face, an equilateral triangle of side $18$, becomes a regular hexagon of side $6$:

\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
