Choosing a unit cube uniformly at random and then a uniformly random one of its $6$ faces is the same as choosing one of the $216\cdot6=1296$ unit faces uniformly at random, because every unit face is equally likely: its probability is $\dfrac{1}{216}\cdot\dfrac{1}{6}$.

