\]

\textbf{$K=\dfrac{abc}{4R}$.} First we show $c=2R\sin C$. Let $O$ be the circumcentre and $M$ the midpoint of $AB$; since $OA=OB=R$, triangle $OAB$ is isosceles and $OM\perp AB$.

