Externally tangent equal circles have centres $2r$ apart, so $PQR$ is an equilateral triangle of side $2r$. Its side $QR$ is parallel to $BC$ (both $Q$ and $R$ are at distance $r$ from $BC$), and
\[
BC=\sqrt3\,r+2r+\sqrt3\,r=(2+2\sqrt3)r .
\]
The two triangles are similar with ratio $\dfrac{BC}{QR}=\dfrac{(2+2\sqrt3)r}{2r}=1+\sqrt3$, so
\[
\dfrac{[ABC]}{[PQR]}=(1+\sqrt3)^2=4+2\sqrt3 .
\]
Thus $a=4$, $b=2$ and $a+b=\boxed{6}$.

The units digit must be $0$, $2$ or $4$, and the leading digit cannot be $0$.
\begin{itemize}
\item Units digit $0$: the other five digits can be arranged in $5!=120$ ways.
\item Units digit $2$ or $4$ ($2$ choices): the leading digit is one of the $4$ remaining nonzero digits, and the other $4$ digits fill the middle in $4!=24$ ways: $2\cdot4\cdot24=192$.
\end{itemize}
The total is $120+192=\boxed{312}$.

