The volume is $3\cdot4\cdot12=\boxed{144}$.

Let the ant start at $P$ and go to the opposite vertex $Q$. No single face contains both $P$ and $Q$, so any path on the surface crosses from a face containing $P$ to a face containing $Q$, passing through a common edge of the two faces. Unfold those two adjacent faces into a $1\times2$ rectangle; the path becomes a path in the rectangle from one corner to the opposite corner, which is at least as long as the straight segment.

