The blocks have disjoint interiors, so the total is $36\cdot4=\boxed{144}$. (This agrees with the general count $m+n-\gcd(m,n)=72+108-36$.)

Let $O$ be the centre and $r=3\sqrt2$ the radius. The tangent segments from $A$ make equal angles with $AO$, so $\angle OAK=\dfrac{1}{2}\angle KAM$ and, in the right triangle $OKA$,
\[
\sin\angle OAK=\dfrac{r}{AO}=\sqrt{\dfrac{2}{5}}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad AO^2=\dfrac{5}{2}r^2=\dfrac{5}{2}\cdot18=45 .
\]

