By the symmetry of the fold, $\angle PCA=\angle DCA$, and $\angle DCA=\angle CAB$ since $DC\parallel AB$. So $\angle PCA=\angle PAC$ and triangle $APC$ is isosceles with $PA=PC$. Let $PA=PC=t$; then $PB=16-t$ and the right triangle $PBC$ gives
\[
(16-t)^2+12^2=t^2\quad\Longrightarrow\quad 400=32t\quad\Longrightarrow\quad t=12.5 .
\]
The overlap triangle $APC$ has base $AP=12.5$ on $AB$ and height $BC=12$, so its area is $\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot12.5\cdot12=\boxed{75}$.

