So the monkey can fly in $\dfrac{7}{8}$ of a ball of radius $12$:
\[
\dfrac{7}{8}\cdot\dfrac{4}{3}\pi\cdot12^3=\dfrac{7}{8}\cdot2304\pi=\boxed{2016\pi},
\]
answer \textbf{(c)}.

The volume of a sphere is $\dfrac{4}{3}\pi r^3$, so using all the snow means
\[
r_1^3+r_2^3+r_3^3=6^3=216,\qquad r_1\ge r_2\ge r_3\ge1 .
\]
Here $r_1\le5$ (with $r_1=6$ nothing would be left).
\begin{itemize}
\item $r_1=5$: $r_2^3+r_3^3=91$. With $r_2=4$ we get $r_3^3=27$, $r_3=3$. With $r_2\le3$ the sum is at most $54<91$.
\item $r_1=4$: $r_2^3+r_3^3=152>2\cdot4^3$, impossible.
\item $r_1\le3$: the total is at most $3\cdot27=81<216$.
\end{itemize}
So $\boxed{\text{yes}}$: the only way is radii $5$, $4$ and $3$ inches, because $3^3+4^3+5^3=6^3$.

