(d) The graph is the part of the vertical strip $0\le x\le2$ strictly below the line $y=x+4$ (dashed top edge, not included), extending downward without end. It is not a function: $x=0$ is paired with $y=0$ and $y=1$, for example. Every point has $y<x+4\le6$, and every $y<6$ occurs (with $x=2$), so the range is $\boxed{y<6}$.

