From the ratios,
\[
AX=\dfrac{3}{4}AB,\ XB=\dfrac{1}{4}AB,\qquad BY=\dfrac{4}{5}BC,\ YC=\dfrac{1}{5}BC,\qquad CZ=\dfrac{5}{6}CA,\ ZA=\dfrac{1}{6}CA .
\]
Two triangles with a common angle have areas in the ratio of the products of the sides enclosing that angle (area $=\dfrac{1}{2}\cdot$ side $\cdot$ side $\cdot\sin$ angle). Hence
\[
\dfrac{[AXZ]}{[ABC]}=\dfrac{AX\cdot AZ}{AB\cdot AC}=\dfrac{3}{4}\cdot\dfrac{1}{6}=\dfrac{1}{8},\quad
\dfrac{[BYX]}{[ABC]}=\dfrac{BX\cdot BY}{BA\cdot BC}=\dfrac{1}{4}\cdot\dfrac{4}{5}=\dfrac{1}{5},\quad
\dfrac{[CZY]}{[ABC]}=\dfrac{CY\cdot CZ}{CB\cdot CA}=\dfrac{1}{5}\cdot\dfrac{5}{6}=\dfrac{1}{6} .
\]
So the three corner triangles have areas $30$, $48$ and $40$:

