So $\boxed{6}$ is the least number of points that forces three collinear points or a right triangle.

Count pairs (face, red edge on that face). Each of the $6$ faces has $2$ red edges, giving $12$ pairs. Each edge lies on exactly $2$ faces, so each red edge is counted twice. If $R$ edges are red, then $2R=12$, so $R=\boxed{6}$.

Such a colouring exists. Put the cube at $\{0,1\}^3$ and colour the six edges of the closed path
