(0,0,0)\to(1,0,0)\to(1,1,0)\to(1,1,1)\to(0,1,1)\to(0,0,1)\to(0,0,0),
\]
shown in red below. The face $z=0$ contains the first two of these edges, $x=1$ the second and third, $y=1$ the third and fourth, $z=1$ the fourth and fifth, $x=0$ the fifth and sixth, and $y=0$ the sixth and first; so every face has exactly $2$ red edges.

