The angle bisectors of a triangle are concurrent, so $I$ is the incentre and $AI$ bisects $\angle A$. Here $\angle A=180^\circ-63^\circ-51^\circ=66^\circ$, so $\angle IAB=33^\circ$ and $\angle IBA=\dfrac{63^\circ}{2}=31.5^\circ$. In triangle $AIB$,
\[
\angle AIB=180^\circ-33^\circ-31.5^\circ=\boxed{\dfrac{231}{2}^\circ=115.5^\circ} .
\]

