Take side length $2$: $A=(0,0)$, $B=(2,0)$, $C=(2,2)$, $D=(0,2)$, $E=(1,0)$. The circle is $x^2+y^2=4$, and the points of segment $EC$ are $(1+t,2t)$ with $0\le t\le1$, where $t$ is the fraction of the way from $E$ to $C$. Substituting,
\[
(1+t)^2+4t^2=4\iff5t^2+2t-3=0\iff(5t-3)(t+1)=0,
\]
so $t=\dfrac{3}{5}$ and $F=\left(\dfrac{8}{5},\dfrac{6}{5}\right)$. Since $F$ is $\dfrac{3}{5}$ of the way from $E$ to $C$,
\[
\dfrac{EF}{FC}=\dfrac{\dfrac{3}{5}}{\dfrac{2}{5}}=\boxed{\dfrac{3}{2}}.
\]

\begin{asy}
