\item[(b)] How many nonempty subsets of $\{-2,-1,0,1,2\}$ have elements with sum $0$?
\end{enumerate}

solution:
The inequality is unchanged when $x$ is replaced by $-x$ or $y$ by $-y$, so the region is symmetric about both axes. In the first quadrant it is $x+y\le4$ with $x,y\ge0$: a right triangle with legs $4$, of area $8$.

