Two of the three sides must be equal.
\begin{itemize}
\item $x-4=2x-9$ gives $x=5$, with sides $1,1,0$. A side of length $0$ is impossible (equivalently, $1+0>1$ fails), so this is not a triangle.
\item $x-4=3x-15$ gives $x=\dfrac{11}{2}$, with sides $\dfrac{3}{2},2,\dfrac{3}{2}$. The triangle inequality holds: $\dfrac{3}{2}+\dfrac{3}{2}=3>2$.
\item $2x-9=3x-15$ gives $x=6$, with sides $2,3,3$, and $2+3>3$.
\end{itemize}
(All three sides cannot be equal, since the first two equations give different values of $x$.)

