There are $20$ ducks in a duck tank at a fair, and exactly $3$ of them are specially marked; picking a marked duck wins a grand prize. A grandfather pays for a number of picks for his grandson, and each pick is a duck chosen uniformly at random from the ducks in the tank. What is the least number of picks needed so that the probability of winning at least one grand prize is at least $80\%$
