In every case $\angle BAC=\angle BA''C$, and since $AB=A''B$ and $AC=A''C$, SAS gives $\triangle ABC\cong\triangle A''BC$. Combined with $\triangle A''BC\cong\triangle A'B'C'$, this proves $\triangle ABC\cong\triangle A'B'C'$. $\blacksquare$

