The roots are $-4$ and $\dfrac{3}{2}$, so $y=a(x+4)\left(x-\dfrac{3}{2}\right)$. At $x=0$: $a\cdot4\cdot\left(-\dfrac{3}{2}\right)=-6a=-15$, so $a=\dfrac{5}{2}$. Hence
\[
y=\dfrac{5}{2}(x+4)\left(x-\dfrac{3}{2}\right)=\boxed{\dfrac{5}{2}x^2+\dfrac{25}{4}x-15}
\]
(equivalently $y=\dfrac{5}{4}(x+4)(2x-3)$).

