Stewart's theorem for the cevian $AD$ states $b^2m+c^2n=a\left(d^2+mn\right)$. So
\[
100\cdot5+144\cdot6=11\left(d^2+30\right)\iff1364=11d^2+330\iff d^2=94 .
\]
Hence $AD=\boxed{\sqrt{94}}$.

(Check without Stewart: by the law of cosines in triangle $ABC$, $\cos B=\dfrac{12^2+11^2-10^2}{2\cdot12\cdot11}=\dfrac{165}{264}=\dfrac{5}{8}$, and then in triangle $ABD$, $d^2=12^2+5^2-2\cdot12\cdot5\cdot\dfrac{5}{8}=169-75=94$.)

Let the rectangle have width $2r$ and height $h$, so the semicircle has radius $r$.

\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
size(4.5cm);
