Place the dots at the points $(a,b)$ with $a,b\in\{0,1,\dots,7\}$, the corner at $(0,0)$. A line through $(0,0)$ and another dot $(a,b)$ contains also every dot that is a multiple of the reduced direction $\left(\dfrac{a}{g},\dfrac{b}{g}\right)$, where $g=\gcd(a,b)$. So each line corresponds to exactly one dot $(a,b)$ with $\gcd(a,b)=1$ (the first dot on the line after the corner), and we count such dots.

