\item Triangle $MCN$: triangles $MCN$ and $BCN$ have the same height from $N$ and bases $MC=\dfrac{1}{3}BC$, so $[MCN]=\dfrac{1}{3}[BCN]$; triangles $BCN$ and $BCD$ have the same height from $B$ and bases $CN=\dfrac{1}{2}CD$, so $[BCN]=\dfrac{1}{2}[BCD]=\dfrac {S}{4}$. Hence $[MCN]=\dfrac{S}{12}$.
