Hence
\[
[AMN]=S\left(1-\dfrac{1}{3}-\dfrac{1}{12}-\dfrac{1}{4}\right)=\dfrac{S}{3}=20,
\]
and the area of the parallelogram is $\boxed{60\text{ cm}^2}$.

Write $\alpha,\beta,\gamma$ for the angles at $A,B,C$. The exterior angle at $B$ (between side $BC$ and the extension of $AB$ beyond $B$) is $180^\circ-\beta$, and $BX$ bisects it; the bisectors at $B$ and $C$ meet on the side of $BC$ away from $A$.

\begin{asy}
usepackage("amsmath");
