There are always five numbers on the board. Look at how many of them are odd. If the two erased numbers are
\begin{itemize}
\item both even: sum and product are even, so the count of odd numbers is unchanged;
\item one even, one odd: the sum is odd and the product even, so the count is unchanged;
\item both odd: the sum is even and the product odd, so the count drops by one.
\end{itemize}
So the number of odd numbers never increases. At the start it is $2$ (namely $3$ and $5$), but $2017,2019,2021$ are three odd numbers. Hence it is $\boxed{\text{not possible}}$.

