\item[(b)] Find the smallest possible value of $x_1+x_2+\cdots+x_{2009}$.
\end{enumerate}

solution:
Each interior angle of a regular pentagon is $\dfrac{(5-2)\cdot180^\circ}{5}=108^\circ$. Since $B,C,P$ are collinear, the angle $\angle DCP$ is supplementary to the interior angle $\angle BCD$: $\angle DCP=180^\circ-108^\circ=72^\circ$. Likewise $\angle CDP=180^\circ-\angle EDC=72^\circ$.

