Let the angles be $a<b<c$ (all different, since a scalene triangle has three different angles). Then
\[
a+c=180-b,
\]
so we must make the middle angle $b$ as large as possible. Since $c>b$ and $a\ge1$, we have $180=a+b+c\ge1+b+(b+1)$, so $b\le89$. The triangle with angles $1^\circ,89^\circ,90^\circ$ is scalene with integer angles, and it gives $a+c=1+90=\boxed{91}$ degrees.

