Use vectors. Since $M=\dfrac{B+D}{2}$ and $N=\dfrac{C+E}{2}$,
\[
2\,\overrightarrow{NM}=(B-E)+(D-C).
\]
Let $\mathbf u$ and $\mathbf v$ be unit vectors from $A$ towards $B$ and towards $C$. Then $B-E=6\mathbf u$ (from $E$ to $B$ along $AB$) and $D-C=-10\mathbf v$ (from $C$ towards $A$ along $CA$). Hence
\[
4MN^2=|6\mathbf u-10\mathbf v|^2=36+100-120\cos\angle BAC .
\]
With $MN=7$: $196=136-120\cos\angle BAC$, so $\cos\angle BAC=-\dfrac{1}{2}$ and $\angle BAC=\boxed{120^\circ}$.

