Let the width be $w$, so the length is $w+5$. The figure consists of the rectangle, two squares of side $w$ and two squares of side $w+5$:
\[
w(w+5)+2w^2+2(w+5)^2=120\quad\Longrightarrow\quad5w^2+25w+50=120\quad\Longrightarrow\quad w^2+5w-14=0 .
\]
So $(w+7)(w-2)=0$ and $w=2$ (the width is positive). The rectangle is $2$ cm by $7$ cm, with perimeter $2(2+7)=\boxed{18\text{ cm}}$. Check: $14+2\cdot4+2\cdot49=120$.

