\end{asy}

Since $DE$ is a diameter, $O$ lies on line $AE$, and $AB=\dfrac{1}{2}DE$ equals the radius, so $AB=OB=OC$.
\begin{itemize}
\item Triangle $ABO$ is isosceles with $AB=OB$, so $\angle BOA=\angle BAO=24^\circ$.
\item $\angle OBC$ is an exterior angle of triangle $ABO$, so $\angle OBC=24^\circ+24^\circ=48^\circ$; triangle $OBC$ is isosceles with $OB=OC$, so $\angle OCB=48^\circ$.
\item $\angle COE$ is an exterior angle of triangle $AOC$ at $O$, so $\angle COE=\angle OAC+\angle OCA=24^\circ+48^\circ=\boxed{72^\circ}$.
\end{itemize}

\begin{asy}
