A plane through the axis of the cone cuts it in a triangle with two sides $20$ (slant heights) and base $20$ (a diameter): an equilateral triangle of side $20$. The inscribed sphere meets this plane in the incircle of the triangle, so the radius of the sphere is the inradius
\[
r=\dfrac{20}{2\sqrt3}=\dfrac{10\sqrt3}{3}.
\]
The cube is inscribed in the sphere, so its space diagonal $x\sqrt3$ is a diameter:
\[
x\sqrt3=\dfrac{20\sqrt3}{3}\quad\Longrightarrow\quad x=\boxed{\dfrac{20}{3}}.
\]
So the poster's answer $\dfrac{20}{3}\approx6.67$ is correct. In the figure the cube is drawn with vertical edges along the axis direction; the plane through the axis and two opposite vertical edges cuts the cube in a rectangle $x\sqrt2$ wide and $x$ high, whose diagonal $x\sqrt3$ is a diameter of the circle.

