Inversely proportional to $7,14,2$ means proportional to $\dfrac{1}{7},\dfrac{1}{14},\dfrac{1}{2}$, i.e.\ to $2,1,7$. Scale so that $AE=2$, $EF=1$, $FB=7$. Then $AB=10$ and $AD=BC=2$. In the right triangles $DAE$, $DAF$, $DAB$ (right angle at $A$):
\[
\tan\angle AED=\dfrac{2}{2}=1,\qquad\tan\angle AFD=\dfrac{2}{3},\qquad\tan\angle ABD=\dfrac{2}{10}=\dfrac{1}{5} .
\]
So $\angle AED=45^\circ$. For the other two acute angles,
\[
\tan(\angle AFD+\angle ABD)=\dfrac{\dfrac{2}{3}+\dfrac{1}{5}}{1-\dfrac{2}{3}\cdot\dfrac{1}{5}}=\dfrac{\dfrac{13}{15}}{\dfrac{13}{15}}=1,
\]
and their sum lies between $0^\circ$ and $180^\circ$, so $\angle AFD+\angle ABD=45^\circ$. The total is $\boxed{90^\circ}$.

