\end{asy}

Drop perpendiculars from $D$ and $C$ to $AB$, with feet $P$ and $Q$. Then
\[
h=DP=8\sin75^\circ,\qquad AP=QB=8\cos75^\circ,
\]
and $AB-CD=AP+QB=16\cos75^\circ$. Since $AB=2CD$, this difference is $CD$, so $CD=16\cos75^\circ$ and $AB=32\cos75^\circ$. The area is
\[
\dfrac{AB+CD}{2}\cdot h=24\cos75^\circ\cdot8\sin75^\circ=96\cdot2\sin75^\circ\cos75^\circ=96\sin150^\circ=\boxed{48\text{ cm}^2}.
\]
(Numerically $CD\approx4.14$, $AB\approx8.28$, $h\approx7.73$.)

