Since $3^2+4^2=5^2$, the triangle has a right angle opposite the side $5$. The hypotenuse of a right triangle is a diameter of its circumcircle (the right angle is inscribed in a semicircle), so the circumcentre $O$ is the midpoint of the hypotenuse and $R=\dfrac{5}{2}$.

