usepackage("amsmath");
size(5cm);
defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));
string[] L={"C","A","M","P","G","R","O","U","N","D"};
pair[] V; for(int i=0;i<10;++i) V[i]=dir(90-36*i);
draw(V[0]--V[1]--V[2]--V[3]--V[4]--V[5]--V[6]--V[7]--V[8]--V[9]--cycle,linewidth(0.8));
for(int i=0;i<10;++i){dot(V[i]);label("$"+L[i]+"$",V[i],dir(90-36*i));}
draw(V[4]--V[7]--V[2]--V[9]--V[5]--V[6]--V[3],red+linewidth(1));
dot(V[4],red);dot(V[3],red);
label("\mbox{}",(min(currentpicture,user=true)+max(currentpicture,user=true))/2,black); // keeps the text after the figure black when LaTeX typesets the labels inline
\end{asy}

So the length is $L=3d_3+d_5+d_4+d_1$. With $\sin18^\circ=\dfrac{\sqrt5-1}{4}$ and $\varphi=\dfrac{1+\sqrt5}{2}\approx1.618$:
\[
d_1=1,\quad d_3=\dfrac{\sin54^\circ}{\sin18^\circ}=\varphi^2=\varphi+1\approx2.618,\quad d_4=\dfrac{\sin72^\circ}{\sin18^\circ}=\cot18^\circ\approx3.078,\quad d_5=\dfrac{1}{\sin18^\circ}=2\varphi\approx3.236 .
\]
Hence $L=3(\varphi+1)+2\varphi+\cot18^\circ+1=5\varphi+4+\cot18^\circ\approx8.090+4+3.078=15.17$. The closest integer is $\boxed{15}$.

If $x=0$ (and so $y\ge1$), the point $(0,y)$ is on the $y$-axis, and no line $y=mx$ passes through it, since $y=mx$ gives $y=0$ at $x=0$. If $(x,y)=(0,0)$ were allowed, every line $y=mx$ would pass through it and there would be infinitely many values of $m$; that is why the origin is excluded.

For $1\le x\le y\le5$, the line through the origin and $(x,y)$ has slope $m=\dfrac {y}{x}\ge1$. The distinct values are the fractions $\dfrac {y}{x}$ in lowest terms with $1\le x\le y\le5$:
\[
1,\ 2,\ 3,\ 4,\ 5,\ \dfrac{3}{2},\ \dfrac{5}{2},\ \dfrac{4}{3},\ \dfrac{5}{3},\ \dfrac{5}{4} .
\]

