The committee has $4$ seniors and $3$ juniors, $5$ boys and $2$ girls. Split by the number $g$ of senior girls ($g\le2$ since there are only $2$ girls); then there are $4-g$ senior boys, $2-g$ junior girls and $3-(2-g)=1+g$ junior boys.
\begin{itemize}
\item $g=0$: $\dbinom{10}{4}\dbinom{15}{1}\dbinom{10}{2}=210\cdot15\cdot45=141750$;
\item $g=1$: $\dbinom41\dbinom{10}{3}\dbinom{15}{2}\dbinom{10}{1}=4\cdot120\cdot105\cdot10=504000$;
\item $g=2$: $\dbinom42\dbinom{10}{2}\dbinom{15}{3}=6\cdot45\cdot455=122850$.
\end{itemize}
The total is $141750+504000+122850=\boxed{768600}$.

