In right triangle $ADF$ (right angle at $D$), $DF=h\tan\theta$. In right triangle $ABE$ (right angle at $B$), with $\angle BAE=90^\circ-2\theta$,
\[
BE=w\tan(90^\circ-2\theta)=\dfrac{w\cos2\theta}{\sin2\theta},\qquad AE=\dfrac{w}{\cos(90^\circ-2\theta)}=\dfrac{w}{\sin2\theta}.
\]
The condition $DF+BE=AE$ becomes
\[
h\tan\theta=\dfrac{w(1-\cos2\theta)}{\sin2\theta}=\dfrac{w\cdot2\sin^2\theta}{2\sin\theta\cos\theta}=w\tan\theta .
\]
Since $\tan\theta>0$, we get $h=w$, so $ABCD$ is a square. $\blacksquare$

(Conversely, in a square the relation $AE=DF+BE$ always holds, by the same computation.)

