The square has area $4$. The points of the square with $x\le y$ form the triangle with vertices $(1,1)$, $(1,2)$, $(2,2)$ (above the line $y=x$), which has legs $1$ and area $\dfrac{1}{2}$. So the region where $x>y$ (shaded) has area $4-\dfrac{1}{2}=\dfrac{7}{2}$, and the probability is
\[
\dfrac{\dfrac{7}{2}}{4}=\boxed{\dfrac{7}{8}}.
\]

