Factor: $a^2-2ab-3b^2=(a-3b)(a+b)=0$, so $a=3b$ or $a=-b$.
\begin{itemize}
\item If $a=3b$: $\dfrac{a}{2b-a}=\dfrac{3b}{-b}=-3$.
\item If $a=-b$: $\dfrac{a}{2b-a}=\dfrac{-b}{3b}=-\dfrac{1}{3}$.
\end{itemize}
In both cases $2b-a\ne0$ since $b\ne0$. The possible values are $\boxed{-3\text{ and }-\dfrac{1}{3}}$.

Two pairs of equal angles make the triangles similar (AA), with the correspondence $A\leftrightarrow D$, $B\leftrightarrow F$, $C\leftrightarrow G$. The ratio of similarity is $\dfrac{DF}{AB}=\dfrac{10}{15}=\dfrac{2}{3}$, so every side of $DFG$ is $\dfrac{2}{3}$ of the corresponding side of $ABC$:
\[
DG=\dfrac{2}{3}\,AC=\dfrac{2}{3}\cdot9=6\text{ m},\qquad BC=\dfrac{3}{2}\,FG=\dfrac{3}{2}\cdot12=18\text{ m}.
\]
So $\boxed{BC=18\text{ m and }DG=6\text{ m}}$. (Both triangles exist: $9+15>18$ and $6+10>12$.) In the figure the computed lengths are shown in blue; equal angles are marked with the same number of arcs.

